BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20160128T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20160128T203000
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:0ovj3n84qdoi5f6chg9lgoairk@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20160128T190000
CREATED:20150902T235309Z
DESCRIPTION:January 14\, 21\, 28\, & February 4\nWalter Benjamin: A Jewish 
 Nietzsche? (4 sessions w/ Michael Loebs)\nMichael Loeb’s classes meet Thurs
 day nights in the CBS Board Room from 7-8:30 p.m.\n\nJanuary 28: Art\, Cult
 ure\, & Technology  Reading: Friedrich Nietzsche\, The Gay Science (Book 2\
 , pp. 57-59\, 78-89\, 107)\n\n Reading: Walter Benjamin\, Das Kunstwerk im 
 Zeitalter seiner technischen Reproduzierbarkeit (The Work of Art in the Age
  of Mechanical Reproduction\, 1936)\n\n+++++\n\nOur “Thinking Matters: Mode
 rn Jewish Philosophy” course series continues this winter!\n\nJoin an impre
 ssive line-up of teachers to wrestle with the exciting and challenging ques
 tions of modern Jewish philosophy! Can there be such a thing as a Jewish ph
 ilosophy\, or a philosophy of Judaism? How have Jewish traditions participa
 ted in the philosophical canon? How are Judaism and Jewish ideas relevant t
 o the modern relationship of ethics\, theology\, and philosophy?\n\nFor an 
 introduction to Jewish modern thought and philosophy\, we recommend Steven 
 Katz’s essay\, “Eliezar Berkovits & Modern Jewish Philosophy.”\n\nDetails a
 nd readings for the “Thinking Matters” mini-courses taught in January – Mar
 ch 2016 are included at the link below.\n\nhttp://bethsholomsf.org/shul-sch
 ool-thinking-matters-2/
LAST-MODIFIED:20160316T214449Z
LOCATION:Board Room
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Thinking Matters: Modern Jewish Philosophy 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20160411T000000Z
DTEND:20160411T013000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:599d7stvstlakfj6er0t0e7h9o@google.com
CREATED:20160329T063247Z
DESCRIPTION:"HAGGADAH"\nOpening Sunday\, April 10\, 2016\, in the Kahn Gall
 ery at 5 p.m. Taste of Passover reception follows.\n\nPassover\, perhaps mo
 re than any other holiday\, is steeped in tradition and ritual. Fortunately
 \, we have a wonderful\, step by step guide through the Seder – the Haggada
 h. \n\nThe CBS library has dozens of haggadot that you can peruse and borro
 w: The Maxwell House version that many of us grew up with\, the beautiful S
 hahn\, Baskin or Szyk. There are haggadot aimed at children\, interfaith fa
 milies\, vegetarians\, Holocaust\, animated\, illuminated\, and just plain 
 fun.\n\nThe Kahn Gallery of Congregation Beth Sholom\, behind the Gronowski
  Family Chapel\, will be showcasing haggadot from our own CBS Library! Come
  see the show\, HAGGADAH\, learn about the haggadah\, and join us for a “Ta
 ste of Passover” reception. You will also have the opportunity to ‘sponsor’
  one of the framed photographs to help defray the cost of the show!\n\nCura
 ted by Rosemary Rothstein and Eva-Lynne Leibman\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20160329T063300Z
LOCATION:Kahn Gallery
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Haggadah Exhibition Reception
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
