UID:0ovj3n84qdoi5f6chg9lgoairk@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20160317T190000
CREATED:20150902T235309Z
DESCRIPTION:February 11\, 18\, & March 17\, 24\nPhilosophy of Purim: Modern
 ity & Perennial Parody (4 sessions w/ Rabbi Aubrey Glazer) Rabbi Glazer’s c
 lasses meet Thursday nights in the CBS Board Room from 6:30-7 p.m. \n\nMarc
 h 17: Philosophy of Purim in The Big Lebowski\, Part I: “I don’t roll on Sh
 abbos\,” Jewish Identity\, & the Philosophy of History   Reading: TBD\n\n++
 +++\n\nOur “Thinking Matters: Modern Jewish Philosophy” course series conti
 nues this winter!\n\nJoin an impressive line-up of teachers to wrestle with
  the exciting and challenging questions of modern Jewish philosophy! Can th
 ere be such a thing as a Jewish philosophy\, or a philosophy of Judaism? Ho
 w have Jewish traditions participated in the philosophical canon? How are J
 udaism and Jewish ideas relevant to the modern relationship of ethics\, the
 ology\, and philosophy?\n\nFor an introduction to Jewish modern thought and
  philosophy\, we recommend Steven Katz’s essay\, “Eliezar Berkovits & Moder
 n Jewish Philosophy.”\n\nDetails and readings for the “Thinking Matters” mi
 ni-courses taught in January – March 2016 are included at the link below.\n
 \nhttp://bethsholomsf.org/shul-school-thinking-matters-2/
LAST-MODIFIED:20160316T214449Z
LOCATION:Board Room
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Thinking Matters: Modern Jewish Philosophy 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
