CREATED:20090219T235818Z
DESCRIPTION:301 14th Avenue\, Koret Hall\n\nThe Joy of Jewish Dancing with 
 Bruce Bierman\n10 sessions. Cost: $75 members\, $100 nonmembers\nPreregistr
 ation strongly encouraged\, but walk-ins welcome.\n\nWorkshop participants 
 will learn the basic steps\, patterns\, gestures\, and styles of Yemenite\,
  Hasidic\, Yiddish\, and Israeli folkdance. Special emphasis will be on dan
 cing with "dveykus"-clinging close to the powerful rhythms of the music\, o
 n another's friendship\, and your own unique expression.\n\nBruce Bierman i
 s the artistic director of the Jewish Dance Theatre. He is an award-winning
  actor\, director\, choreographer and playwright with dance residencies cur
 rently throughout the Bay Area.\n\nContact Yaffa Tygiel to register at YTyg
 iel@bethsholomsf.org.
LAST-MODIFIED:20090219T235818Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:The Joy of Jewish Dancing
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20160612T090000Z
DTEND:20160612T100000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:q9a61oj7jqgl84nqbg3dclmabc@google.com
CREATED:20160603T171319Z
DESCRIPTION:"Healing Faces So Divine: אדרא רבא Idra Rabbah (Zohar III :127b
 –145a)\," with Rabbi Aubrey Glazer\n\nThe all night vigil known as Tikkun L
 eil Shavuot is one of the most audacious “ancient-new” rituals created and 
 practiced with the circle of the Zohar in 13th century Spain. Inspired by R
 abbi Shimon bar Yochai and his coterie of mystical fellow-travelers\, we en
 gage in adorning the jewels of Torah upon the different faces of the divine
  that conjoin on the night of Shavuot — the moment when Torah is revealed t
 o the Assembly of Israel. This Great Assembly\, known as the Idra Rabbah\, 
 is a mystical moment and a healing journey of unification from midnight to 
 dawn. The Zohar to be explored is part of a larger tikkun that Rabbi Shimon
  bar Yochai wants to catalyze before his passing from this world to the nex
 t. Like Bar Yochai\, we too want to explore how this tikkun might open fell
 ow travelers to heal\, adorn and unify the faces so divine that we yearn to
  encounter this sacred night.
LAST-MODIFIED:20160607T172458Z
LOCATION:Gronowski Family Chapel
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Healing Secret Faces So Divine in Zohar’s Idrah Rabbah for Shavuot
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
