DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20160414T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20160414T200000
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:0ovj3n84qdoi5f6chg9lgoairk@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20160414T190000
CREATED:20150902T235309Z
DESCRIPTION:April 7\, 14 & May 5\, 12\nPhilosophies of Early Zionism\n(4 se
 ssions w/ Ephraim Margolin)\nMr. Margolin’s classes meet Thursday nights in
  the Main Meeting Room from 6:30-8 p.m.\n\nApril 14: 1800 Years of Diaspora
 \; Political Zionism\nReading: Stfan Zweig\, "In The Snow" (copies provided
  during first class)\n\n+++++\n\nOur “Thinking Matters: Modern Jewish Philo
 sophy” course series continues this spring!\n\nJoin an impressive line-up o
 f teachers to wrestle with the exciting and challenging questions of modern
  Jewish philosophy! Can there be such a thing as a Jewish philosophy\, or a
  philosophy of Judaism? How have Jewish traditions participated in the phil
 osophical canon? How are Judaism and Jewish ideas relevant to the modern re
 lationship of ethics\, theology\, and philosophy?\n\nFor an introduction to
  Jewish modern thought and philosophy\, we recommend Steven Katz’s essay\, 
 “Eliezar Berkovits & Modern Jewish Philosophy.”\n\nhttp://bethsholomsf.org/
 shul-school-spring-thinking-matters-series/
LAST-MODIFIED:20160331T064447Z
LOCATION:Main Meeting Room
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Thinking Matters: Modern Jewish Philosophy 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
