DESCRIPTION:From: New Frontier [mailto:miller@uscj.org] \nSent: Thursday\, 
 April 09\, 2015 11:40 AM\nTo: Michael Lederman\; Molly Reichman\nSubject: B
 eth Sholom Possibly Hosting?\n \nHi Michael and Molly\,\nI hope you are bot
 h doing well and having a good Passover. I wanted to check in with you abou
 t the possibility of Beth Sholom hosting Mini-Mission-Mitzvah Day next year
 . It’s scheduled for Sunday\, January 17th. It would involve using a social
  hall type of space throughout the day/evening for activities and as a “hom
 e base” while we went out into the community for service projects throughou
 t the day. I would take care of all of the supplies and food. It would lite
 rally just be use of the space. If you want\, you can ask Shani Gross at Ko
 l Emeth about it—they hosted it this year. I would love to highlight the co
 ngregation as a “hosting community” next year\, and this is the easiest of 
 all our events to start with. Let me know what you think.\nWarmly\,\nSarah\
 n \nSarah Miller\nRegional Youth Director\, New Frontier\nUnited Synagogue 
 of Conservative Judaism\n4676 Mayette Ave.\nSanta Rosa\, CA 95405\nMobile: 
 (408) 892-2732\nE-mail: Miller@uscj.org\nWebsite: www.newfrousy.org\nFacebo
 ok: NewFrontier USY\nTwitter: newfrontierusy
LAST-MODIFIED:20160106T201418Z
LOCATION:Koret Hall\, MMR\, CBS Kitchen
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:USY Mini-Mission Mitzvah
