DESCRIPTION:Professor Martin Kupiec (Tel Aviv University)\, who is currentl
 y on sabbatical at UC Berkeley\, will present a talk titled\, "Coffee or be
 er? The choice could effect your genome."\n\nProf. Martin Kupiec was born i
 n Buenos Aires\, Argentina\, and immigrated to Israel in 1977. He received 
 a BSc in Biology in 1979 and his PhD in Genetics in 1985 from the Hebrew Un
 iversity in Jerusalem\, Israel. Today\, he leads the Applied Genetics and M
 icrobiology group at the Faculty of Life Sciences\, Tel Aviv University. A 
 hallmark of his work is his multi-disciplinary approach\, which combines ge
 netics\, molecular biology\, computational and systems biology\, as well as
  cell biology and biochemistry. 
LAST-MODIFIED:20160508T220252Z
LOCATION:Koret Hall
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Dr. Ernest M. Weitz Breakfast Club
