DESCRIPTION:Join us on Tuesday\, July 8\, when we screen "When Jews Were Fu
 nny\," a documentary about the history of Jewish comedy\, from the early da
 ys of Borsht belt to the present\, ultimately exploring not just ethnicity 
 in the entertainment industry\, but also the entire unruly question of what
  it means to be Jewish.\n\nTickets:\nAdults: $10\nChildren (ages 12 and und
 er): $5\n\nSchedule:\n6 p.m. - Minyan in the Gronowski Family Chapel\n6:30 
 - 7 p.m. - Pizza\, beer\, wine\, and kid-friendly refreshments in Koret Hal
 l\n7 - 8:30 p.m. - Screening of "When Jews Were Funny"\n\nPlease R.S.V.P. t
 o David Wolk\, dwolk@bethsholomsf.org by Wednesday\, July 2\, so we order e
 nough pizza for all.
