BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20141031T020000Z
DTEND:20141031T040000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:6ucqa4g3b58i78oounatkm5vic@google.com
CREATED:20140919T182150Z
DESCRIPTION:International Mizrahi Remembrance Month \nSan Francisco Ceremon
 y to Honor the Forgotten Refugees \n \nWith Musician Yair Harel\,  JIMENA C
 o-founder Semha Alwaya\, & Israel's Consul General to the Pacific Northwest
 \, Dr. Andy David. \n \nThursday\, October 30th \n7:00PM\nCongregation Beth
  Sholom\n301 14th Ave\, San Francisco \nRSVP to info@jimena.org\n \nOn June
  23\, 2014 the Government of Israel adopted a law which designates November
  30th as an annual\, national day of commemoration for the 850\,000 Jewish 
 refugees who were displaced from Arab countries and Iran in the 20th centur
 y. Throughout the months of November & December events are being planned ar
 ound the world to honor Jews from Arab countries.\n \nJoin JIMENA in San Fr
 ancisco as we commemorate the heritage of the 850\,000 Jews who were displa
 ced from North Africa and the Middle East in the 20th century. The program 
 will include a music performance by Yair Harel\, a Jerusalem-born musician 
 and educator who is credited for having played a major role repopularizing 
 ancient piyutim - a form of ancient liturgical poetry that thrived in the A
 rab world.\n\n The San Francisco program will also feature remarks by JIMEN
 A co-founder and Iraqi native\, Semha Alwaya. In her JIMENA testimony\, Sem
 ha relates that "I was born in Baghdad\, and like most other Iraqis\, my mo
 ther tongue is Arabic. My family's cuisine\, our mannerisms\, our outlook\,
  are all strongly influenced by our synthesized Judeo-Arabic culture. In di
 scussions about refugees in the Middle East\, a major piece of the narrativ
 e is routinely omitted\, and my life is part of the tapestry of what's miss
 ing. I am a Jew\, and I\, too\, am a refugee. Some of my childhood was spen
 t in a refugee camp in Israel (yes\, Israel).  And I am far from being alon
 e."\n \nThe program will conclude with remarks by Israel's Consul General t
 o the Pacific Northwest\, Andy David. Dr. David will provide a synopsis of 
 the new Israeli initiative and the efforts that are taking place in Israel 
 to ensure that Mizrahi and Sephardic heritage and history is passed down to
  the benefit of future generations. \n\nThis program is co-sponsored by The
  Israel Center of the San Francisco Jewish Community Federation\, The Consu
 late General of Israel to the Pacific Northwest\, and Congregation Beth Sho
 lom\n\n JIMENA JIMENA's mission is to achieve universal recognition for the
  heritage and history of the 850\,000 indigenous Jewish refugees from the M
 iddle East and North Africa. Our programs aim to ensure that the accurate h
 istory of Mizrahi and Sepahrdic Jews is incorporated into mainstream Jewish
  and Middle Eastern narratives in order to create balance in attitudes\, na
 rratives\, discourse\, and negotiations about Middle Eastern refugees and t
 he modern Jewish experience.\n \n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20140919T182437Z
LOCATION:Sanctuary
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:International Mizrahi Remembrance Month  San Francisco Ceremony to 
 Honor the Forgotten Refugees   
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
