CREATED:20150909T032557Z
DESCRIPTION:Remy and Joe Pessah will share their remarkable story with Brea
 kfast Club attendees. The couple was married during the time Joe was impris
 oned in the Tora concentration camp with all of Egypt's Jewish men for two 
 years after the 1967 War. This talk is presented in conjunction with JIMENA
  (http://www.jimena.org/)\, an organization dedicated to educating and advo
 cating on behalf of the 850\,000 Jewish refugees from the Middle East and N
 orth Africa.\n\nThe Breakfast club currently meets four times each year on 
 a Sunday with an informal talk on topics of interest to the Jewish communit
 y. Speakers have included many community leaders of the San Francisco Jewis
 h community\, along with members of Beth Sholom. Meetings are held at 9:00 
 a.m. and start with a delicious breakfast.\n\nCost: $80 per couple & $40 pe
 r individual for all four meetings\, $15 drop-in
LAST-MODIFIED:20160331T070153Z
LOCATION:Koret Hall
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Dr. Ernest M. Weitz Breakfast Club
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
