UID:0ovj3n84qdoi5f6chg9lgoairk@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20160121T190000
CREATED:20150902T235309Z
DESCRIPTION:January 14\, 21\, 28\, & February 4\nWalter Benjamin: A Jewish 
 Nietzsche? (4 sessions w/ Michael Loebs)\nMichael Loeb’s classes meet Thurs
 day nights in the CBS Board Room from 7-8:30 p.m.\n\nJanuary 21: Morality a
 nd the Critique of Violence   Reading: Friedrich Nietzsche\, On the Genealo
 gy of Morals\, Part I\n\n Reading: Walter Benjamin\, Zur Kritik der Gewalt 
 (Critique of Violence\, 1921)\n\n+++++\n\nOur “Thinking Matters: Modern Jew
 ish Philosophy” course series continues this winter!\n\nJoin an impressive 
 line-up of teachers to wrestle with the exciting and challenging questions 
 of modern Jewish philosophy! Can there be such a thing as a Jewish philosop
 hy\, or a philosophy of Judaism? How have Jewish traditions participated in
  the philosophical canon? How are Judaism and Jewish ideas relevant to the 
 modern relationship of ethics\, theology\, and philosophy?\n\nFor an introd
 uction to Jewish modern thought and philosophy\, we recommend Steven Katz’s
  essay\, “Eliezar Berkovits & Modern Jewish Philosophy.”\n\nDetails and rea
 dings for the “Thinking Matters” mini-courses taught in January – March 201
 6 are included at the link below.\n\nhttp://bethsholomsf.org/shul-school-th
 inking-matters-2/
LAST-MODIFIED:20160316T214449Z
LOCATION:Board Room
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Thinking Matters: Modern Jewish Philosophy 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
