DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20160610
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20160612
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:4861t4p5bj3idt6vcccdr9c7fg@google.com
CREATED:20160303T050550Z
DESCRIPTION:TWO-DAY SHABBAT RETREAT (June 10+11)\nLed by Norman Fischer and
  Rabbi Aubrey Glazer\, with a special Kabbalat Shabbat service led by Amand
 a Russell\n\nWe will meet on Friday\, June 10\, 5 - 9 p.m.\, and again on S
 aturday\, June 11\, 10 a.m. - 9:30 p.m.\n\nFOR CBS MEMBER TICKETS: https://
 www.universe.com/makororshabbatmeditationretreat\n\nRegister now to join Ma
 kor Or in meditation\, celebrating Shabbat\, and preparing for Shavuot. Lis
 ten to teachings from Norman Fischer and Rabbi Aubrey Glazer and enjoy the 
 special Kabbalat Shabbat service led by rabbinic intern\, Amanda Russell.\n
   \nIn this retreat\, we will practice silent meditation\, returning to the
  source of all being where we belong and find true rest. We will eat silent
  meals\, pray\, read\, study Torah\, and sing.  Makor Or Shabbat retreats h
 ave always been our favorite\, full of joy\, depth and fellowship.\nNo prev
 ious experience with meditation\, Hebrew\, or prayer is necessary. All are 
 welcome.\nOut of respect for our members with asthma\, please do not wear s
 cented products to Makor Or programs.\n\n*****\n\nAbout Makor Or: Founded J
 anuary 1\, 2000 by Rabbi Alan Lew (z"l) and Norman Fischer\, the Jewish med
 itation practice of Makor Or incorporates sitting and walking meditation\, 
 and Jewish chant. Our mission is to bring the clarity and depth of meditati
 on practice to our Jewish life and observance\, to facilitate the transform
 ation that Judaism can effect in our lives.\nNorman Fischer is the spiritua
 l leader of Makor Or. He is also a Zen master\, founder of Everyday Zen and
  a poet. His books include\, Jerusalem Moonlight\, Taking Our Places\, Sail
 ing Home and The Strugglers.\nRabbi Aubrey Glazer is the Rabbi of Congregat
 ion Beth Sholom in San Francisco. He has studied and practiced meditation w
 ith Rabbis Jonathan Omerman\, and Miles Krassen\, and is a graduate of the 
 Institute for Jewish Spirituality. His books include Mystical Vertigo and T
 angle of Matter & Ghost - a study of mysticism\, Rinzai Buddhism in the son
 gbook of Leonard Cohen.\nMakor Or is a program of the Taube Foundation for 
 Jewish Life & Culture.  \n
LAST-MODIFIED:20160602T200032Z
LOCATION:Congregation Beth Sholom
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Makor Or Shabbaton Retreat
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
