CREATED:20090219T235818Z
DESCRIPTION:301 14th Avenue\, Board Room\n\nIn this course we will read the
  biblical text\, examine the historical evidence of David's reign\, study t
 he poetry\, listen to the music\, and admire the extensive art (including p
 aintings\, drawings\, engravings\, woodcuts\, stained glass\, and sculpture
 s) based on King David's story. From anonymous early manuscript illustrator
 s\, to medieval Italian\, Dutch and German painters\, through great Renaiss
 ance artists\, to nineteenth-century and contemporary painters\, we will se
 e how the many aspects of the David story have been interpreted.\n\nTo regi
 ster contact Yaffa Tygiel at YTygiel@bethsholomsf.org.
LAST-MODIFIED:20090219T235818Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Course on King David
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20160512T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20160512T200000
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:0ovj3n84qdoi5f6chg9lgoairk@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20160512T190000
CREATED:20150902T235309Z
DESCRIPTION:April 7\, 14 & May 5\, 12\nPhilosophies of Early Zionism\n(4 se
 ssions w/ Ephraim Margolin)\nMr. Margolin’s classes meet Thursday nights in
  the Main Meeting Room from 6:30-8 p.m.\n\nMay 12: Socialist Zionism\, Birt
 h of the State\, & Personal Comments\nReading: N/A\n\n+++++\n\nOur “Thinkin
 g Matters: Modern Jewish Philosophy” course series continues this spring!\n
 \nJoin an impressive line-up of teachers to wrestle with the exciting and c
 hallenging questions of modern Jewish philosophy! Can there be such a thing
  as a Jewish philosophy\, or a philosophy of Judaism? How have Jewish tradi
 tions participated in the philosophical canon? How are Judaism and Jewish i
 deas relevant to the modern relationship of ethics\, theology\, and philoso
 phy?\n\nFor an introduction to Jewish modern thought and philosophy\, we re
 commend Steven Katz’s essay\, “Eliezar Berkovits & Modern Jewish Philosophy
 .”\n\nhttp://bethsholomsf.org/shul-school-spring-thinking-matters-series/
LAST-MODIFIED:20160504T211741Z
LOCATION:Boardroom
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Thinking Matters: Modern Jewish Philosophy 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
