DESCRIPTION:Shabbat Art Experience is a new Shabbat activity for families w
 ith children in grades 2nd – 6th that will occur on Shabbats when our Shabb
 at School is not taking place. The program is free of charge\, however part
 icipation in each session is limited to the first ten families that RSVP. P
 lease RSVP to Michael Lederman (mlederman@bethsholomsf.org). \n\nLed by Ely
 ssa Wortzman\, a visual artist with experience teaching and creating commun
 ity programming for children and adults in the New York\, Toronto\, and San
  Francisco Jewish communities\, these sessions are open to all. We invite C
 BS Shabbat School families to join us\, but also encourage families from th
 e greater Jewish community (e.g.\, the Brandeis School) to participate in t
 hese free activities!\n\nDuring this Shabbat Art Experience\, participants 
 will play Mishkan Twister! Using the game of Twister\, we will explore the 
 shapes and forms of the Mishkan (the Tabernacle or portable sanctuary\, a s
 piritual center in the desert). Like Bezalel\, builder of the Mishkan and o
 ne of the first Jewish artists\, participants will then build their own por
 table sanctuaries out of candy.
LAST-MODIFIED:20160127T213515Z
LOCATION:Main Meeting Room
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Shabbat Art Experience
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
