DESCRIPTION:February 25\, March 3\, 10\, & 31\nGhetto Thinking: From the Ve
 nice Ghetto to the Last Ghetto in Lodz\n(4 sessions w/ Dr. Michael Thaler)\
 nDr. Thaler’s classes meet Thursday nights in the CBS Board Room from 7-8:3
 0 p.m.\n\nMarch 3: The Venice Ghetto   Reading: TBD\n\n+++++\n\nOur “Thinki
 ng Matters: Modern Jewish Philosophy” course series continues this winter!\
 n\nJoin an impressive line-up of teachers to wrestle with the exciting and 
 challenging questions of modern Jewish philosophy! Can there be such a thin
 g as a Jewish philosophy\, or a philosophy of Judaism? How have Jewish trad
 itions participated in the philosophical canon? How are Judaism and Jewish 
 ideas relevant to the modern relationship of ethics\, theology\, and philos
 ophy?\n\nFor an introduction to Jewish modern thought and philosophy\, we r
 ecommend Steven Katz’s essay\, “Eliezar Berkovits & Modern Jewish Philosoph
 y.”\n\nDetails and readings for the “Thinking Matters” mini-courses taught 
 in January – March 2016 are included at the link below.\n\nhttp://bethsholo
 msf.org/shul-school-thinking-matters-2/
LAST-MODIFIED:20160316T214449Z
LOCATION:Board Room
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Thinking Matters: Modern Jewish Philosophy 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
