CREATED:20160105T014323Z
DESCRIPTION:Rabbi Torchio's Tikkun Middot Intensive will meet 10 times over
  the course of 2016: January 6\; February 10\; March 9\; April 6\; May 11\;
  June 8\; July 6\; August 10\; September 7\; and October 5.\n\nTikkun Middo
 t is inspired by the techniques of mindfulness and Mussar\, a Jewish moveme
 nt focused on ethical behavior and character development. Tikkun Middot tra
 nslates as “repair of a measure\,” but we understand middot to mean "traits
 \," so the Tikkun Middot practice requires us to refine character traits su
 ch as forgiveness\, generosity\, and humility. By cultivating our attention
  to these core traits\, we are better able to acknowledge and reduce negati
 ve behavioral patterns\, and to respond with deeper wisdom and greater comp
 assion to ourselves and others.\n\nWe will sit in silence\, learn text\, an
 d reflect together on our experiences of the middot in our lives. \n\nTo re
 gister or for answers to any questions you may have\, please email Rabbi Ba
 tshir Torchio: Batshir@yahoo.com
LAST-MODIFIED:20160105T185434Z
LOCATION:Makom Sholom
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Rabbi Batshir Torchio's Tikkun Middot Intensive
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
