BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20090301T220000Z
DTEND:20090302T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:1235087898-a0de140-20802@www.bethsholomsf.org
CREATED:20090219T235818Z
DESCRIPTION:301 14th Avenue\n\nReady for a new view on parenthood?\n\nJoin 
 Congregation Beth Sholom For\nLiving At the Top\nof Your Lungs: \nPrivacy\,
  Publicity\, and Parenting in the 21st Century\nAn Afternoon with Ayelet Wa
 ldman \nFree and open to the public\n\nAyelet Waldman is a novelist and ess
 ayist whose work has appeared in The San Francisco Chronicle and Salon.com.
  Waldman brings refreshing candor to the socially-charged issues of wifehoo
 d\, motherhood\, sexuality and family.\n\nComplimentary childcare is availa
 ble on a reservation-only basis. Contact Congregation Beth Sholom by Februa
 ry 23 to reserve your spot.\n\nAbout the Series: \nThe Levinson Speaker Ser
 ies is a program sponsored by The David Levinson Memorial Lecture Series En
 dowment Fund and presented by Congregation Beth Sholom. The series was esta
 blished by the Levinson family in memory of David Levinson. David was a lon
 gtime board member of Beth Sholom and an active congregant who served the s
 ynagogue with passion and commitment\, including his many years of involvem
 ent with the Education Committee. This series brings to our community visio
 nary Jews from across the country to speak on a wide range of subjects. \n\
 nOther events in this series are:\n\nSunday\, April 19\, 2009—Evvy Eisen: C
 elebrated photographer of local Holocaust survivors\, Ms. Eisen will share 
 her experience of photographing survivors and learning their amazing storie
 s of survival. Her exhibition Mulitply by Six Million will be in the Beth S
 holom gallery space during March and April 2009.\n\nJune 2009—Sacred Space 
 Symposium: In celebration of the first anniversary of the opening of our ne
 w building\, a diverse panel of architects\, historians\, and rabbis will h
 old a discussion on sacred space in the 21st century.\n\nFor more informati
 on please contact Ariana Barth at 415.221.8736\, ext. 111\, or ABarth@beths
 holomsf.org.
LAST-MODIFIED:20090219T235818Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:David Levinson Speaker Series
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
