UID:ldj3eq8ksv1j6trscoap0bl4o8@google.com
CREATED:20160308T040737Z
DESCRIPTION:On Thursday\, March 31\, 6 - 8 p.m.\, join members of the CBS c
 ommunity at the Contemporary Jewish Museum for a private tour of Roman Vish
 niac Rediscovered led by CJM docent and CBS congregant\, Judy Leash.\n \nRo
 man Vishniac (1897–1990) was an extraordinarily versatile and innovative ph
 otographer\, and he created the most widely recognized photographic record 
 of Jewish life in Eastern Europe between the two World Wars. This exhibitio
 n introduces recently discovered and radically diverse new bodies of work a
 nd repositions Vishniac's iconic photographs of Eastern Europe within the b
 roader tradition of 1930s commissioned social documentary photography. Orga
 nized by the International Center of Photography\, New York. \n\nAfter the 
 museum visit\, all participants are invited to share a glass of wine\, cup 
 of tea\, or other libation and good conversation at The Grove Café. (The CJ
 M is located at 736 Mission Street\, between 3rd and 4th Streets. The Grove
  Café is nearby at 690 Mission Street.) \n \nPlease RSVP to creiger [at] be
 thsholomsf [dot] org by Friday\, March 25\, or call 415.940.7099. The tour 
 is available to the first 20 people who RSVP\; there is no charge for admis
 sion.
LAST-MODIFIED:20160308T040737Z
LOCATION:Contemporary Jewish Museum\, 736 Mission St\, San Francisco\, CA 9
 4103\, United States
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Tour of Roman Vishniac Rediscovered @ CJM
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20160616T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20160616T203000
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:0ovj3n84qdoi5f6chg9lgoairk@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20160609T190000
CREATED:20150902T235309Z
DESCRIPTION:June 16\nInterrogating the Academic BDS of Israel on Campus\n(1
  session w/ Tammi Rossman-Benjamin & Russell Berman)\nThis class meets Thur
 sday night in the CBS Board Room from 7-8:30 p.m.\n\nReading: TBD\n\n+++++\
 n\nOur “Thinking Matters: Modern Jewish Philosophy” course series continues
  this spring!\n\nJoin an impressive line-up of teachers to wrestle with the
  exciting and challenging questions of modern Jewish philosophy! Can there 
 be such a thing as a Jewish philosophy\, or a philosophy of Judaism? How ha
 ve Jewish traditions participated in the philosophical canon? How are Judai
 sm and Jewish ideas relevant to the modern relationship of ethics\, theolog
 y\, and philosophy?\n\nFor an introduction to Jewish modern thought and phi
 losophy\, we recommend Steven Katz’s essay\, “Eliezar Berkovits & Modern Je
 wish Philosophy.”\n\nDetails and readings for the “Thinking Matters” mini-c
 ourses taught April - June 2016 are on the CBS website: http://bethsholomsf
 .org/shul-school-spring-thinking-matters-series/
LAST-MODIFIED:20160530T225410Z
LOCATION:Main Meeting Room
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Thinking Matters: Modern Jewish Philosophy 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
