CREATED:20141222T185430Z
DESCRIPTION:Maimouna: A Post Passover Celebration with Jaffa Road\n\nCongre
 gation Beth Sholom and JIMENA invite you to celebrate Maimouna.\n \nMaimoun
 a is an exhuberant Moroccan Jewish festival that is celebrated following Pa
 ssover. The word “Mainouna” is derived from the Arabic word for wealth and 
 good fortune. Come and celebrate the end of Passover by enjoying scrumptiou
 s delicacies\, music\, and dancing with Congregation Beth Sholom and JIMENA
 !\n \nJoin us on Friday\, April 17 for a special 3rd Friday Musical Kabbala
 t Shabbat featuring mellifluous tones from Rabbi Glazer and Jaffa Road\, a 
 band that blends Jewish roots\, jazz\, Indian and Arabic music\, and ancien
 t Hebrew poetry. Following the service we are hosting a catered Spanish-ins
 pired vegetarian community dinner highlighted by an intimate Ladino concert
  experience with Aviva Chernick\, Jaffa Road vocalist.\n\nContact Beth Jone
 s at bjones@bethsholomsf.org or 415.940.7092 for further information.\n 
LAST-MODIFIED:20150408T164535Z
LOCATION:Sanctuary and Main Meeting Room
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Musical Kabbalat Shabbat Service & Maimouna Post Passover Celebrati
 on
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
