UID:17e111l66a6anr9jpia7r1s2k0@google.com
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20140129T224912Z
DESCRIPTION:On Saturday\, February 8\, after Kiddush\, at about 1:15 p.m.\,
  a group from Beth Sholom will gather in the Rainbow Courtyard to walk over
  to the Botanical Gardens in Golden Gate Park (about a 20-minute walk).\n\n
 Please note: Free entry to the Botanical Gardens requires a picture i.d. an
 d proof of San Francisco residency\; otherwise there is an entry fee.\n\nWe
  will informally tour the gardens (aka as Strybing Arboretum) with a congre
 gant who is a former docent\, along with a current docent.\n\nWe will be fo
 cusing on the magnolias\, which are presently in bloom. The Botanical Garde
 n has an exceptional collection of Asian magnolias\, which bloom before the
  leaves come out. This creates some dramatic profiles of huge white or pink
  blossoms against bare branches. If you have any questions please contact M
 arilyn Kohn\, m6kohn@gmail.com. \n
LAST-MODIFIED:20140129T224922Z
LOCATION:San Francisco Botanical Garden
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Shabbat Afternoon Walk! 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
