UID:954j9ou6i3grmpeih8rcitlrfg@google.com
CREATED:20160203T011729Z
DESCRIPTION:The CBS Book Club for Kids (for 5th\, 6th\, and 7th graders) wi
 ll meet in the Main Meeting Room\, to discuss The Hebrew Kid and the Apache
  Maiden\, by Robert Avrech. The novel is narrated by 12-year old Ariel\, wh
 ose religiously observant family has left Russia for America in the 19th ce
 ntury\, and is now traveling though the dangerous American West. As he prep
 ares for his bar mitzvah\, Ariel strikes up a friendship with Lozen\, a you
 ng warrior of the Apache tribe. Through their friendship\, Ariel and Lozen 
 learn about each other’s traditions and beliefs in the face of incredible c
 hallenges.\n\nDinner will begin at 6 p.m.\, followed by a group conversatio
 n facilitated by Howard Freedman\, a CBS congregant and Director of the Jew
 ish Community Library. The book's author will also connect with the partici
 pants via FaceTime.\n\nThere is no cost\, but space is limited. Please emai
 l Elin Cohen (elincohen@hotmail.com) to register.
LAST-MODIFIED:20160203T011844Z
LOCATION:Main Meeting Room
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:CBS Kids Book Group
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
