DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20160602T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20160602T200000
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:0ovj3n84qdoi5f6chg9lgoairk@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20160519T190000
CREATED:20150902T235309Z
DESCRIPTION:May 19\nOn the Prejudice of Philosophers & the Search for Authe
 nticity\n(1 session w/ Rabbi Aubrey Glazer)\nRabbi Glazer’s classes meet Th
 ursday nights in the CBS Board Room from 6:30-8 p.m.\n\nMay 19: On the Prej
 udice of Philosophers & the Search for Authenticity\nReading: R. Menahem Me
 ndel of Kotzk\, Amud ha’Emet (selections)\n\n+++++\n\nOur “Thinking Matters
 : Modern Jewish Philosophy” course series continues this spring!\n\nJoin an
  impressive line-up of teachers to wrestle with the exciting and challengin
 g questions of modern Jewish philosophy! Can there be such a thing as a Jew
 ish philosophy\, or a philosophy of Judaism? How have Jewish traditions par
 ticipated in the philosophical canon? How are Judaism and Jewish ideas rele
 vant to the modern relationship of ethics\, theology\, and philosophy?\n\nF
 or an introduction to Jewish modern thought and philosophy\, we recommend S
 teven Katz’s essay\, “Eliezar Berkovits & Modern Jewish Philosophy.”\n\nDet
 ails and readings for the “Thinking Matters” mini-courses taught April - Ju
 ne 2016 are posted on the CBS website: http://bethsholomsf.org/shul-school-
 spring-thinking-matters-series/
LAST-MODIFIED:20160511T060125Z
LOCATION:Board Room
SEQUENCE:3
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Thinking Matters: Modern Jewish Philosophy 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
