UID:lu0hhnp8oo3q7gdo0j838ru0ec@google.com
CREATED:20150305T190249Z
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for an afternoon of premium wine & gourmet chees
 e tasting at Congregation Beth Sholom\, on Sunday\, March 22\, 2015 from 3 
 to 6 p.m. Sip on grapes that will transport you to Napa and Sonoma Valleys\
 , while you pair your tastings with artisan cheeses from Cowgirl Creamery a
 nd listen to the sweet sounds from cellist\, Dr. Alex Kelly. \n\nWe will be
  pouring premium wines from the most prestigious vintners from the great No
 rthern California wine country including: Covenant\, Hagafen\, Patland\, Bu
 rt Street Cellars\, Tetra/Expression\, and B. R. Cohn Winery\, and mead fro
 m the San Francisco Mead Company. Each winery will bring its top of the lin
 e wines\, many of which are not otherwise available outside of the winery. 
 There will be opportunities to sign-up for the vintner’s premium wine clubs
  and to order wines directly from them.\n\nMichael Zilber\, marketing manag
 er of Cowgirl Creamery\, will be available to discuss the exceptional chees
 es he selects to pair with the wines. All are vegetarian-based rennet chees
 es.\n\nMore information about Dr. Kelly can be found at AlexKelly.com. Comp
 limentary child care will be provided.\n\nTickets to the event are $100 per
  person through Friday\, March 20 and $125 thereafter and at the door. We w
 ill be raffling off premium bottles from congregants' cellars and from sele
 ct wineries. Raffle tickets are $25 each and 5 for $100. All proceeds will 
 support our synagogue programs. \n\nTickets can be purchased at: 3rd winech
 eesebethsholome.eventbrite.com or by contacting Julia Yasser\, jyasser@beth
 sholomsf.org or 415.940.7099.\n\nPlease forward this to your friends. You d
 on’t have to be Jewish to enjoy Jewish wines!\nWe hope you and your friends
  can join us!\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20150305T190249Z
LOCATION:Koret Hall
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:3rd Annual Wine & Cheese Tasting Event
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
