DESCRIPTION:February 25\, March 3\, 10\, & 31\nGhetto Thinking: From the Ve
 nice Ghetto to the Last Ghetto in Lodz\n(4 sessions w/ Dr. Michael Thaler)\
 nDr. Thaler’s classes meet Thursday nights in the CBS Board Room from 7-8:3
 0 p.m.\n\nMarch 10: Lodz: The Last Ghetto\n  Reading: TBD\n\n+++++\n\nOur “
 Thinking Matters: Modern Jewish Philosophy” course series continues this wi
 nter!\n\nJoin an impressive line-up of teachers to wrestle with the excitin
 g and challenging questions of modern Jewish philosophy! Can there be such 
 a thing as a Jewish philosophy\, or a philosophy of Judaism? How have Jewis
 h traditions participated in the philosophical canon? How are Judaism and J
 ewish ideas relevant to the modern relationship of ethics\, theology\, and 
 philosophy?\n\nFor an introduction to Jewish modern thought and philosophy\
 , we recommend Steven Katz’s essay\, “Eliezar Berkovits & Modern Jewish Phi
 losophy.”\n\nDetails and readings for the “Thinking Matters” mini-courses t
 aught in January – March 2016 are included at the link below.\n\nhttp://bet
 hsholomsf.org/shul-school-thinking-matters-2/
LAST-MODIFIED:20160316T214449Z
LOCATION:Board Room
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Thinking Matters: Modern Jewish Philosophy 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
