DESCRIPTION:Traveling Tikkun Leil Shavuot Shul Crawl!\n\nJoin rabbis and te
 achers from Congregation Beth Sholom\, Sherith Israel\, Emanu-El\, and the 
 Jewish Community Center of San Francisco\, for a stimulating evening of lea
 rning and schmoozing on Saturday\, May 23. Our forbears\, the original Isra
 elites\, had to escape slavery in Egypt\, cross the Red Sea\, and wander th
 e desert before they were given the revelation at Sinai. We have it much ea
 sier. We only need to join up with the SF Jewish community and walk along t
 he California Street corridor to receive wonderful nuggets of learning from
  our own rabbis and those from other congregations. We hope you will join u
 s! \n\nSCHEDULE \n8:30-9:15 p.m. - Music and Havdallah with Emanu-El Cantor
  Marsha Attie and Rabbi Julie Saxe-Taller of Congregation Sherith Israel.\n
 2266 California Street\n \n9:45-10:45 p.m. - Coffee tasting and Tikkun at t
 he Jewish Community Center. \n3200 California Street\n \n10:45-11:45 p.m. -
  Panel discussion on “What do we do with the parts of the Torah we wish we 
 had not received?” at Congregation Emanu-El.\n2 Lake Street\n \n11:45 p.m.-
 5:54 a.m. - End the journey at Congregation Beth Sholom with teachings by R
 abbi Glazer\, Henry Hollander\, and more from midnight till Shacharit! \n30
 1 14th Avenue\n\nClick here to view the promotional flyer.  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\
 n\n\n Facebook \n\n\n\n Twitter \n\n\n\n Website \n\n\n\n Email \n\n\n\n\n\
 n\nCopyright © 2015 Congregation Beth Sholom\, All rights reserved.\nYou ar
 e receiving this email because you are a member of Congregation Beth Sholom
  or have subscribed to our mailing list.\n\nOur mailing address is:\nCongre
 gation Beth Sholom\n301 14 Avenue\, San Francisco\, CA 94118\, United State
 s\nSan Francisco\, CA 94118\n\nAdd us to your address book\n\n\nunsubscribe
  from this list    update subscription preferences \n\n \n\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20150521T233121Z
LOCATION:Gronowski Family Chapel
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Traveling Tikkun Leil Shavuot Shul Crawl
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
