UID:0f3456ftiit7j9shve0fnftlmo@google.com
CREATED:20160127T213000Z
DESCRIPTION:Shabbat Art Experience is a new activity for families with chil
 dren in grades 2nd – 6th that will occur on Shabbats when our CBS Shabbat S
 chool is not taking place. The program is free of charge\, however particip
 ation in each session is limited to the first ten families that RSVP. Pleas
 e RSVP to Michael Lederman (mlederman@bethsholomsf.org). \n\nLed by Elyssa 
 Wortzman\, a visual artist with experience teaching and creating community 
 programming for children and adults in the New York\, Toronto\, and San Fra
 ncisco Jewish communities\, these sessions are open to all. We invite CBS S
 habbat School families to join us\, but also encourage families from the gr
 eater Jewish community (e.g.\, the Brandeis School) to participate in these
  free activities!\n\nDuring this Shabbat Art Experience\, participants will
  look at artist Archie Rand's satirical painting of the 501st mitzvah ("Do 
 not insult or harm anybody with words!") and Reb Nachman of Breslov's teach
 ing about seeing the good in everyone. Kids will have the opportunity to cr
 eate collages interpreting these teachings\, and these artworks may be hung
  in your homes as a reminder to use their ayin tov (eyes of seeing the good
 ).\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20160128T194118Z
LOCATION:Main Meeting Room
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Shabbat Art Experience
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
