UID:6qk9vlj73m7vcc9k0cecs7uh6k@google.com
CREATED:20140724T183824Z
DESCRIPTION:On Tuesday\, August 5\, Rabbi Glazer will conclude the Fast of 
 Tisha B'Av with services\, preceded by a contemplative art ‘walk and talk’ 
 called\, “Creation from Destruction” about the new painting series on displ
 ay in the CBS Gallery\, entitled\, Aleph Beit After Auschwitz.\n\n6 p.m. - 
 Minyan in the Gronowski Family Chapel with Torah and Haftarah reading\n6:30
  - 8:30 p.m. - Beginning & concluding with a sit in the meditation room\, R
 abbi Glazer will lead contemplative 'walk and talk' art tour of his paintin
 gs\, Aleph Beit After Auschwitz\n8:30 - 9 p.m. - Ma'ariv service in the Gro
 nowski Family Chapel\n9 p.m. - Break-the-Fast meal in the Main Meeting Room
  \n\n\n    
LAST-MODIFIED:20140724T183931Z
LOCATION:Makom Sholom\, GF Chapel\, Main Meeting Room
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Fast of Tisha B'Av Conclusion with "Creation from Destruction" walk
  and talk
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20140828T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20140828T203000
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:1ukqfpans6q89jpq7b0rdl5geg@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20140828T193000
CREATED:20140805T185550Z
DESCRIPTION:With millions of viewers on the edge of their seats for each ep
 isode as this series enters its fifth season\, everyone is wondering— Who w
 ill take back the throne? Nine noble families fight for control of the myth
 ical land of Westeros. Intrigue is pervasive. All while a very ancient evil
  awakens in the farthest north and all that stands between the realms of th
 e holy and icy horrors beyond is a neglected military order of misfits\, th
 e Night's Watch. Drawing on the zeitgeist of Game of Thrones\, join us as w
 e explore the mystical underpinnings of this journey to take back the thron
 e. These mystical resonances—common to a genre of vision quests—continue te
 ll a mythic tale. Why does that tale of the journey continue to captivate u
 s today? We will explore this pilgrimage of archetypal encounters in a ques
 t for psycho-spiritual integration through The Journey of Losing the Prince
 ss as told by Reb Nahman of Bratzlav. Translations of the story available f
 rom David Wolk.
LAST-MODIFIED:20140810T213113Z
LOCATION:Board Room
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:What's the Kabbalah behind Game of Thrones?
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
