DESCRIPTION:301 14th Avenue\, Rabin Library/ Room 125\n \nClub Shabbat is a
  special program designed to provide children of all ages with a Shabbat re
 lated spiritual\, educational and social experience in the synagogue. Every
  Saturday morning from 10 a.m.-12 noon\, counselors and childcare providers
  stand by to care for our congregation's children while parents attend serv
 ices.  I invite parents to check out the following programs: \n\n•Childcare
  is provided to families with children ages newborn–7 in Room 27 located on
  the second floor in the school building. Kit and Erin\, our childcare prov
 iders\, will provide interactive Shabbat appropriate activities.\n\n•School
 -age children will gather in the Youth Lounge with Alisa and David\, the Sh
 abbat counselors\, for board games\, discussions\, sports and social activi
 ties\; they will also use the library for reading and prayers.\n\nAll child
 ren are invited to join the congregation for the concluding Adon Olam praye
 r at the end of morning services\, followed by Kiddush.\n\nFor more informa
 tion call Yaffa Tygiel at 415.221.8736\, ext. 106.
LAST-MODIFIED:20090219T235818Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Club Shabbat
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
