BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20160204T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20160204T203000
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:0ovj3n84qdoi5f6chg9lgoairk@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20160204T190000
CREATED:20150902T235309Z
DESCRIPTION:January 14\, 21\, 28\, & February 4\nWalter Benjamin: A Jewish 
 Nietzsche? (4 sessions w/ Michael Loebs)\nMichael Loebs' classes meet Thurs
 day nights in the CBS Board Room from 7-8:30 p.m.\n\nFebruary 4: Redemption
  from History & Messianism\n\nReading 1: Friedrich Nietzsche\, On the Advan
 tage & Disadvantage of History (Forward\, Sec. 1-3\, 6-7) \n\nReading 2: Wa
 lter Benjamin\, Über den Begriff der Geschichte (On the Concept of History 
 / Theses on the Philosophy of History\, 1940)\, w/ “Theologico-Political Fr
 agment”\n\n+++++\n\nOur “Thinking Matters: Modern Jewish Philosophy” course
  series continues this winter!\n\nJoin an impressive line-up of teachers to
  wrestle with the exciting and challenging questions of modern Jewish philo
 sophy! Can there be such a thing as a Jewish philosophy\, or a philosophy o
 f Judaism? How have Jewish traditions participated in the philosophical can
 on? How are Judaism and Jewish ideas relevant to the modern relationship of
  ethics\, theology\, and philosophy?\n\nFor an introduction to Jewish moder
 n thought and philosophy\, we recommend Steven Katz’s essay\, “Eliezar Berk
 ovits & Modern Jewish Philosophy.”\n\nDetails and readings for the “Thinkin
 g Matters” mini-courses taught in January – March 2016 are included at the 
 link below.\n\nhttp://bethsholomsf.org/shul-school-thinking-matters-2/
LAST-MODIFIED:20160316T214449Z
LOCATION:Board Room
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Thinking Matters: Modern Jewish Philosophy 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
