BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20090219T033000Z
DTEND:20090219T050000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:1235087898-a0d808c-20802@www.bethsholomsf.org
CREATED:20090219T235818Z
DESCRIPTION:301 14th Avenue\, Board Room\n\nPre-Event Dinner and Workshop\n
 Join Erin Hyman\, PhD for an evening dedicated to all things Ayelet Waldman
 . An opportunity to discuss her work and ideas in a book club setting\, and
  to prepare for a lively Q&A on March 1. A vegetarian dinner will be provid
 ed. RSVP required.\n\nTo learn more about the event\, or to RVSP for the pr
 e-event workshop or childcare\, please contact Ariana Barth in the CBS offi
 ce. ABarth@bethsholomsf.org\, 415.221.8736\, ext. 111. \n\nAbout Ayelet Wal
 dman\n“Maternal ambivalence is my subject\,” says the provocative novelist\
 , essayist\, and mystery writer Ayelet Waldman. In her bestselling and crit
 ically acclaimed novels\, and in essays that have appeared in The New York 
 Times \, the San Francisco Chronicle\, Salon.com and others\, Waldman bring
 s refreshing candor to the socially-charged issues of wifehood\, motherhood
 \, sexuality and family. Waldman is a mother of four and the wife of Pulitz
 er-prize winning author Michael Chabon.
LAST-MODIFIED:20090219T235818Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Pre-Event Dinner and Workshop for Ayelet Waldman
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
