CREATED:20090219T235818Z
DESCRIPTION:301 14th Avenue\, Board Room\n\nIn this course we will read the
  biblical text\, examine the historical evidence of David's reign\, study t
 he poetry\, listen to the music\, and admire the extensive art (including p
 aintings\, drawings\, engravings\, woodcuts\, stained glass\, and sculpture
 s) based on King David's story. From anonymous early manuscript illustrator
 s\, to medieval Italian\, Dutch and German painters\, through great Renaiss
 ance artists\, to nineteenth-century and contemporary painters\, we will se
 e how the many aspects of the David story have been interpreted.\n\nTo regi
 ster contact Yaffa Tygiel at YTygiel@bethsholomsf.org.
LAST-MODIFIED:20090219T235818Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Course on King David
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20150531T220000Z
DTEND:20150601T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:kas1ei4f4od51dcjm3ciqhp1ug@google.com
CREATED:20150423T173819Z
DESCRIPTION:"In this Place\," an exhibition featuring the work of San Franc
 isco artists\, Elyssa Wortzman and Andrea Guerra\, will open at CBS on Sund
 ay\, May 31 with a special event and run through the end of June. The exhib
 ition explores the story of Jacob's ladder and how we find and mark sacred 
 space in unnoticed places. Guerra and Wortzman explore how we define\, tran
 sform and discover sacred "place" and how the image of ascending and descen
 ding the ladder - moving between the highs and lows of daily life - is part
  of this process. \n\nOpening Event\n\nJoin us on Sunday\, May 31\, from 3-
 6 p.m.\,  for a community event and exhibition opening for all ages:\n3-4 p
 .m.\nA guided art project to decorate the stairway (in the Rainbow courtyar
 d) as an interpretive Jacob’s ladder.\n4-4:30 p.m.\nGuided tour of the exhi
 bition and Q&A with the artists.\n4:30-6 p.m.\nPeruse the exhibit at your l
 eisure and enjoy food prepared by our Davka Ysrael group\, a new CBS group 
 planning events to highlight Israeli culture and much more! If you are inte
 rested in learning more about the group\, there will be an opportunity to s
 peak with some of the members at the event.  
LAST-MODIFIED:20150423T173819Z
LOCATION:Gronowski Family Chapel Gallery 
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:In this Place Opening Event
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
