DESCRIPTION:301 14th Avenue\, Gronowski Family Chapel\n\nThe Learners' Miny
 an: Introduction to Jewish Prayer\n\n4 Classes Monday nights\nFebruary 2\, 
 9\, 16\, 23\n\nWe will be studying the evening prayer service. All the idea
 s and concepts discussed in class will also apply to the Shabbat and Festiv
 al services.\n\n\n"I had been going to shul since I was a child\, but that 
 didn’t mean I understood what was going on -- the Learners’ Minyan made the
  service much more understandable and approachable.”\n(from a student)\n\n•
 Deepen your personal connection to the prayer service\n•Increase your abili
 ty to participate\n•Learn to develop spiritual mindfulness (kavanah)\n•Disc
 over the liturgical\, spiritual\, and emotional structure of the service\n\
 nThe traditional service offers a deep and intricate path of spirituality. 
 But the ancient origins and depth of its meanings can also make the service
  seem inaccessible and forbidding. \n\nThe goal of the Learners' Minyan is 
 to help each student find personal meaning and connection to the words of t
 his ancient prayer text.\n\nIn class\, we delve deeply into the traditional
  Jewish liturgy\, learning methods of spiritual mindfulness\, practicing pa
 tterns of movement and speech\, and struggling with the meaning of the word
 s. The Learners' Minyan offers students the opportunity to take some first 
 steps on the path to Jewish spirituality.\n\nThe Learners' Minyan is taught
  by congregants David Malman and Ellen Shireman. Classes include study foll
 owed by a shortened service. For more information please contact David Malm
 an (david@aldsf.com) and Ellen Shireman (ellenshireman@aol.com).
LAST-MODIFIED:20090219T235818Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Learners' Minyan
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
