UID:reu58un5tu52qcvak4p9555vm4@google.com
CREATED:20150706T162122Z
DESCRIPTION:Oz chronicles his childhood in Jerusalem at the end of the Brit
 ish Mandate for Palestine and the early years of the State of Israel\, and 
 his teenage years on Kibbutz Hulda. As a child\, he crossed paths with prom
 inent figures in Israeli society\, among them Shmuel Yosef Agnon\, Shaul Tc
 hernichovsky\, and David Ben-Gurion. One of his teachers was the Israeli po
 et Zelda. Joseph Klausner was his great-uncle. Told in a non-linear fashion
 \, Oz's story is interwoven with tales of his family's Eastern European roo
 ts. The family's name was Klausner. By changing the name to a Hebrew one\, 
 Oz rebelled against that European background while affirming loyalty to the
  land of his birth.
LAST-MODIFIED:20150706T162410Z
LOCATION:Rabin Library 
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:CBS Book Club: Discussing Amos Oz: A Tale of Love and Darkness
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20150813T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20150813T213000
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;UNTIL=20150821T030000Z;BYDAY=TH
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:rehpdmp44jd8h9irkbvmqpne2k@google.com
CREATED:20150813T174750Z
DESCRIPTION:As the Psalmist wonders by the rivers of Babylon\, in the heart
  of exile\, so too in our own day many of us in the heart of the diaspora w
 onder how we shall sing a new song of religious Zionism\, of Eretz Yisrael\
 , of the Holy Land?\n\nJoin us for this 2 session mini-course Thursdays\, A
 ugust 13 and August 20\, at 8 p.m.\, as we explore the theological roots at
  the heart of songs for Zion\, starting with the Israeli national anthem\, 
 Hatikvah\, understanding how it re-reads biblical theology in light of Zion
 ism and then exploring some new anthems by contemporary Hebrew songwriters 
 and poets like Yonatan Razel and Haviva Pedaya.\n\nAll are welcome\, texts 
 and music will be explored in Hebrew with English translations.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20150813T174750Z
LOCATION:Board Room
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Rabbi Glazer's August Mini-Course: "How Shall We Sing a Song of Zio
 n?"
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
