DESCRIPTION:February 11\, 18\, & March 17\, 24\nPhilosophy of Purim: Modern
 ity & Perennial Parody (4 sessions w/ Rabbi Aubrey Glazer) Rabbi Glazer’s c
 lasses meet Thursday nights in the CBS Board Room from 6:30-7 p.m. \n\nFebr
 uary 18: Philosophy of Purim in Woody Allen\, Part II: Zelig\, Inauthentici
 ty\, & Personal Identity  \nReading: TBD\n\n+++++\n\nOur “Thinking Matters:
  Modern Jewish Philosophy” course series continues this winter!\n\nJoin an 
 impressive line-up of teachers to wrestle with the exciting and challenging
  questions of modern Jewish philosophy! Can there be such a thing as a Jewi
 sh philosophy\, or a philosophy of Judaism? How have Jewish traditions part
 icipated in the philosophical canon? How are Judaism and Jewish ideas relev
 ant to the modern relationship of ethics\, theology\, and philosophy?\n\nFo
 r an introduction to Jewish modern thought and philosophy\, we recommend St
 even Katz’s essay\, “Eliezar Berkovits & Modern Jewish Philosophy.”\n\nDeta
 ils and readings for the “Thinking Matters” mini-courses taught in January 
 – March 2016 are included at the link below.\n\nhttp://bethsholomsf.org/shu
 l-school-thinking-matters-2/
LAST-MODIFIED:20160316T214449Z
LOCATION:Board Room
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Thinking Matters: Modern Jewish Philosophy 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
