DESCRIPTION:January 14\, 21\, 28\, & February 4\nWalter Benjamin: A Jewish 
 Nietzsche? (4 sessions w/ Michael Loebs)\nMichael Loeb’s classes meet Thurs
 day nights in the CBS Board Room from 7-8:30 p.m.\n\nJanuary 14: On Friends
 hip As Metaphysics\n Reading: Friedrich Nietzsche\, “of the Three Metamorph
 oses\,” “Of War and Warriors\,” and “Of the Friend\,” from Thus Spake Zarat
 hrustra\, Part I\n\n Reading: Walter Benjamin\, “Dialogue on the Religiosit
 y of the Present” (1912)\n\n+++++\n\nOur “Thinking Matters: Modern Jewish P
 hilosophy” course series continues this winter!\n\nJoin an impressive line-
 up of teachers to wrestle with the exciting and challenging questions of mo
 dern Jewish philosophy! Can there be such a thing as a Jewish philosophy\, 
 or a philosophy of Judaism? How have Jewish traditions participated in the 
 philosophical canon? How are Judaism and Jewish ideas relevant to the moder
 n relationship of ethics\, theology\, and philosophy?\n\nFor an introductio
 n to Jewish modern thought and philosophy\, we recommend Steven Katz’s essa
 y\, “Eliezar Berkovits & Modern Jewish Philosophy.”\n\nDetails and readings
  for the “Thinking Matters” mini-courses taught in January – March 2016 are
  included at the link below.\n\nhttp://bethsholomsf.org/shul-school-thinkin
 g-matters-2/
LAST-MODIFIED:20160316T214449Z
LOCATION:Board Room
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Thinking Matters: Modern Jewish Philosophy 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
