CREATED:20150902T235309Z
DESCRIPTION:February 11\, 18\, & March 17\, 24\nPhilosophy of Purim: Modern
 ity & Perennial Parody (4 sessions w/ Rabbi Aubrey Glazer) Rabbi Glazer’s c
 lasses meet Thursday nights in the CBS Board Room from 6:30-8 p.m. \n\nMarc
 h 24: Philosophy of Purim in The Big Lebowski\, Part II: “That Ain’t Legal 
 Either\,” Rules\, Authenticity\, & Hyper-nomianism   Reading: TBD\n\n+++++\
 n\nOur “Thinking Matters: Modern Jewish Philosophy” course series continues
  this winter!\n\nJoin an impressive line-up of teachers to wrestle with the
  exciting and challenging questions of modern Jewish philosophy! Can there 
 be such a thing as a Jewish philosophy\, or a philosophy of Judaism? How ha
 ve Jewish traditions participated in the philosophical canon? How are Judai
 sm and Jewish ideas relevant to the modern relationship of ethics\, theolog
 y\, and philosophy?\n\nFor an introduction to Jewish modern thought and phi
 losophy\, we recommend Steven Katz’s essay\, “Eliezar Berkovits & Modern Je
 wish Philosophy.”\n\nDetails and readings for the “Thinking Matters” mini-c
 ourses taught in January – March 2016 are included at the link below.\n\nht
 tp://bethsholomsf.org/shul-school-thinking-matters-2/
LAST-MODIFIED:20160316T214449Z
LOCATION:Board Room
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Thinking Matters: Modern Jewish Philosophy 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
