UID:4j1pka7enhtr4lis54gm001llc@google.com
CREATED:20140827T220439Z
DESCRIPTION:Movie Screening: American Jerusalem\nFollowed by Q&A with Marc 
 Dollinger\, Ph.D.\n\nJoin us on Wednesday\, September 10\, at 6:30 p.m. whe
 n we screen American Jerusalem: Jews and the Making of San Francisco\, the 
 epic story of the pioneering Jews of San Francisco\, their rise to prominen
 ce\, and how\, freed from discrimination\, they reinvented themselves as a 
 distinctly new kind of Jew: they weren't just American Jews—they were San F
 rancisco Jews. Following the film we will have a question and answer by Mar
 c Dollinger\, Ph.D.\, historian and Richard and Rhoda Goldman Chair in Jewi
 sh Studies and Social Responsibility at San Francisco State University.\n\n
 Pizza\, beer\, wine\, and kid-friendly refreshments will be served. Pizza a
 nd drinks are $10 for adults and $5 for children ages 5-12. Complimentary c
 hildcare will be provided. Please R.S.V.P. to rsvp@bethsholomsf.org or call
  415.221.8736\, by Friday\, September 5 so we know how much pizza to order.
  \n
LAST-MODIFIED:20140827T220456Z
LOCATION:Koret Hall
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Dr. Marc Dollinger Film and Talk
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
