DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20160407T200000
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:0ovj3n84qdoi5f6chg9lgoairk@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20160407T190000
CREATED:20150902T235309Z
DESCRIPTION:April 7\, 14 & May 5\, 12\nPhilosophies of Early Zionism\n(4 se
 ssions w/ Ephraim Margolin)\nMr. Margolin’s classes meet Thursday nights in
  the Main Meeting Room from 6:30-8 p.m.\n\nApril 7: Biblical Zionism\nReadi
 ng: N/A\n\n+++++\n\nOur “Thinking Matters: Modern Jewish Philosophy” course
  series continues this spring!\n\nJoin an impressive line-up of teachers to
  wrestle with the exciting and challenging questions of modern Jewish philo
 sophy! Can there be such a thing as a Jewish philosophy\, or a philosophy o
 f Judaism? How have Jewish traditions participated in the philosophical can
 on? How are Judaism and Jewish ideas relevant to the modern relationship of
  ethics\, theology\, and philosophy?\n\nFor an introduction to Jewish moder
 n thought and philosophy\, we recommend Steven Katz’s essay\, “Eliezar Berk
 ovits & Modern Jewish Philosophy.”\n\nhttp://bethsholomsf.org/shul-school-s
 pring-thinking-matters-series/
LAST-MODIFIED:20160331T064233Z
LOCATION:Main Meeting Room
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Thinking Matters: Modern Jewish Philosophy 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
