UID:tjelna3i31cbo5q2irjeaudthk@google.com
CREATED:20170227T195047Z
DESCRIPTION:The CBS Book Club will meet in the Rabin Library. The book to b
 e discussed is: Meir Shalev's memoir\, "My Russian Grandmother and Her Amer
 ican Vacuum Cleaner"\n\nFrom  Publishers' Weekly:\n"In this tender\, hilari
 ous memoir of his grandparents' early life as new settlers to Palestine\, I
 sraeli author Shalev (A Pigeon and a Boy) evokes all his idealism and disap
 pointments in Zionism. A new GE vacuum cleaner sent by Uncle Yeshayahu in A
 merica underscored for the hard-working migrants from Russia to mid-1930s P
 alestine their poverty and their pride: while Uncle Yeshayahu had gone to L
 os Angeles to become a rich businessman\, his brother\, Aharon\, and sister
 -in-law\, Tonia\, migrated to Palestine\, resolved to plow the land\, creat
 ing a socialist state and "foothold for persecuted and wandering Jews." How
 ever\, it was undeniably backbreaking labor\, especially for the author's g
 randma Tonia\, a woman originally from the Ukrainian village of Rokitno\, w
 ho is obsessed with cleaning the dust from her house and jealously guards t
 he "svieeperrr" in the locked bathroom\, never to use it again\, mostly bec
 ause it too will get dirty. The author joyfully remembers those days he spe
 nt as a boy with his grandparents in the bucolic Jezreel Valley\, and in th
 is quirky tribute commemorates the spirit of an exacting\, tireless charact
 er who was "the purified essence of us all\, for better and worse."\n\nThe 
 book is available in print through the San Francisco Public Library and in 
 print or Kindle format through Amazon.\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20170303T232648Z
LOCATION:Rabin Family Library
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:CBS Book Club
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
