UID:jom35bknip8tj5r6801uqqu0ps@google.com
CREATED:20160914T184539Z
DESCRIPTION:Zion(ism) Matters\n"On Love Of Israel"\nNovember 10\, December 
 8\, January 26\, & February 23\n(4 sessions w/ Ephraim Margolin\, Esq.)\n\n
 Registration: https://www.universe.com/cbsthinkingmatters\n\nCourse Descrip
 tion: Ephraim Margolin is a longtime professor of law who\, before moving t
 o the United States\, served as Secretary to Menachem Begin\, leader of the
  IRGUN. He is a Hebrew University and Yale Law School graduate who has a ri
 ch knowledge of Israeli politics and culture. This four-session mini-course
  will consider Israel through a contemporary lens\, drawing on the country’
 s remarkable history and much Jewish thinking. Session 1: "Limits On Critic
 ism of Israel"\; Session 2: "Glorifying & Rejecting Jewish Power"\; Session
  3: "Academic Take On Nationalism & Bi-Nationalism"\; Session 4: "Self-Hate
  In Modern Israeli Culture."\n\n\nReadings: TBD\n\nAll sessions are FREE fo
 r CBS members\, but students are encouraged to make a donation to CBS. For 
 nonmembers\, each single session is $12. Alternatively\, nonmembers can pur
 chase an 8-session pack for $84\, or the full semester subscription for $18
 0.
LAST-MODIFIED:20161206T222513Z
LOCATION:Boardroom
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Zion(ism) Matters
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
