DESCRIPTION:Shaliach tzibbur (prayer leader)\, musician\, and teacher Aviva
  Chernick returns to CBS to lead "Renew Our Days: The High Holy Days Unboun
 d\," a special\, two-part service occurring on the mornings of Rosh Hashana
 h Day 1 and Yom Kippur. \n\n"Renew Our Days" is not halachic (e.g.\, there 
 is no Torah service) – the experimental service is based on traditional lit
 urgy\, but not bound to it. Highlighting selected passages and prayers\, Av
 iva will guide participants on a journey\, an opportunity to rediscover and
  reconnect with the spiritual\, emotional\, and intellectual substance of J
 ewish prayer and the High Holy Days. “So much of what we want and need is a
 lready in the liturgy\,” Aviva says\, and it extends “an invitation to our 
 spirits\, voices\, bodies\, and minds.”\n\nJoin us in song\, prayer\, and r
 eflection as we experience the "Days of Awe" in a fresh and inspiring way.\
 n\n"Renew Our Days" is open to all CBS High Holy Day ticket holders\, but s
 pace is limited. Please plan to join us promptly at 10 a.m. The service wil
 l end at approximately 1 p.m.\n\nFor details and registration: http://beths
 holomsf.org/?p=9195\n\nIf you would like to read\, blow the shofar\, greet 
 attendees\, etc.\, please email Aviva.\n\n"Renew Our Days" is supported by 
 two anonymous grants.
LAST-MODIFIED:20160814T012503Z
LOCATION:Gronowski Family Chapel
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Aviva Chernick's "Renew Our Days" service
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
