BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20170505T010000Z
DTEND:20170505T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:8cgpnmas3bgicui1ncdjt4gp8k@google.com
CREATED:20170308T234759Z
DESCRIPTION:CBS kids in Grades 4 & 5\, please join us for a discussion abou
 t Susan Lynn Meyer's book\, "Black Radishes." This work of historical ficti
 on\, inspired by the author’s father’s experience\, is set in France in 194
 0. When Paris is occupied by the Nazis\, a 10-year-old boy\, Gustave\, and 
 his family have to flee to the French countryside. Gustave’s new friend Nic
 ole works with the French Resistance\, and when Gustave learns that German 
 soldiers love to eat black radishes\, he comes up with a clever scheme to u
 se them as a distraction when helping his father to smuggle Jewish relative
 s across the occupied line. The book is the winner of the Sydney Taylor Hon
 or Award and is appropriate for 4th graders and up.\n\nOur discussion will 
 take place in the CBS Boardroom from 6 – 7 p.m.\, and be facilitated by How
 ard Freedman\, CBS congregant and director of the Jewish Community Library.
  Participants will also be able to have a Skype conversation with the autho
 r of the book! Dinner will be served.\n\nPlease borrow a copy of the book f
 rom the Jewish Community Library or purchase a book from your favorite loca
 l book store\, or on-line. The book is available from Amazon for $3.\n\nREG
 ISTRATION: please email elincohen@hotmail.com to register. The cost for the
  program\, dinner\, and a hardbound edition of "Skating with the Statue of 
 Liberty\," the new sequel to Black Radishes is $18. Please pay via PayPal. 
 (We've decided to purchase the sequel Skating with the Statue of Liberty to
  show our appreciation to the author who is volunteering her time talking t
 o our kids.)
LAST-MODIFIED:20170323T163728Z
LOCATION:Boardroom
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:CBS Book Club for Kids (Grades 4 & 5)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
