CREATED:20160914T000327Z
DESCRIPTION:Thinking Matters\n"Elie Wiesel and the Problems of Holocaust Re
 presentation"\nSeptember 22\, October 27\, January 12 & 19\, February 2\, M
 arch 2 & 30\, & April 20 (8 sessions w/ Dr. Michael Thaler)\n\nRegistration
 : https://www.universe.com/cbsthinkingmatters\n\nCourse Description: Elie W
 iesel is universally recognized as the leading voice of Holocaust commemora
 tion and interpretation. This course will trace Wiesel’s trajectory from mu
 te survivor to the world’s foremost interlocutor of the Shoah\, and his jou
 rney\, recently completed\, from dejected mourner for his lost faith to dev
 out practitioner. Students will discuss significant differences in content 
 and message between Wiesel’s original Yiddish memoir\, Un di velt hot geshv
 ign (And the World Remained Silent)\, which is known only to a handful of s
 cholars\, and the universally acclaimed French (La Nuit) and English (Night
 ) versions. We will also compare Wiesel’s work of Holocaust representation 
 with the accounts of other key witnesses. Each class session will focus on 
 one of the eight chapters of Un di velt hot geshvign and the corresponding 
 section in Night.\n\nReadings:\nElie Wiesel\, Un Di Velt Hot Geshvign (Yidd
 ish)\nElie Wiesel\, La Nuit (French) and Night (English)\nJerzy Kosinski\, 
 The Painted Bird\nTadeusz Borowski\, This Way To The Gas\, Ladies and Gentl
 emen\nCharlotte Delbo\, None Of Us Will Return\nJean Amery\, At The Mind’s 
 Limits\nPrimo Levi\, Survival In Auschwitz\n\nCost per session for CBS memb
 ers is $12. Alternatively\, members can purchase an 8-session pack for $84 
 or a full semester subscription (17 sessions confirmed to date) for $180. F
 or nonmembers\, each session is $24\, $168 for an 8-session pack\, or $360 
 for the full semester subscription.
LAST-MODIFIED:20161102T232806Z
LOCATION:Main Meeting Room
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Thinking Matters
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
