CREATED:20170306T203639Z
DESCRIPTION:Purim is a holiday that celebrates reversals and inversions\, w
 hich is why the most appropriate Purim greeting is "V’nahafokh hu!" ("We sh
 all invert things!").\n\nRabbi Julia Andelman of the Jewish Theological Sem
 inary writes\, "Cross-dressing\, inebriation\, public parodies of teachers 
 and friends—all of these traditionally questionable or forbidden boundary c
 rossings are sanctioned and even celebrated on this one day of the year whe
 n norms are freely reversed." Let's not disappoint!\n\nJoin the CBS communi
 ty this coming Saturday\, March 11\, at 8 p.m. to kick off our Purim revelr
 y with a rowdy megillah reading in Koret Hall. We'll be providing some unor
 thodox (but kosher) flourishes during the reading\, which will be followed 
 by a wild dance party DJed by congregant Ovid Jacob.\n\nCome in costume (of
  course) and bring your own hooch. Bonus points if you have to be carried h
 ome. But sleep it off\, because you'll need to return to CBS the next morni
 ng for "Purimpalooza."
LAST-MODIFIED:20170306T203652Z
LOCATION:Koret Hall
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Havdalah & Purim party
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
