UID:nl1i2m8sa67jra9p6n1jui8t10@google.com
CREATED:20160914T181706Z
DESCRIPTION:Thinking Matters\n"Ethics In Sacrificing One Life For Another"\
 nNovember 17\n(1 session w/ Rabbi Doug Kahn)\n\nRegistration: https://www.u
 niverse.com/cbsthinkingmatters\n\nCourse Description: “Two people were trav
 eling\, and [only] one of them had a canteen of water. [There was only enou
 gh water so that] if both of them drank they would both die\, but if one of
  them drank [only]\, he would make it back to an inhabited area [and live].
  Ben Petura taught: ‘Better both should drink and die than that one see his
  friend’s death\,’ until Rabbi Akiva came and taught: ‘Your brother should 
 live with you’ (Vayikra 25:36) – your life takes precedence over the life o
 f your friend’s.’” (Bava Metzia 62a) This one-session class wrestles with t
 he ultimate ethical issue – saving one life at the expense of another. Rabb
 i Kahn will examine how Jewish law was applied to agonizing life-for-life s
 ituations during the Holocaust and continues to be relevant in today’s worl
 d.\n\nReadings: None\n\nCost per session for CBS members is $12. Alternativ
 ely\, members can purchase an 8-session pack for $84 or a full semester sub
 scription (17 sessions confirmed to date) for $180. For nonmembers\, each s
 ession is $24\, $168 for an 8-session pack\, or $360 for the full semester 
 subscription.
LAST-MODIFIED:20160914T181706Z
LOCATION:Main Meeting Room
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Thinking Matters
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
