CREATED:20171214T021016Z
DESCRIPTION:The Dr. Ernest M. Weitz Breakfast Club is a quarterly breakfast
  gathering featuring a thought-provoking guest speaker. The Club is dedicat
 ed to increasing knowledge of contemporary Jewish issues and ideas. Many of
  the speakers are leaders in the San Francisco Bay Area Jewish community. \
 n\nWhere: Koret Hall\nNext Speaker: "Begin Again: Songs of Peace and Hope\,
 " Cantor Rita Glassman\n\nJoin members the Dr. E.M. Weitz Breakfast Club on
  Sunday\, January 28\, at 9 a.m.\, for a presentation by Cantor Rita Glassm
 an\, who writes that “music is a universal language that can act as a power
 ful bridge between people of all faiths and cultures. It is also\, at its b
 est\, a magnificent tool that can reach the heart when nothing else can.”\n
 \nCantor Glassman's "Begin Again: Songs of Peace and Hope" weaves together 
 music and stories\, and participation will likely be invited in some of the
  songs and prayers. "Begin Again" is guaranteed to calm\, soothe\, and insp
 ire.\n\nCantor Glassman is an ordained cantor\, singer/songwriter and board
 -certified chaplain\, with a particular interest in music that reaches and 
 lifts the heart and heals the spirit. In her cantorial role\, Rita has serv
 ed congregations in New York\, Marin County\, and\, most recently\, Congreg
 ation Sherith Israel in San Francisco. She has recorded six cds with origin
 al music on the themes of healing and peace.\n\nContact: Beth Jones \nFees:
  $40 per year for an individual\, $80 for a couple\,\n   or $15 per meeting
 . Checks payable to: Congregation\n   Beth Sholom (please write “Dr. Ernest
  M. Breakfast Club\n   Dues” in the note section)
LAST-MODIFIED:20180122T234954Z
LOCATION:Koret Hall
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Dr. Ernest M. Weitz Breakfast Club
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
