UID:3h98j399cv35aq4atumvk4bvk9@google.com
CREATED:20180913T225049Z
DESCRIPTION:Come to the 50th Annual CBS Yom Kippur Lecture by Ephraim Margo
 lin\n\nCongregation Beth Sholom is pleased to announce that Ephraim Margoli
 n will provide us with his 50th Yom Kippur Lecture entitled\, Mosaic of the
  Moseic Teaching.\n\nThe lecture will highlight an untranslated love story 
 by Amos Oz and provide comments about Love. Ephraim will address how Jews i
 nvented the concept of Love as our basic moral teaching. Why were we differ
 ent than any other religions at the time and remained tribal\, curious\, ch
 oosy\, and devoted to family lives and to Israel? A very personal account…\
 n\nEphraim Margolin is a local attorney\, activist\, and scholar. He was bo
 rn in Berlin\; raised in Poland and Tel Aviv (where one of his house guests
  was a young Polish refugee named Menachem Begin)\; served in Israel’s War 
 for Independence with the Irgun\; served as Menachem Begin’s secretary\; an
 d has taught and practiced law in the Bay Area\, served as president of the
  San Francisco Jewish Community Council\, and provided free legal service t
 o Israelis.
LAST-MODIFIED:20180913T225049Z
LOCATION:Sanctuary 
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Yom Kippur Lecture by Ephraim Margolin
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
