UID:1u17b73ib6gmm9lonnj426n4q9@google.com
CREATED:20180309T162840Z
DESCRIPTION:Americana is a cholent – a rich stew – of diverse musical diale
 cts and perspectives\, including folk\, bluegrass\, country\, soul\, gospel
 \, rock\, and more.<br><br>Like the Jewish experience\, though\, Americana’
 s disparate elements work in unison to create an original sound and story t
 hat we recognize as specifically American.<br><br>Joan Baez\, The Grateful 
 Dead\, Bob Dylan\, Neil Young\, Joni Mitchell\, The Derailers\, The Lone Be
 llow\, and Son Volt – all of these artists and performers are on the same f
 amiliar road\, searching for a way back home. We are their fellow travelers
 .<br><br>Congregation Beth Sholom invites you to experience the Americana J
 am Band Kabbalat Shabbat!<br><br>It’s a folk-rock jam session with a Jewish
  soul\, a casual prayer service with country swagger. If you like to sing a
 nd/or play an instrument (think piano\, guitar\, double bass\, melodica\, h
 armonica\, or vibraphone)\, pull up a chair and join the jam on select Frid
 ay nights in 2017-18. Maybe you won’t always play “in the pocket”\, but tha
 t’s not the point – it’s about our journey. Together\, we’ll make music in 
 a sacred space and create something new and meaningful as we mark the week’
 s end and the arrival of Shabbat.<br><br>Let’s jam on Friday\, March 23\, a
 t 6:30 p.m.! The Americana Jam Band Kabbalat Shabbat service is free\, but 
 pre-registration is required.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=
 http%3A%2F%2Fbethsholomsf.org%2Famericana-jam-band-returns%2F&amp\;sa=D&amp
 \;usd=2&amp\;usg=AFQjCNGCmNj99uzijTyHi6NmAgcrq60YXw" target="_blank">http:/
 /bethsholomsf.org/americana-jam-band-returns/</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20180309T162840Z
LOCATION:Gronowski Family Chapel
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Americana Jam Band Kabbalat Shabbat Services
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20170520T013000Z
DTEND:20170520T023000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:4106k0gfqupl6hptm02hq04844@google.com
CREATED:20160620T200802Z
DESCRIPTION:The words of our Jewish liturgy may be recited silently\, chant
 ed\, or sung. The CBS Fusion Friday Musical Kabbalat Shabbat series emphasi
 zes the latter\, louder approach!\n\nLed by Rabbi Aubrey Glazer\, the Shir 
 Hashirim Ensemble (Hazzan Richard Kaplan\, violinist Lila Sklar\, and John 
 Erlich on ud and guitar) provides participants with an exquisite Friday nig
 ht service that features Jewish sacred music from around the world - Sefard
 i\, Mizrachi\, and Ashkenazic\, including a Jewish/Turkish/Sufi zikr\, cont
 emplative prayer\, and Zoharic teachings and meditations by Rabbi Glazer.\n
 \nWhen we raise our voices together as a community to welcome Shabbat\, we 
 create a powerful transformative experience\, one that sustains and empower
 s us not just in the moment\, but also during the rest of the week. Let's s
 ing together on Friday\, September 16\, at 6:30 p.m.!
LAST-MODIFIED:20160620T200802Z
LOCATION:Gronowski Family Chapel
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Fusion Friday Kabbalat Shabbat Services
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
