BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20160717T160000Z
DTEND:20160717T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:rtajq9c43fl39ib8q705g6palk@google.com
CREATED:20160630T050255Z
DESCRIPTION:The CBS Book Club will meet Sunday\, April 17 at 9:30am. in the
  Rabin Library. The book to be discussed is: JEWS AND WORDS\, by Amos Oz & 
 Fania Oz-Sulzberger.\n\nThese four long essays – really more of a free-flow
 ing conversation between the noted Israeli novelist and his daughter\, a hi
 storian – focus primarily on the Jews as "a nation only by virtue of its te
 xts\," from the Bible to the work of contemporary Israeli poet Yehuda Amich
 ai – and the interpretations and argumentations that flow from them.\n\nThe
  two combine their considerable talents to examine the role words and langu
 age have played in binding the Jewish people to their heritage. Although ne
 ither is religious (nor\, for that matter\, a believer)\, both find rich me
 aning in the words of the Bible (as well as the commentaries that followed)
 . They theorize that the reason Judaism has survived is more about texts th
 an faith\, with “controversy built into them from the start.” Exhibiting ey
 e-popping feats of literary scholarship and stunning swoops into the minds 
 of writers\, readers\, and rabbis\, the authors clearly relish the richness
  of their topic.
LAST-MODIFIED:20160630T050256Z
LOCATION:Rabin Family Library
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:CBS Book Club
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20170723T160000Z
DTEND:20170723T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:sd045d4k3v969t40qos4dbmghs@google.com
CREATED:20170315T051200Z
DESCRIPTION:Have fun while helping the feed the hungry! Join other members 
 of the CBS community to “do Jewish” at the SF-Marin Food Bank! \n\nWe will 
 sort\, inspect\, and repackage thousands of pounds of food during a short\,
  2-hour shift. This is an all-ages event\; kids ages 4 and up with parents 
 are welcome to participate. The work is not super strenuous\, but it is sup
 er fun...and it's a wonderful way to introduce children to "doing Jewish."\
 n\nAll are welcome\, but advance registration is required. If you are inter
 ested in participating or have questions\, please email congregant Katherin
 e Hollander (khollander [at] friedmanspring [dot] com).\n\nCan’t do July 23
 ? Participate now by helping Beth Sholom fill its Food Bank donation barrel
  with non-perishable food items (especially peanut butter\, pasta\, canned 
 beans and tuna). The barrel is located in the entry plaza on the back wall 
 near the kitchen.
LAST-MODIFIED:20170616T060050Z
LOCATION:San Francisco and Marin Food Bank\, 900 Pennsylvania Ave\, San Fra
