UID:mngbrn9hhs6j8kl8mlj30ethqk@google.com
CREATED:20161212T225015Z
DESCRIPTION:We are thrilled to launch a Jewish historical fiction book club
  for 4-5th graders. Our plan is for the group to meet 2-3 times per year. \
 n\nThe book: "Secrets in the House of Delgado\," by Gloria Miklowitz\nIn Sp
 ain in 1492\, fourteen-year-old Maria\, a Catholic orphan\, becomes a serva
 nt to a wealthy family of Conversos\, converted Jews\, at a time when the J
 ews are being expelled from the country and when the Inquisition is diligen
 tly searching for religious heretics.\n\nThe book is available at the Jewis
 h Community Library\, San Francisco Public Library\, or purchase the book o
 n-line or check if your  local book store has it or can order it for you. \
 n\nMeets immediately after Shabbat School in the CBS Boardroom. The discuss
 ion will be facilitated by CBS congregant and Jewish Community Library Dire
 ctor Howard Freedman. Dinner will be served. \n\nRegistration: please email
  Elin Cohen elincohen@hotmail.com if you want your child to participate. Th
 e cost ( preferably paid via PayPal) is $10 to cover the cost of the dinner
 . \n\n\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20161212T225015Z
LOCATION:Boardroom
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:CBS Book Club For Kids (Grades 4–5)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
