DTEND:20170921T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:juibr7mlp59s3ue4k5migqcdlg@google.com
CREATED:20170626T211758Z
DESCRIPTION:Shaliach tzibbur (prayer leader)\, musician\, and teacher Aviva
  Chernick returns again to CBS to lead "Renew Our Days: The High Holy Days 
 Unbound\," a special\, two-part service occurring on the mornings of Rosh H
 ashanah Day 1 and Yom Kippur. \n\n"Renew Our Days" is a prayer lab\, a non-
 halachic service (e.g.\, there is no Torah service) inspired by traditional
  liturgy\, but not bound to it. The service continues to evolve from last y
 ear’s initial iteration\; it will move a bit further from a traditional str
 ucture\, letting go of more of the text and incorporating more contemplativ
 e and embodied practice.\n\nHighlighting selected passages and prayers\, Av
 iva will guide participants on a journey\, an opportunity to rediscover and
  reconnect with the spiritual\, emotional\, and intellectual substance of J
 ewish prayer and the High Holy Days. “With curiosity and an openness to dis
 cover the experience of prayer anew\,” Aviva says\, “so much is possible.”\
 n\nJoin us in song\, prayer\, and reflection as we experience the Days of A
 we in a fresh and inspiring way.\n\nR.S.V.P. by visiting the CBS website an
 d following the registration instructions you’ll find there. After you have
  registered\, you will be emailed a link to music files that will introduce
  you to some of the "Renew Our Days" melodies.\n\n"Renew Our Days" is open 
 to all CBS High Holy Day ticket holders\, but space is limited. Please plan
  to join us promptly at 10 a.m. The service will end at approximately 1 p.m
 .\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20170627T170003Z
LOCATION:Gronowski Family Chapel
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:"Renew Our Days" (w/ Aviva Chernick)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
