UID:2v9n8eo3rr490scb6ft58rm0fm@google.com
CREATED:20180426T195919Z
DESCRIPTION:Meditation will begin at 8 p.m. \nMa’ariv and Eicha will begin 
 at 9:09 p.m. \n\nJoin Congregation Beth Sholom and Makor Or - along with No
 rman Fischer and Rabbi Dan Ain - for an evening that challenges us to enter
  into the meaning of this holy day - and the fragile sacredness of life - t
 hrough meditation\, silence and hearing the haunting cries from the Book of
  Lamentations.\n\nThe Ninth of Av (Tisha b’Av) is a solemn date on the Hebr
 ew calendar\, marking the destruction of both Temples in Jerusalem and the 
 loss of an ancient and sacred civilization.\nIn an era when many people cit
 e "feeling good" as the goal of their spiritual practice\, this lesser know
 n fast day insists that light can not be fully appreciated without an aware
 ness of the darkness.\n\nAll Welcome. This is a no charge event.\nEmail: in
 fo@bethsholomsf.org for more information.
LAST-MODIFIED:20180713T195704Z
LOCATION:Congregation Beth Sholom\, 301 14th Ave\, San Francisco\, CA 94118
 \, USA
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Tisha B'Av Meditation w/ Makor Or
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
