DTEND:20170226T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:lne29p3vnp8pvf3fsl445c50ao@google.com
CREATED:20170123T175711Z
DESCRIPTION:The CBS Book Club will meet in the Rabin Library. The book to b
 e discussed is: "Dogs Of God: Columbus\, the Inquisition\, and the Defeat o
 f the Moors\," by James Reston\, Jr.\n\nA riveting account of the pivotal e
 vents of 1492\, when towering political ambitions\, horrific religious exce
 sses\, and a drive toward international conquest changed the world forever.
  James Reston\, Jr.\, brings to life the epic story of Spain’s effort to co
 nsolidate its own burgeoning power by throwing off the yoke of the Vatican.
  By waging war on the remaining Moors in Granada and unleashing the Inquisi
 tor Torquemada on Spain’s Jewish and converso population\, King Ferdinand a
 nd Queen Isabella attained enough power and wealth to fund Columbus’ expedi
 tion to America and to chart a Spanish destiny separate from that of Italy.
  With rich characterizations of the central players\, this engrossing narra
 tive captures all the political and religious ferment of this crucial momen
 t on the eve of the discovery of the New World.\n\nThe book is available th
 rough the SF Public Library (and Link+)\, Amazon and is available in Kindle
  e-book format.  (Please be aware that there are other books by other autho
 rs on completely different subjects with similar\, if not the exact title.)
LAST-MODIFIED:20170217T222529Z
LOCATION:Rabin Family Library
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:CBS Book Club
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
