DESCRIPTION:<style type="text/css">p.p1 {margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px\; 
 font: 14.0px Tahoma\; color: #2b4042\; -webkit-text-stroke: #2b4042}span.s1
  {font-kerning: none}</style><p class="p1"><span class="s1"><b><i>'Why do Y
 ou hide Your face?': Questioning God in the Psalms</i>:&nbsp\;</b>An overvi
 ew of select Psalms that explore suffering and injustice with attention to 
 the roles that humans and God each play in causing and alleviating these ex
 istential difficulties.</span></p><p class="p1"><span class="s1"><br></span
 ></p><p class="p1">CBS Welcomes Visiting Scholar\,&nbsp\;<span style="-webk
 it-text-stroke-width: initial\;">Professor Joel Kaminsky</span></p><p class
 ="p1">Dr. Kaminsky is the Morningstar Professor of Jewish Studies at Smith 
 College where he teaches courses on the Hebrew Bible and Judaism.</p><p cla
 ss="p1"><br></p><p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span></p><p class="p1">Dr.
  Kaminsky has held appointments at St. Olaf College\, Muhlenberg College\, 
 Whitman College\, and Loyola University of Chicago. He has been a visiting 
 professor at Duke Divinity School\, Harvard Divinity School\, and Yale Divi
 nity School and has authored or collaborated on eight books.</p>
