DESCRIPTION:Critic Liel Leibovitz recently wrote in the NY Jewish Week abou
 t the significance of the individual as an instrument in both art and relig
 ion\, yet he laments that "it is no longer common in contemporary art for t
 he two to intersect."\n\nJoin us this Kabbalat Shabbat for an alternative p
 rayer experience led by Dr. Elyssa Wortzman. We will mindfully connect art\
 , ritual\, and prayer as participants in an interactive project called 22\,
  based on the the Kabbalistic concept of transmutation of Hebrew letters. (
 No Hebrew required\, and participation meets halachic standards for Shabbat
 .)
LAST-MODIFIED:20180222T231511Z
LOCATION:Gronowski Family Chapel
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Kabbalat Shabbat Services (w/ Dr. Elyssa Wortzman)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
