CREATED:20180201T201236Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>The Book Club For Teens in Grades 7 – 9</b> is back with <b>
 <i>Starglass</i></b>\, a futuristic\, outer space thriller. Join us on <b>S
 unday\, March 11\, 5:30 – 7 p.m. at Sabina's house in the Sunset District</
 b> for dinner and a book discussion facilitated by Howard Freedman\, Direct
 or of the Jewish Community Library AND a conversation and Q &amp\; A via Sk
 ype with the author Phoebe North.<br><br>If you're interested in signing yo
 ur teen up\, please RSVP to Elin:&nbsp\;elinjcohen [at] gmail [dot] com<br>
 <br><b>Note there is a $10 fee to cover dinner charges.</b> The book is ava
 ilable at the Jewish Community Library\, or purchase a copy from your local
  book store or online.<br><br>So what's <i>Starglass</i> about? Humanity wa
 s given five years to prepare when they learned that an asteroid would dest
 roy Earth. The healthiest humans were sent away from Earth\, flying in ever
 y direction in the hopes that the human race could survive by finding a new
  home. The rest of our species is left to wait. Nearly 500 years have passe
 d since the asteroid arrived\, and the only home that Terra has ever known 
 is on the Asherah\, a massive spaceship ferrying roughly 1\,000 Jewish sett
 lers to their new planet. But after 16-year-old Terra witnesses the Captain
 ’s guard murder an innocent man\, she’s drawn into a secret rebellion bent 
 on restoring power to the people. The stakes are higher than anything she c
 ould have imagined. When the rebellion gives Terra an all-important mission
 \, she has to decide where her loyalties lie for once and for all.
LAST-MODIFIED:20180215T214003Z
LOCATION:See below (Off-site)
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Book Club For Teens (Grades 7 – 9)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
