UID:k1ecso384tss19964841hsl9ug@google.com
CREATED:20160914T184551Z
DESCRIPTION:Zion(ism) Matters\n"On Love Of Israel"\nNovember 10\, December 
 15\, January 26\, & February 23\n(4 sessions w/ Ephraim Margolin\, Esq.)\n\
 nRegistration: https://www.universe.com/cbsthinkingmatters\n\nCourse Descri
 ption: Ephraim Margolin is a longtime professor of law who\, before moving 
 to the United States\, served as Secretary to Menachem Begin\, leader of th
 e IRGUN. He is a Hebrew University and Yale Law School graduate who has a r
 ich knowledge of Israeli politics and culture. This four-session mini-cours
 e will consider Israel through a contemporary lens\, drawing on the country
 ’s remarkable history and much Jewish thinking. Session 1: "Limits On Criti
 cism of Israel"\; Session 2: "Glorifying & Rejecting Jewish Power"\; Sessio
 n 3: "Academic Take On Nationalism & Bi-Nationalism"\; Session 4: "Self-Hat
 e In Modern Israeli Culture."\n\n\nReadings: TBD\n\nAll sessions are FREE f
 or CBS members\, but students are encouraged to make a donation to CBS. For
  nonmembers\, each single session is $12. Alternatively\, nonmembers can pu
 rchase an 8-session pack for $84\, or the full semester subscription for $1
 80.
LAST-MODIFIED:20170106T005530Z
LOCATION:Board Room
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Zion(ism) Matters
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
