DESCRIPTION:<span>Please join us to celebrate the publication of CBS member
 \,&nbsp\;</span><strong>Mark Gunther's</strong><span>&nbsp\;novel of grief 
 and recovery\,&nbsp\;</span><em>Without Jenny.&nbsp\;</em><span>We’ll sip a
 nd schmooze and Mark will&nbsp\;speak&nbsp\;about the novel and his own exp
 erience as a bereaved father. He will read selected excerpts and do a book 
 signing.</span><br><br><span><em>Without Jenny</em><span>&nbsp\;is based in
  San Francisco. It&nbsp\;chronicles a Jewish family's experiences after the
  sudden\, accidental death of ten-year-old Jenny\, their oldest.&nbsp\;An e
 motional story told with honest and haunting detail\, the novel is an intim
 ate portrait of two people in a loving marriage that gets stretched to the 
 breaking point by the unspeakable.</span></span><span><span><br></span></sp
 an><br><span><span><span><span><strong>DATE:</strong>&nbsp\;Sunday\, April 
 29<br><strong>TIME:&nbsp\;</strong>4&nbsp\;p.m.<br><strong>PLACE:&nbsp\;</s
 trong>Gronowski Family Chapel</span></span><span></span><p><span><span>The 
 book will be on sale for $20\, with $5 going to Beth Sholom’s grief support
  efforts.</span></span></p></span></span>
LAST-MODIFIED:20180419T210735Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Book Reading: Without Jenny
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
