UID:03akuhlrs1ktsal2eu37pst6i4@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20181006T090000
CREATED:20181003T175332Z
DESCRIPTION:Following Shabbat Morning Services\, we conclude with Kiddush l
 unch at noon\, with the entire CBS community.\n\nCBS Shabbat School strives
  to:\n*Support parents in the mitzvah of teaching our children.\n*Teach mid
 dot (Jewish values) through Torah study\, personal reflection\, and acts of
  Tikkun Olam.\n*Create powerful Shabbat and holiday experiences with the gr
 eater CBS community.\n*Teach our children to pray as Jews.\n*Cultivate an a
 wareness of God in nature and in human relationships.\n*Provide the tools t
 o lead an engaged Jewish life in our modern world.
LAST-MODIFIED:20181003T181110Z
LOCATION:CBS
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:FIRST Shabbat School (Kindergarten - Grade 6)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20170820T163000Z
DTEND:20170820T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:4ppl690voc91vm5lvtlkdknq60@google.com
CREATED:20170724T034907Z
DESCRIPTION:The CBS Book Club will meet in the Rabin Library.\n\nThe book t
 o be discussed is "Here I Am\," by Jonathan Safron Foer. Showcasing the sam
 e high-energy inventiveness\, hilarious irreverence\, and emotional urgency
  that readers loved in his earlier work\, "Here I Am" is Foer’s most search
 ing\, hard-hitting\, and grandly entertaining novel yet. How do we fulfill 
 our conflicting duties as father\, husband\, and son\; wife and mother\; ch
 ild and adult? Jew and American? How can we claim our own identities when o
 ur lives are linked so closely to others’? These are the questions at the h
 eart of Jonathan Safran Foer’s first novel in eleven years―a work of extrao
 rdinary scope and heartbreaking intimacy.\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20170726T192212Z
LOCATION:Rabin Family Library
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:CBS Book Club
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
