DESCRIPTION:Our engaging\, university-accredited Intro To Judaism course is
  interactive and encourages questions\, discussion\, and hands-on learning.
  No knowledge of Hebrew is required\, but you will learn to read the langua
 ge as part of the class. Wherever you find yourself on your Jewish journey\
 , join us to enrich your understanding of Judaism and deepen your connectio
 n to Jewish heritage and tradition.\n\nCo-taught by Rabbi Dan Ain and CBS R
 abbinic Intern\, Amanda Russell.\n\n$400 – Single\, $600 – Couple -- 50% di
 scount for members\n8 classes (Oct-May) + 1 private session with Rabbi Ain\
 n\nTo learn more\, to ask questions\, or to enroll contact Amanda Russell: 
 arussell@bethsholomsf.org\n\nThis class is taught once-a-month on the 2nd T
 hursday evening of the month. Classes resume in Fall 2018.\n\nDates include
 : \nOct. 11 \nNov. 8 \nDec. 13 \nJan. 10 \nFeb. 7 \nMar. 7 \nApr. 11 \nMay 
 9 \n*dates may be subject to change
LAST-MODIFIED:20180928T033843Z
LOCATION:Board Room 
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Canceled: Introduction to Judaism
TRANSP:OPAQUE
