UID:r8qommp9jcb2l3eeiop9bkjfec@google.com
CREATED:20170103T044303Z
DESCRIPTION:The CBS Book Club will meet in the Rabin Library. The book to b
 e discussed is: "The Seven Good Years\," by Etgar Keret.\n\nThis is a memoi
 r by the Israeli author of "Suddenly a Knock on the Door." It chronicles hi
 s life between the birth of his son and the death of his father. Like his s
 hort stories\, the memoir is short\, only 177 pages\, thoroughly entertaini
 ng\, and challenges readers to rack their brains to discover and uncover th
 e underlying moral\, social\, and/or political commentary that maybe or may
  not be there. Unlike his short stories which occur in fantastic surreality
 \, his memoir takes place in the surreality\, as he sees it\, of life in Is
 rael.   \n\nThe book is readily available in print\, e-book and audio versi
 ons.  The SF Public Library has a copies in all formats (physical\, e-books
  and audio).
LAST-MODIFIED:20170103T044327Z
LOCATION:Rabin Family Library
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:CBS Book Club
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
