UID:5cu1m6ssep657ftbimicp5v70f@google.com
CREATED:20190730T174828Z
DESCRIPTION:Tisha B'Av at Congregation Beth Sholom\n\n\n"Rabbi Lew z"l wrot
 e: Tisha B'Av commemorates the fall of the first and second Temples in Jeru
 salem and\, by extension the whole gamut of disasters that have befallen th
 e Jewish people. Tisha B'Av is not about victimization. Both as individuals
  and as a people\, we are called by Tisha B'Av to acknowledge the dark side
  of our existence and to take responsibility for it as well.\n\nAs such\, i
 t makes an excellent starting point for our High holidays preparations\, Ti
 sha B'Av is about our estrangement from God\, from ourselves and from other
 s. Rosh Hashanah and Yom Kippur\, which begin exactly seven weeks after Tis
 ha B' Av\, are about reconciliation\, atonement and teshuvah. On the deepes
 t level\, Tisha B'Av and the High Holidays are part of the same process. [R
 .Lew z"l 7/2004 Cong. Beth Sholom newsletter.]"\n\nSaturday\, August 10:\n\
 n\n9:00 a.m. - 12:00 p.m.  |  Shabbat morning services in the Sanctuary\n11
 :15 a.m. - 12:00 p.m.  |  Tot Shabbat in GFC\n12:00 p.m. - 1:15 p.m.  |  Co
 mmunity Kiddush in Koret Hall\n1:45 p.m. - 2:30 p.m.  |  Shabbat Mincha Min
 yan in GFC\n8:00 a.m. - 9:00 p.m.  | Makor Or Meditation in Makom Shalom\n8
 :00 a.m. - 9:00 p.m.  | Tisha B'Av Shiur led by Marilyn Heiss in Board Room
  \n9:00 a.m. - 10:30 pm  |  Book of Lamentations and Ma'ariv service in GFC
 \n\n\nSunday\, August 11:\n\n8:00 a.m. - 10:00 a.m.  |  Minyan in GFC\n10:0
 0 a.m. - 5:00 p.m.  |  Makor Or Silent Retreat in Makom Shalom\n1:45 p.m. -
  2:30 p.m.  |  Tisha B'Av Mincha Minyan in GFC\n\n*please note Mincha servi
 ce moved to 1:45pm
LAST-MODIFIED:20190805T194806Z
LOCATION:Makom Shalom 
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Tisha B'Av Meditation with Makor or 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
