UID:3rspasg4bcghbee4kvq7mnmv1q@google.com
CREATED:20181130T040037Z
DESCRIPTION:Kabbalat Shabbat Service\nSING on the second Friday of each mon
 th\nShiru L’Adonai shir hadash – Sing out to God\, a new song.\n\nHow can w
 e take the routine liturgy that we know so well and make it new time and ti
 me again? One way by singing out loud!\nJoin Amanda Russell\, CBS rabbinica
 l intern and musical director\, Jonathan Bayer\, for a musical Shabbat expe
 rience\, which will combine old and new tunes from different places around 
 the world. We will use the music as a vehicle to prayer\, grounding us wher
 e we feel comfortable and allowing us to deepen our prayer with melodies mo
 re unfamiliar to us.\nAmanda Russell is in her final year of Rabbinical Sch
 ool at The Ziegler School of Rabbinic Studies in Los Angeles\, and has serv
 ed as the Rabbinic Intern at CBS for three years. Many of you know her as t
 he shlikhat tzibur (prayer leader) on Shabbat and holidays at CBS\, as she 
 strives to infuse our prayer life with music and song. She and her husband 
 David Katz\, look forward to another year together with the CBS community.\
 n\nJonathan Bayer of San Francisco is a singer\, instrumentalist and Jewish
  educator. You may know him as the Music Specialist at CBS and he is an ass
 et to our musical team. His contributions in the Preschool\, Shabbat School
  program and other Shabbat services are unmatched and he looks forward to a
 nother year with the CBS team and exploring new ways to pray and make music
  together.
LAST-MODIFIED:20190801T205524Z
LOCATION:Gronowski Family Chapel
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Kabbalat Shabbat Services - SING
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
