UID:41vf2revt8g7qf9toq6hccbgmd@google.com
CREATED:20190830T204911Z
DESCRIPTION:\nThese holy days include what has made this time of year speci
 al at Congregation Beth Sholom\, and also new offerings that expand opportu
 nities for celebration\, reflection\, and discovery. From the familiar styl
 e of our Sanctuary service\, to the meditative traditions founded at our sy
 nagogue\, to musical exploration picking up on the popularity of this year’
 s LISTEN Kabbalat Shabbat services\, everyone will find an accessible and m
 eaningful way to connect to each other and to the awesome power that calls 
 us each year through the blast of the shofar.\n\nROSH HASHANAH DAY 1 SCHEDU
 LE:\n8:30 a.m. - 11 a.m.     Traditional Morning Service (Sanctuary)\n8:30 
 a.m. - 11 a.m.     Musical Alternative Morning Service (Koret Hall)\n10 a.m
 . - 11 a.m.         Meditation\, Singing and Reflection (Makom Sholom)\n10 
 a.m. - 11 a.m.         Family Service (Newborns - Age 5\; Gronowski Family 
 Chapel)\n10 a.m. - 2 p.m.          Camp Beth Sholom (Newborns - Age 5\; Pre
 school Building)\n10 a.m. - 2 p.m.          Camp Beth Sholom (Kindergarten 
 - Grade 5\; School Building)\n11 a.m. - 2 p.m.           Shofar Service and
  Sermon (Sanctuary)\n11 a.m. - 12:30 p.m.   Camp Beth Sholom (Grades 6-12\;
  Youth Lounge)\n12 p.m. - 1:30 p.m.     Traditional Musaf afternoon service
  (Sanctuary)\n12 p.m. - 1:30 p.m.     Alternative afternoon service (Koret 
 Hall)\n12 p.m. - 1:30 p.m.     Afternoon meditation (Makom Shalom)\n3 p.m. 
 - 4 p.m.            Mincha Gedolah (Sanctuary)\n4 p.m.                     
        Tashlich (Meet near Front Entrance)\n\nLunch boxes will be distribut
 ed at 12:30 p.m. and we hope everybody will enjoy them on our Eva Gunther P
 laza\, and share the holiday spirit with each other.\n\n For more informati
 on on our services this year please visit our website at https://www.bethsh
 olomsf.org/highholydays
LAST-MODIFIED:20190830T210636Z
LOCATION:Sanctuary\, Koret\, Makom Shalom\, Gronowski Family Chapel\, Presc
 hool Building\, School Building\, Youth Lounge
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Rosh Hashanah Day 1
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
