CREATED:20200110T200631Z
DESCRIPTION:Glide Memorial Church in the Tenderloin serves 2000 meals a day
 \, 365 days a year to the homeless and those who are food insecure. We rese
 rve 20 spaces for CBS members\, ages 6-106\, to help serve lunch (11 a.m. –
  1 p.m.)\, each month. Check the CBS website for dates and to reserve your 
 spot.\n\nLast year\, a group of 10 Beth Sholom families participated in a p
 ilot project at Glide\, learning with Rabbi Michael Lezak\, Glide Community
  Rabbi\, about the Tenderloin community through a Jewish lens and volunteer
 ing on a monthly basis. Now we’re extending this mitzvah opportunity to you
 !\nPlease join us for this important work taking our Jewish values of justi
 ce and righteousness outside the CBS. \n\nPrice: Free\nLocation: Glide Memo
 rial Church \nTimes: 11 a.m. - 1 p.m.\, Sundays\nUpcoming Dates: April 12\,
  May 3\, June 7\nFor more information about volunteering to serve meals\, c
 ontact: Dawne Bear Novicoff dbnovicoff@gmail.com or Becky Buckwald beckybuc
 kwald@gmail.com
LAST-MODIFIED:20200110T200631Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Serve Sunday Lunch at Glide
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
