UID:354b1gqjpdd14fr26dnpuq689h@google.com
CREATED:20191030T172037Z
DESCRIPTION:Jonathan is Saul's son - David is Saul's "frenemy" - Jonathan i
 s David's friend. Sounds like a formula for trouble\, doesn't it? Join us a
 s we unpack the love/hate relationship between all three\, learning about e
 mpowerment\, loyalty\, and devotion when pushed to the extreme. This course
  continues where last year’s Saturday morning classes with Evan left off - 
 about halfway through their epic tale. Join us as things continue to heat u
 p. Participation last year is not a prerequisite.<br><br>Price: Public $540
  | CBS Members $108<br>Location: Beit Midrash (Library)<br>Time: Saturdays\
 , 9:45-11 a.m.<br>Dates: January 25\, February 22\, 29\, April 4\, 25\, May
  2<br><br>Evan Wolkenstein holds a Masters in Jewish Education from Hebrew 
 University and a Certificate of Jewish Studies from Machon Pardes. He has t
 aught in the classroom for 16 years\, and serves as Director of Experientia
 l Education and Tanach teacher on the Jewish Studies faculty of The Jewish 
 Community High School of the Bay (JCHS) in San Francisco. Evan has develope
 d curricula in Classic Jewish Texts’ intersection with Human Relationships\
 , Psychology\, and Literary Analysis. In addition\, Evan has advised at Bim
 Bam\, mentors teachers in pedagogy\, classroom management\, and educational
  technology\, and writes two blogs:  magnetiCClassroom.com on the intersect
 ion of tech\, education\, and interpersonal relationships\, and StyleForDor
 ks.com. His first novel has been picked up by Random House and is due to be
  published next year.<br><br><a href="https://bethsholomsf.secure.nonprofit
 soapbox.com/lovetriangle1" id="ow1705" __is_owner="true">Register for this 
 class</a>!
LAST-MODIFIED:20200109T224531Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:The Love Triangle: Jonathan\, David\, & Saul (Shabbat Morning Study
 ) with Evan Wolkenstein
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
