DESCRIPTION:\nDAVEN - on the first Friday of each month\n\n\nFor 500 years\
 , Jews have used the Kabbalat Shabbat service to\nmake a transition from bu
 sy weekdays to the calm spaciousness\nof Shabbat. In the DAVEN service\, we
  will explore the Hebrew\nliturgy\, using niggun (wordless melody)\, chant\
 , song\, and silence\nto engage this joyous tradition with our friends and 
 families.\n\nDavid Malman has been a CBS member since 1998. He has led\nSha
 bbat\, daily minyan\, and High Holy Days services. He is an\nactive partici
 pant in Makor Or\, the meditation group started by\nRabbi Alan Lew (z”l). D
 avid and his wife Ellen Shireman taught\na successful Learner’s Minyan for 
 several years\, and he attended\nJoey Weisenberg’s “Building Singing Commun
 ities” multi-day\nworkshops in 2013 and 2014. He is honored and pleased to 
 be\nwelcoming Shabbat with the CBS community.
LAST-MODIFIED:20190613T210449Z
LOCATION:Gronowski Family Chapel
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Kabbalat Shabbat Services - DAVEN
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
