UID:2ojgkfuiq93m0m2oedrm3tbtlc@google.com
CREATED:20200203T045214Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Nostalgia\, a wishful affection or sentimental longing for a
  past that cannot be recovered\, is a powerful theme in American Jewish rel
 igion and culture that is communicated through what American Jews make\, bu
 y\, and sell. </p><p>Join Dr. Rachel B. Gross\, the John and Marcia Goldman
  Chair in American Jewish Studies at San Francisco State University\, for a
  Bimah Dialogue with Rabbi Dan Ain. Together they will discuss Dr. Gross's 
 research on how contemporary American Jews use nostalgia to create religiou
 s communities.&nbsp\;</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20200203T045214Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Bimah Dialogue with Rachel B. Gross
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
