UID:7591tp5ko53dkqbqhak4g8car1@google.com
CREATED:20190912T004513Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Shabbat services on September 21 for a special bimah
  dialogue between Rabbi Dan Ain and Rabbi Michael Lezak\, Staff Rabbi of Me
 morial United Methodist Church in the Tenderloin (though he considers himse
 lf more of a shaliach from the Jewish community). At Glide\, Rabbi Lezak ha
 s launched some inspiring new initiatives\, from challah baking in Glide’s 
 kitchen to a joint trip of Jewish community members and Glide staff to visi
 t the National Memorial for Peace and Justice in Alabama\, which commemorat
 es African American victims of lynching.&nbsp\;<br><br><br>In the past year
  a group of 10 Beth Sholom families participated in a pilot project at Glid
 e\, learning with Rabbi Lezak about the Tenderloin community through a Jewi
 sh lens and volunteering on a monthly basis\, serving lunch at Glide’s meal
  program. As a kehilla kedosha (holy community)\, complementing the Chicken
  Soupers and Schenina work at CBS\, we will be organizing a group volunteer
  opportunity one Sunday per month at Glide. Stay tuned for more details and
  instructions to sign up.&nbsp\;<br>&nbsp\;<br>For more about Rabbi Lezak a
 nd Glide\, see this wonderful profile in <a href="https://www.tabletmag.com
 /jewish-life-and-religion/281444/the-rabbi-and-his-church">Tablet Magazine<
 /a>. We hope to see you on the 21st to learn more about social justice work
  at Glide\, and how you can get involved through Beth Sholom’s new Chesed V
 a-Tzedek group.<br><br>DATE: Saturday\, September 21<br>TIME: 9 a.m.<br>PLA
 CE: Sanctuary
LAST-MODIFIED:20190912T011244Z
LOCATION:Sanctuary
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Bimah Dialogue with Rabbi Michael Lezak of Glide
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
