DESCRIPTION:\nRabbi Ain will provide pre-B’nai Mitzvah students with the op
 portunity to study and interpret Torah alongside him and their peers while 
 also learning from specialists and artists. \nNoa Bar will continue the lea
 rning as they dive deep and explore the balance between the nature of fixed
  and routine prayer (kevah) with the prayer that is intentional or spontane
 ous (kavanah) and how that fits into their modern lives today. \n\nStudents
  will meet on Thursday evenings with Rabbi Ain and Noa Bar approximately th
 ree times each month starting with minyan at 6:00 pm and dinner at 6:30 pm.
  The evening concludes at 8:00 pm.\n\nOctober 18 and 25\nNovember 1\, 8\, a
 nd 15\nDecember 13\nJanuary 10\, 17\, and 24\nFebruary 7\, 14\, and 28\nMar
 ch 7\, 14\, and 28\nApril 11 and 18\nMay 2\, 9\, and 16
