BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20200301T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20200301T200000
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:mles0p980pcj9tg5ud4k78igr9@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20200301T183000
CREATED:20191030T170653Z
DESCRIPTION:Nostalgia\, a sentimental longing for a past that cannot be rec
 overed\, is a powerful theme in American Jewish religion and culture that i
 s communicated through what American Jews make\, buy\, and sell. This cours
 e will examine how American Jews tell stories about Ashkenazi Jews' immigra
 tion to the United States at the turn of the twentieth century\, and how th
 ey connect to it emotionally and physically through Jewish genealogy\, visi
 ting historic synagogues\, buying children's books and dolls\, and eating o
 ut at restaurants reimagining Ashkenazi cuisine. Through these institutiona
 l and commercial activities and others\, contemporary American Jews express
  their longing for authentic Jewish pasts\, build community in the present\
 , and pass on their values to future generations. Dr. Gross will discuss hi
 storic synagogues\, children's books and dolls\, and the Jewish deli reviva
 l\, among other topics.    \n\nPrice: Public $180 | CBS Members $36\nTime: 
 Sundays\, 6:30 p.m.\nDates:  March 1\, 8  and 15\n\nRachel B. Gross is the 
 John and Marcia Goldman Professor of American Jewish Studies in the Departm
 ent of Jewish Studies at San Francisco State University. \nHer manuscript\,
  Feeling Jewish: Nostalgia and American Jewish Religion\, examines how cont
 emporary American Jews use nostalgia to create religious communities. She r
 eceived her Ph.D. in Religion from Princeton University.
LAST-MODIFIED:20200228T212358Z
LOCATION:Board Room
SEQUENCE:4
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:The Good Old Days: Creating American Jewish Nostalgia with Rachel G
 ross
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20200409T010000Z
DTEND:20200409T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:3ktb9qurq4qm6m1ipghcg58hlu@google.com
CREATED:20200401T223717Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Seder is the Hebrew word for Order.&nbsp\;While we shelter i
 n place\, socially distance\, distance learn and wear pajamas for days – ca
 n we find order in the disorder? Can we celebrate freedom as our lives feel
  more and more confined and constricted each day?&nbsp\;This fun-filled\, i
 nteractive\, hopefully&nbsp\;engaging Seder will provide the framework\, as
  we strive to answer these questions\, and many more.</p><p>Geared for fami
 lies with elementary school-aged children\,&nbsp\;and community members wit
 h a curious mind\, heart and soul.</p><p>Register:&nbsp\;https://www.eventb
 rite.com/e/the-curious-kid-shelter-in-place-seder-tickets-101472703588?ref=
 elink&nbsp\;</p><p>Zoom Link: <a href="https://ucsf.zoom.us/j/7167803882">h
 ttps://ucsf.zoom.us/j/7167803882</a></p><p>Meeting ID: 716-780-3882  |  Cal
 l-in: (669)-900-6833</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20200403T171515Z
LOCATION:https://ucsf.zoom.us/j/7167803882
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:The Curious Kid Shelter in Place Seder
TRANSP:OPAQUE
