CREATED:20190830T205727Z
DESCRIPTION:These holy days include what has made this time of year special
  at Congregation Beth Sholom\, and also new offerings that expand opportuni
 ties for celebration\, reflection\, and discovery. From the familiar style 
 of our Sanctuary service\, to the meditative traditions founded at our syna
 gogue\, to musical exploration picking up on the popularity of this year’s 
 LISTEN Kabbalat Shabbat services\, everyone will find an accessible and mea
 ningful way to connect to each other and to the awesome power that calls us
  each year through the blast of the shofar. <br><br>ROSH HASHANAH DAY 2 SCH
 EDULE:<br>8:30 a.m. - 10 a.m.    Traditional Morning Service (Sanctuary)<br
 >10 a.m. - 11 a.m.          Morning Torah Service (Sanctuary)<br>10 a.m. - 
 1:30 p.m.      Camp Beth Sholom (Newborns - Age 5\; Preschool Building)<br>
 10 a.m. - 1:30 p.m.      Camp Beth Sholom (Kindergarten - Grade 5\; School 
 Building)<br>11 a.m. - 12 p.m.           Shofar Service and Sermon (Sanctua
 ry)<br>11 a.m. - 12:30 p.m.     Camp Beth Sholom (Grades 6-12\; Youth Loung
 e)<br>12 p.m. - 1:30 p.m.       Musaf afternoon service (Sanctuary)<br>6 p.
 m. - 6:30 p.m.       Mincha (Gronowski Family Chapel)<br><br><br>For more i
 nformation on our Congregation\, services and schedules please visit our we
 bsite at <a href="https://www.bethsholomsf.org/highholydays">https://www.be
 thsholomsf.org/highholydays</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20190830T210757Z
LOCATION:Sanctuary\, Gronowski Family Chapel\, Preschool Building\, School 
 Building
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Rosh Hashanah Day 2
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
