UID:0hi4ptdfgm8ljp8v58pih48kv7@google.com
CREATED:20190509T223114Z
DESCRIPTION:The next meeting of the CBS Book Group will discuss "Yosl Rakov
 er Talks to God"  by Zvi Kolitz.\n\nZvi Kolitz was a Lithuanian Jew who lef
 t Europe in 1940 for Jerusalem and become a ardent Zionist freedom fighter.
  Shortly after the end of WWII\, while visiting Argentina\, he wrote a powe
 rful short story\, "Yosl Rakover Talks to God"\, the last confession of a f
 ictional Jewish man who died in the Warsaw Ghetto.\n\nThe First Vintage ver
 sion that the group will discuss includes the story of Yosl Rakover\, a man
  who refuses to abandon his faith in God\, despite the mania and chaos that
  is about to crush him\, followed by commentaries showing how fictions can 
 be knowingly and unknowingly turned into powerful truths.\n\nThis is a shor
 t book but a powerful book. The 112 pages include the short story and the e
 ssays.\n\nDATE: Sunday\, May 19\nTIME: 9:39 a.m.\nPLACE: Koret Hall\nCOST: 
 FREE\n\nFor more information\, please contact Howard Gordon at hgordon@soni
 c.net.
LAST-MODIFIED:20190513T204442Z
LOCATION:Board Room
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:CBS Book Group: 'Yosl Rakover Talks to God'
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
