CREATED:20180306T235427Z
DESCRIPTION:Kabbalat Shabbat Service\nOFFER on the fourth Friday of each mo
 nth.\nKorban Shabbat - A Sabbath of communal offerings - a loose\, free-for
 m\, Friday night experience that is Jewish in contenet and feeling.\n\nJoin
  Rabbi Ain for an alternative and communal Friday night experience\, as he 
 started in Brooklyn\, Adapted\, adoping and apporpriating styles form multi
 ple communities and perspectives\, not two Korban Shabbat evenings are the 
 same. Used colloquially to mean sacrifice\, Korban is a Heberw word whose E
 nglisgh translations have obscured its central meaning: an offering that is
  brough fro the purpose of drsing nearer to tohers and to G-d.\n\nMeeting i
 n Makom Sholom\, each Korban Shabbat  is determiend by the offerings brougt
  by those present\, including but not limited to music\, readings\, and med
 itations. If what is offered is self\, heart\, and willing engagement\, the
  gatehring will be a holy community\, one in which G-d's presence is brough
 t close.\n\nIf you are intersted in making an offering at an upcoming Korba
 n Shabbat\, we want to hear from you!
LAST-MODIFIED:20190801T220010Z
LOCATION:Gronowski Family Chapel
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Kabbalat Shabbat Services
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
