DESCRIPTION:Have you ever skipped out on Shabbat services because you feare
 d your kids would be disruptive? \n\nHave you ever looked around and wished
  there were more families during times of prayer? \n\nThis is the service f
 or you!\n\nThe youth and our families are the future! Please join us for wh
 at will be an inter-generational Shabbat service. A space where children ca
 n be themselves\, where parents can pray alongside their children and congr
 egants of all ages can feel at home.\n\nRabbi Amanda Russell joined our tea
 m full-time in July after serving as the Rabbinic Intern for four years. Sh
 e has a young family and truly appreciates the structure of a “traditional”
  Shabbat service. She is excited to explore the merging of these two Jewish
  values\, family and prayer\, into a service that will be inviting for all!
  Rabbi Russell will be joined by some of our most loved CBS staff and music
 ians.\n\nOur musicians will use instruments through Kabbalat Shabbat and we
  will pray from a family-friendly siddur.\n\nDinner will be served in advan
 ce of each service. Bring your own California grown libation to share. This
  event is free to the community but please register in advance to help us p
 repare the appropriate amount of food.\n\nL’dor V’dor...please JOIN us!\n\n
 DATE: Fourth Friday of every month\nTIME: 5:30pm dinner\, 6:00pm service\nL
 OCATION: Main Meeting Room & Gronowski Family Chapel
LAST-MODIFIED:20191011T171316Z
LOCATION:Gronowski Family Chapel
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Kabbalat Shabbat Services JOIN
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
