DTSTART:20190811T170000Z
DTEND:20190812T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:0cju0fqv71p42866c9633c77h7@google.com
CREATED:20181008T212417Z
DESCRIPTION:Makor Or: A Center for Jewish Meditation\nTisha B’Av - Seeds of
  Growth from the Ashes\n\nSunday Meditation Retreat \nAug. 11th 10am - 5pm 
 with mid-day break\nLed by: Norman Fischer and R. Dorothy Richman.\nTuition
 : $80 \nLocation: Cong. Beth Sholom meditation room\n\nTo register and rese
 rve your place:\nPlease RSVP to : makororsf@gmail.com\n\nWe will be meeting
  in August 11th\, for the observance of Tisha B’Av which commemorates the p
 ain and loss in Jewish history and our ability to acknowledge the pain and 
 move forward.  This is the beginning of our preparation for Yom Kippor and 
 our willingness to examine our lives and to prepare our hearts and souls fo
 r change.\n\nTisha B’Av is a pivotal moment in our Jewish calendar leading 
 us into deeper awareness and the possibility of transformation as we approa
 ch the High Holidays.\n\nJoin us for silent meditation\, study and chanted 
 prayer. Everyone is welcome and no experience with meditation\, Hebrew\, or
  prayer is needed.\n*******************************************************
 *******************************\nAbout Makor Or:  Founded January 1\, 2000 
 by Rabbi Alan Lew (z"l) and Norman Fischer\, the Jewish meditation practice
  of Makor Or incorporates sitting and walking meditation\, and Jewish chant
 .  Our mission is to bring the clarity and depth of meditation practice to 
 our Jewish life and observance\, to facilitate the transformation that Juda
 ism can effect in our lives.\n\nNorman Fischer is the spiritual leader of M
 akor Or.  He is also a Zen Master\, founder of Everyday Zen and a poet.  Hi
 s books include\, Opening to You Zen-Inspired translations of the Psalms\, 
 Training in Compassion Zen Teachings on the practice of LoJong\, Jerusalem 
 Moonlight and The Strugglers.\n\nRabbi Dorothy A. Richman serves as the rab
 bi of Makor Or.  She teaches at Makor Or retreats in San Francisco and lead
 s Makor Or programs in the Eastbay. She is a Master Educator leading Kevah 
 study groups\, and has served as rabbi of Berkeley Hillel\, Sha'ar Zahav an
 d Congregation Beth Sholom with her mentor Rabbi Alan Lew(z"l).
LAST-MODIFIED:20190726T215832Z
LOCATION:Makom Sholom
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Makor Or Silent Retreat
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
