DESCRIPTION:This ongoing course begins with the students and advances at th
 eir pace. The courses will introduce to prayer vocabulary and modern Hebrew
 . It is designed for those with some knowledge of Hebrew. Focus will be on 
 mastery of the past and future tenses and conversation proficiency.\n\nPric
 e: Public $540 | CBS Members $108\nLocation: Beit Midrash (Library)\nTime: 
 Tuesdays\, 4-6 p.m.\nFall: October 29\, November 5\, 12\, 19\, 26\, Decembe
 r 3\, 10\, 17\nWinter: January 8\, 15\, 22\, 29\, February 5\, 12\, 19\, 26
 \nSpring: March 18\, 25\, April 1\, 22\, May 6\, 13\, 20\, 27  \n\nYaffa Ty
 giel graduated from the Hebrew University of Jerusalem with a degree in Heb
 rew Literature and Bible Studies. She later received a Master's degree from
  Hebrew University's School of Education in Educational and Communal Admini
 stration and Early Childhood. Since that time she has served in executive a
 dministrative roles and/or taught Hebrew language and Jewish Studies in a v
 ariety of environments in Israel and the United States\, including SF Ulpan
 \, community centers\, summer camps\, synagogues\, Jewish day schools\, uni
 versities.
