DESCRIPTION:<br>These holy days include what has made this time of year spe
 cial at Congregation Beth Sholom\, and also new offerings that expand oppor
 tunities for celebration\, reflection\, and discovery. From the familiar st
 yle of our Sanctuary service\, to the meditative traditions founded at our 
 synagogue\, to musical exploration picking up on the popularity of this yea
 r’s LISTEN Kabbalat Shabbat services\, everyone will find an accessible and
  meaningful way to connect to each other and to the awesome power that call
 s us each year through the blast of the shofar. <br><br>KOL NIDRE SCHEDULE:
 <br>6:30 p.m. - 8:30 p.m.    Traditional Kol Nidre Service (Sanctuary)<br>6
 :30 p.m. - 8:30 p.m.     Camp Beth Sholom (Newborns - Age 5\; Preschool Bui
 lding)          <br>6:30 p.m. - 8:30 p.m.     Camp Beth Sholom (Kindergarte
 n - Grade 5\; School Building)<br>8:30 p.m. - 10 p.m.         Late Kol Nidr
 e Musical Service  (Koret Hall)<br><br>For more information on our services
  please visit our website at <a href="https://www.bethsholomsf.org/highholy
 days">https://www.bethsholomsf.org/highholydays</a>
