DTEND:20200222T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:62gs46ugvnasvk7dv4e3ualm0s@google.com
CREATED:20191030T172050Z
DESCRIPTION:Jonathan is Saul's son - David is Saul's "frenemy" - Jonathan i
 s David's friend. Sounds like a formula for trouble\, doesn't it? Join us a
 s we unpack the love/hate relationship between all three\, learning about e
 mpowerment\, loyalty\, and devotion when pushed to the extreme. This course
  continues where last year’s Saturday morning classes with Evan left off - 
 about halfway through their epic tale. Join us as things continue to heat u
 p. Participation last year is not a prerequisite.\n\nPrice: Public $540 | C
 BS Members $108\nLocation: Beit Midrash (Library)\nTime: Saturdays\, 9:45-1
 1 a.m.\nDates: January 25\, February 29\, April 4\, 25\, May 2 & 9\n\nEvan 
 Wolkenstein holds a Masters in Jewish Education from Hebrew University and 
 a Certificate of Jewish Studies from Machon Pardes. He has taught in the cl
 assroom for 16 years\, and serves as Director of Experiential Education and
  Tanach teacher on the Jewish Studies faculty of The Jewish Community High 
 School of the Bay (JCHS) in San Francisco. Evan has developed curricula in 
 Classic Jewish Texts’ intersection with Human Relationships\, Psychology\, 
 and Literary Analysis. In addition\, Evan has advised at BimBam\, mentors t
 eachers in pedagogy\, classroom management\, and educational technology\, a
 nd writes two blogs:  magnetiCClassroom.com on the intersection of tech\, e
 ducation\, and interpersonal relationships\, and StyleForDorks.com. His fir
 st novel has been picked up by Random House and is due to be published next
  year.
LAST-MODIFIED:20200218T211451Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:POSTPONED The Love Triangle: Jonathan\, David\, & Saul (Shabbat Mor
 ning Study) with Evan Wolkenstein
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
