DESCRIPTION:with Professor Eran Kaplan\n\nAdults: $15 | Students: Free\nEma
 il achshavyisrael@bethsholomsf.org or call 415.672.3626 to register.\n\nBib
 i Netanyahu is Israel's longest serving prime minister. He is also Israel's
  first sitting prime minister to be indicted\, charged with bribery\, breac
 h of trust and fraud. Israelis will go to the polls on March 2nd for the th
 ird time in less than a year. There is overwhelming consensus in Israel tha
 t all three election campaigns are referendums on Netanyahu. In this very t
 imely talk\, Professor Kaplan will examine Netanyahu's political and ideolo
 gical legacy as well as his current legal status and the political stalemat
 e in Israel.\n\nProfessor Kaplan\, an Israeli American\, holds the Richard 
 and Rhoda Goldman Chair of Israel Studies at San Francisco State University
 .
LAST-MODIFIED:20200224T181420Z
LOCATION:Congregation Beth Sholom\, Koret Hall
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Achshav Yisrael Presents: Netanyahu Indicted\, What's Next?
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
