BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20190222T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20190222T193000
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:dufcfnhfmp60bprbfk4d9seb5k_R20181229T023000@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20190222T183000
CREATED:20180306T235427Z
DESCRIPTION:Korban / OFFER Shabbat \n\nJoin us on the fourth Friday of each
  month for a prayerful experience that is both inspired by - and led by - m
 embers of our community. \nUsed colloquially to mean sacrifice\, Korban is 
 a Hebrew word: An offering that is brought for the purpose of drawing neare
 r to others and to G-d. \nMeeting in Makom Sholom\, each Korban Shabbat is 
 determined by the offerings brought by those present\, including but not li
 mited to music\, readings\, movement and meditations.\n\nThrough our offeri
 ngs and willing engagement\, we create a holy community\, one in which G-d'
 s presence is brought close. Korban Shabbat is an evening of sharing your o
 wn personal connections and avenues to prayer with members of this communit
 y.\n\nCommitting an offering is not required to attend. If you are interest
 ed in giving an offering\, please contact Kelsey Russom.\nPast offerings ha
 ve included song\, mediation\, poetry\, teachings - but are not limited to 
 these - Feel free to offer your own connection to prayer.\n\nWhat to Expect
 :\n*Beginners in all areas welcome / encouraged \n*Sitting on floor cushion
 s / benches: comfortable clothing \n*Geared towards grown-ups / mature teen
 s -- For Ages 16 and older \n*A safe space that is open\, respectful and co
 nducive to sharing\n\nDATE: Friday\, February 22\nTIME: Service\, 6:30 p.m.
 \, Dinner 7:30 p.m.\nPLACE: Makom Sholom\nCOST: Free! All are welcome. Brin
 g a friend!
LAST-MODIFIED:20200309T001037Z
LOCATION:Gronowski Family Chapel
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Kabbalat Shabbat Services - OFFER
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20191107T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20191107T110000
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:242qoosmpjfugsid3707m3ok7g@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20191107T093000
CREATED:20190821T182140Z
DESCRIPTION:<b><u>Ethical Fitness Kevah Group</u></b><br><br>Join us this y
 ear for learning in a intimate group setting through the Kevah Program at H
 AMAQOM|The Place. The Ethical Fitness Kevah group is looking for new learne
 rs! The group meets on Thursday mornings once a month at CBS. This year's t
 opic is Stories and Folklore: Sometimes\, as stories evolve\, so do the mes
 sages they convey and the values they teach. This is especially true of fol
 klore. Together we will look at folkloric motifs—the sleeper\, the rainmake
 r\, the impoverished princess and more-- as they appear in classic Jewish t
 exts. One of the functions of these tales is to help mediate between nostal
 gia/fantasy and the harshness of reality by offering solace and cultivating
  hope. The stories change as a result of the agenda of the teller or are th
 ey more like a centuries-long game of “telephone”?  Do the changes reflect 
 differences in context or artistic choices in the telling? And in the middl
 e of 2019\, facing harsh realities of our own\, can we find solace or hope 
 in these ancient tales? What light can these stories shed on our communal a
 nd personal ethics? Let’s find out… <br><br>This group meets on Thursdays o
 nce a month (10/3\, 11/7\, 12/5\, 1/2\, 2/6\, 3/5\, 4/2\, 5/7) 9:30-11:00 A
 M at Congregation Beth Sholom.<br><br>Contact Associate Director of HAMAQOM
 \, Tamar Zaken at tamar@hmqm.org to sign up
LAST-MODIFIED:20191203T185842Z
LOCATION:Gronowski Family Chapel
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Ethical Fitness Kevah Group
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
