UID:52pipuj56a25tintuakc0n1sar@google.com
CREATED:20190913T174559Z
DESCRIPTION:This month we're watching the film Pi.<br><a href="https://en.w
 ikipedia.org/wiki/Pi_(film)">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pi_(film)</a><br
 ><br><br><br>Max Cohen (Sean Gullette) battles migraines\, and furiously ty
 pes away on his homemade computer in his tiny NYC Chinatown apartment\, try
 ing to mathematically find the answer to life\, the universe and everything
 . Pursued by Wall Street types and messianic Hasids\, he starts showing how
  classic Jewish neuroses of alienation\, paranoia and hypochondria can expl
 ode into full blown psychosis. Shot in high-contrast black-and-white revers
 al film\, and featuring eeriness and body horror worthy of David Lynch or D
 avid Cronenberg\, this movie launched the career of director Darren Aronofs
 ky\, and features wonderful supporting performances by Mark Margolis and Be
 n Shenkman.<br><br>This series of screenings explores the work of prominent
  film directors that have pointed the camera at the American Jewish experie
 nce of which\, they themselves were a part. Rabbi Ain\, in conversation wit
 h CBS congregant and film buff Ben Chinn\, will lead a discussion following
  each movie. Film selections will include works by Joel and Ethan Coen\, Me
 l Brooks\, Mike Nichols\, and other filmmakers who have created their own J
 ewish texts out of celluloid. Dinner is included. Films may include: A Seri
 ous Man\; The Frisco Kid\; The Producers\; Zelig\; Biloxi Blues\; The Heart
 break Kid\; and more.<br><br><br>Price: Public $36/film or $180 for the ser
 ies<br>CBS Members $18/film or $108 for the series<br>Location: Koret Hall<
 br>Time: Sundays\, 6:15 p.m.<br><br><br>Future Dates:<br>February 23<br>Mar
 ch 22<br>April 19 <br>May 31
LAST-MODIFIED:20200122T200709Z
LOCATION:Congregation Beth Sholom\, 301 14th Ave\, San Francisco\, CA 94118
 \, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Pi - Dinner and a Movie: The Jewish Frame
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
