DESCRIPTION:Shabbat Mincha Shiur is back! <br><br><br>Saturday afternoons a
 re a wonderful time for a bit of study. Join Rabbi Dan Ain and Rabbi Amanda
  Russell to study modern teshuvot (Jewish legal papers) that drive the deci
 sions that we make for our Conservative synagogue communities. The Committe
 e on Jewish Law and Standards (CJLS) sets halachic (Jewish law) policy for 
 Rabbinical Assembly rabbis and for the Conservative movement as a whole.<br
 ><br><br>Rabbis in our movement have the opportunity to write <em>teshuvot<
 /em> (rabbinic responses to <em>halachah</em>) in response to a specific qu
 estion. This <em>Shiur </em>(class) will study and discuss these writings.&
 nbsp\;<br><br>These teshuvot serve to guide our movement in decision making
  in many areas of modern Jewish life. Learn the process for which these dec
 isions are made as well as the Jewish texts that support it. See the CJLS w
 ebsite for potential topics: <a href="https://www.rabbinicalassembly.org/je
 wish-law/committee-jewish-law-and-standards">https://www.rabbinicalassembly
 .org/jewish-law/committee-jewish-law-and-standards</a><br><br><br>Cost: Fre
 e
LAST-MODIFIED:20200221T184638Z
LOCATION:Congregation Beth Sholom\, Main Meeting Room
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Shabbat Mincha Shiur
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
