DESCRIPTION:\nThis series of screenings explores the work of prominent film
  directors that have pointed the camera at the American Jewish experience o
 f which\, they themselves were a part. Rabbi Ain\, in conversation with CBS
  congregant and film buff Ben Chinn\, will lead a discussion following each
  movie. Film selections will include works by Joel and Ethan Coen\, Mel Bro
 oks\, Mike Nichols\, and other filmmakers who have created their own Jewish
  texts out of celluloid. Dinner is included. Films may include: A Serious M
 an\; The Frisco Kid\; The Producers\; Zelig\; Biloxi Blues\; The Heartbreak
  Kid\; and more.  \n\n\nPrice: Public $36/film or $180 for the series\nCBS 
 Members $18/film or $108 for the series\nLocation: Koret Hall\nTime: Sunday
 s\, 6:15 p.m. (except 12/25)\nDates:\nOctober 27\nNovember 24\nDecember 25\
 ; Family-friendly movie & Chinese food\nJanuary 26\nFebruary 23\nMarch 22\n
 April 19 \nMay 31
LAST-MODIFIED:20191025T191254Z
LOCATION:Congregation Beth Sholom\, 301 14th Ave\, San Francisco\, CA 94118
 \, USA
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Dinner and a Movie: Jewish types and stereotypes in American film 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
