DTSTART:20200229T174500Z
DTEND:20200229T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:30efn4lvlg2n70q586kdv1cf2n@google.com
CREATED:20191030T172100Z
DESCRIPTION:Jonathan is Saul's son - David is Saul's "frenemy" - Jonathan i
 s David's friend. Sounds like a formula for trouble\, doesn't it? Join us a
 s we unpack the love/hate relationship between all three\, learning about e
 mpowerment\, loyalty\, and devotion when pushed to the extreme. This course
  continues where last year’s Saturday morning classes with Evan left off - 
 about halfway through their epic tale. Join us as things continue to heat u
 p. Participation last year is not a prerequisite.\n\nPrice: Public $540 | C
 BS Members $108\nLocation: Beit Midrash (Library)\nTime: Saturdays\, 9:45-1
 1 a.m.\nDates: January 25\, February 22\, 29\, April 4\, 25\, May 2\n\nEvan
  Wolkenstein holds a Masters in Jewish Education from Hebrew University and
  a Certificate of Jewish Studies from Machon Pardes. He has taught in the c
 lassroom for 16 years\, and serves as Director of Experiential Education an
 d Tanach teacher on the Jewish Studies faculty of The Jewish Community High
  School of the Bay (JCHS) in San Francisco. Evan has developed curricula in
  Classic Jewish Texts’ intersection with Human Relationships\, Psychology\,
  and Literary Analysis. In addition\, Evan has advised at BimBam\, mentors 
 teachers in pedagogy\, classroom management\, and educational technology\, 
 and writes two blogs:  magnetiCClassroom.com on the intersection of tech\, 
 education\, and interpersonal relationships\, and StyleForDorks.com. His fi
 rst novel has been picked up by Random House and is due to be published nex
 t year.
LAST-MODIFIED:20191030T172100Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:The Love Triangle: Jonathan\, David\, & Saul (Shabbat Morning Study
 ) with Evan Wolkenstein
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
