BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20190307T023000Z
DTEND:20190307T040000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055328Z
UID:0621jdmnvqr7u9e5giugmkmd9h@google.com
CREATED:20190226T012544Z
DESCRIPTION:\nDNA and the Secret of Jewish Origins\n\nA scholar of Jewish S
 tudies and Religious Studies\, Steven Weitzman serves as the Abraham M. Ell
 is Professor at the University of Pennsylvania and as the Ella Darivoff Dir
 ector of the Katz Center for Advanced Judaic Studies. His talk will draw on
  his recent book The Origin of the Jews: the Quest for Roots in a Rootless 
 Age (Princeton University Press)\, which is a recipient of a National Jewis
 h Book Award.\nThis engaging talk will last about 40 minutes\, followed by 
 a brief Q&A from the audience.\n\n\nAbout the talk: Science has discovered 
 a kind of historical archive hiding within the human cell-a trove of inform
 ation about the ancestors of present-day Jews. This talk will explore what 
 geneticists have been learning about ancient Jewish ancestry\, and why some
  scholars are very critical of this kind of research.\n\nDATE: Wednesday\, 
 March 6\nTIME: 6:30 p.m. following evening minyan\nPLACE: Gronowski Family 
 Chapel\nRSVP: Email Kelsey Russom at krussom@bethsholomsf.org
LAST-MODIFIED:20190226T012622Z
LOCATION:Gronowski Family Chapel
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:DNA and the Secret of Jewish Origins
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
