DESCRIPTION:Glide Memorial Church in the Tenderloin serves 2000 meals a day
 \, 365 days a year to the homeless and those who are food insecure. We rese
 rve 20 spaces for CBS members\, ages 6-106\, to help serve lunch (11 a.m. –
  1 p.m.)\, each month.<br><br>Last year\, a group of 10 Beth Sholom familie
 s participated in a pilot project at Glide\, learning with Rabbi Michael Le
 zak\, Glide Community Rabbi\, about the Tenderloin community through a Jewi
 sh lens and volunteering on a monthly basis. Now we’re extending this mitzv
 ah opportunity to you!<br>Please join us for this important work taking our
  Jewish values of justice and righteousness outside the CBS. <br><br>Price:
  Free<br>Location: Glide Memorial Church <br>Dates/Time: Oct 27\; Nov 10\; 
 Dec 22\; Check website for dates in 2020<br>For more information about volu
 nteering to serve meals\, contact: Dawne Bear Novicoff <a href="mailto:dbno
 vicoff@gmail.com">dbnovicoff@gmail.com</a> or Becky Buckwald <a href="mailt
 o:beckybuckwald@gmail.com">beckybuckwald@gmail.com</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20191105T224022Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Serve Sunday Lunch at Glide
