DESCRIPTION:<strong>Dinner and a Movie&nbsp\;Hanukkah Celebration</strong><
 br><strong>Hanukkah is coming and we're celebrating - especially on the fou
 rth night!</strong><br>We're taking a break from our monthly "Dinner &amp\;
  a Movie" (adult) program.<br>Please join us on Wednesday\, December 25 at 
 3 p.m. We'll watch&nbsp\;<strong><em>An American Tail</em>&nbsp\;</strong>a
 nd enjoy light dinner (Chinese noodle salad)\, latkes\, and&nbsp\;<em>suffg
 aniot&nbsp\;</em>(donuts). We'll brighten the evening with the candles on t
 he Hanukkiah.<br><br><strong>Bring your Hanukkiah to fill the room with lig
 ht!</strong>&nbsp\;<br><strong>About the family-friendly film:&nbsp\;<em>An
  American Tail</em></strong><br>Fievel is a young Russian mouse separated f
 rom his parents on the way to America\, a land they think is without cats. 
 When he arrives alone in the New World\, he keeps up hope\, searching for h
 is family\, making new friends\, and running and dodging the cats he though
 t he'd be rid off.&nbsp\;<br><br><p>This event is free to attend (with RSVP
 ) for members of Congregation Beth Sholom\, but everyone's invited!<br>Cost
  to attend is $18 for a non-member family.</p><p><strong>DATE</strong>: Wed
 nesday\, December 25<br><strong>TIME</strong>: 3 p.m.<br><strong>PLACE</str
 ong>: Koret Hall<br><strong>COST</strong>: Public $18 per family |  CBS Mem
 bers $Free</p>Tickets:&nbsp\;<a href="https://bethsholomsf.secure.nonprofit
 soapbox.com/hanukkah2019">https://bethsholomsf.secure.nonprofitsoapbox.com/
 hanukkah2019</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20191217T232913Z
LOCATION:Koret Hall
SEQUENCE:4
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Dinner\, Movie\, and No Frills Hanukkah Celebration
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
