DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20211027T210000
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:17v7fudunnol7fq71st2sakl0i@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20211027T200000
CREATED:20210924T200305Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><b>ScholarStream: Cultivating Our Relationships</b></p><p>Bi
 blical stories can inform our understanding of our own relationships. The l
 ife lessons of our ancestors influence our personal\, communal\, and world 
 values.</p><p><b>Rabbi Elliot Dorff\, “The Dysfunctional Families of Genesi
 s: What They -- and Later Jewish Law -- Tell Us About How *Not* to Treat Ou
 r Parents\, Siblings\, and Children”&nbsp\;</b></p><p>We have all read the 
 stories of Genesis many times over and have interpreted them in sermons and
  lessons. The goal of this session is to examine them in the context of fam
 ily ethics.&nbsp\; What bad practices do they exemplify\, and what does Jew
 ish law tell us about how to form better family relationships and avoid fam
 ily violence?<br></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220617T000902Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:ScholarStream: Rabbi Elliot Dorff\, “The Dysfunctional Families of 
 Genesis"
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
