BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20210508T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20210508T120000
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;WKST=SU;UNTIL=20210613T065959Z;BYDAY=SA
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:5kek1k62qgcmdb47m880op04uu@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=bethsh
 olomsf@gmail.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:bethsholomsf@gmail.com
CREATED:20210422T152042Z
DESCRIPTION:<u><strong>HEALTH AND SAFETY PROTOCOLS<br><br>Capacity Protocol
 s</strong></u><ul><li>SFDPH guidelines dictate that attendance at indoor wo
 rship be limited to 50% of a room’s capacity and that congregants from diff
 erent households sit at least six feet from one another.&nbsp\;</li><li>HOW
 EVER\, because much of our service is sung or chanted\, we have decided to 
 space congregants/pods at a twelve foot distance from one another.&nbsp\;</
 li><li>Given the above constraints\, our sanctuary has space for approximat
 ely 50 congregants\, depending on how many people cluster by family/pod.&nb
 sp\;</li></ul><br><u><strong>Attendance Protocols</strong></u><ul><li>Servi
 ce attendance at CBS is at your own risk\, and you must agree to follow all
  rules and instructions.</li><li>Attendee vaccination is not required but i
 s strongly encouraged. Just as we honored the most vulnerable among us duri
 ng the shelter-in-place\, we are going to honor those individuals among us 
 who - for medical reasons - are not able to take the vaccine. We will be co
 ntinuing to follow social distance and safety measures to keep everyone pro
 tected and to remain as inclusive as possible.&nbsp\;</li><li>Individuals o
 r families must sign up in advance to join each Shabbat service.</li><li>Wa
 lk-ins will not be permitted. This allows us to ensure that gatherings rema
 in small\, and enhances our ability to conduct contact tracing in the event
  that someone becomes ill (because we do not write on Shabbat at shul\, we 
 cannot maintain a complete record of attendees if we allow walk-ins).</li><
 li>When you sign up you will complete a health screening survey based on SF
 DPH requirements. If you answer “yes” to any of the questions you must stay
  home.</li><li>Priority will be given&nbsp\;<u>only</u>&nbsp\;to those obse
 rving Yahrtzeit. Otherwise\, all congregants can sign up until we reach cap
 acity.</li></ul><br><u><strong>Protocols for being on-site</strong></u><ul>
 <li>All attendees must bring their own&nbsp\;<em>kippah&nbsp\;</em>and<em>&
 nbsp\;talit.</em></li><li>When you arrive at shul you will be met by traine
 d greeters who will take each person’s temperature\, verbally walk them thr
 ough the health screening questionnaire\, and reiterate the rules for being
  on-site.</li><li>The rules for being on-site will be posted and hand sanit
 izer will be available throughout the shul.&nbsp\;</li><li>Masks must be wo
 rn at all times and physical distancing must be maintained.</li><li>We stro
 ngly encourage people to use restrooms before coming. &nbsp\;Anyone who use
 s the Beth Sholom restrooms please wash your hands properly (with soap for 
 at least 20 seconds) before you leave the bathroom.</li></ul><br><u><strong
 >Protocols for being in the sanctuary</strong></u><ul><li>Shabbat Morning S
 ervices will be two hours long\, from 10 am-noon. Please arrive on time.&nb
 sp\;</li><li>During the services\, all congregants must stay in their seats
  and wear masks (If you need to take a break please use the lower plaza). H
 owever\, standing\, clapping\, singing\, and participating in the Torah dis
 cussion is allowed...and encouraged!</li><li>During the Torah service\, Rab
 bi Ain will take the Torah from the Ark. There will be no processional or r
 ecessional.</li><li>There will only be one person (or family group) at the&
 nbsp\;<em>Bimah</em>&nbsp\;at a time.&nbsp\;</li><li>The sanctuary will be 
 set up to allow the appropriate distance between the&nbsp\;<em>gabbaim</em>
 &nbsp\;(those helping to facilitate the Torah reading) including providing 
 for honors such as&nbsp\;<em>hagbah</em>&nbsp\;and&nbsp\;<em>gelilah</em>.&
 nbsp\;</li><li>During the Torah service\, you can expect the blessing for t
 he aliyah to be recited by the same person who will be chanting the Torah\;
  with Rabbi Ain on the other end of the Sanctuary engaging everyone in dial
 ogue and conversation in between&nbsp\;<em>aliyot</em>.&nbsp\;</li><li>To i
 ncrease ventilation\, all internal leading sanctuary doors will be open and
  a series of air filters will be running inside the sanctuary during the se
 rvice.</li></ul><br>Be on the lookout for more information and details on h
 ow to sign-up for in-person Shabbat morning services. If you have questions
 \, please contact Vered Cohen at&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:vcohen@bethsholomsf.
 org"><strong>vcohen@bethsholomsf.org</strong></a>.
LAST-MODIFIED:20210427T234753Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Shabbat Services
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
