DESCRIPTION:Minyan Yigdal: Kindergarten-3rd Grade\n2nd and 4th Saturday of 
 each month (same days as Munchkins and Mishpacha) In the Gronowski Family C
 hapel 11-12pm (parents welcome but not required)\n\nIn Minyan Yigdal\, chil
 dren are exposed to more tefillot (prayers) of the Shabbat morning service 
 through music and song. Children are encouraged to take a leadership role i
 n services and provided with opportunities to explore prayer as a lens thro
 ugh which Jews relate to God. During the Torah service the parasha (portion
 ) of the week or a story about an upcoming holiday is presented through dis
 cussion\, skits\, and stories. At 12 noon children will go to the Main Meet
 ing Room for a light kiddush with Munchkins & Mishpacha. Families and child
 ren are encouraged to also join the main kiddush in Koret Hall around 12:15
 .
