DESCRIPTION:<br><br><p><strong>WHEN:</strong> Two Mondays\, August 23 and 3
 0\, 7-9 p.m.</p><p><strong>WHERE</strong>: Gronowski Family Chapel at Beth 
 Sholom </p><p>terrible times (ימים נוראים) is a series of art-rituals for t
 he Hebrew New Year. Congregation Beth Sholom joins forces with performance 
 group foreignfire in three High Holy Days events that redraw the boundaries
  of synagogue observance.</p><p><b><a href="https://www.bethsholomsf.org/up
 coming-events/2021/8/16/foreignfire-workshops-8jkc7" id="ow1677" __is_owner
 ="true">Click here for details and registration.</a></b>&nbsp\;</p><br><br>
 <hr><br><br><p>Join us for two trial runs and feedback sessions led by Davi
 d Israel Katz\, and Contribute hands-on to developing two of these timespac
 e-bending Jewish art-rituals:</p><p>FACE: An integrated sound and movement 
 ceremony of reflection and change based on the Kol Nidre text (Monday\, Aug
 ust 23rd)</p><p>BLARE: An extended horn-blowing ceremony to welcome the Heb
 rew New Year (Monday\, August 30)</p>
