DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20191220T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20191220T193000
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:3r35k1sqn0bu4gv5u786gk6c43_R20191116T023000@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20191220T183000
CREATED:20181130T040247Z
DESCRIPTION:Kabbalat Shabbat Service - LISTEN<br>What is the role of music 
 in experiencing the sacred? <br>Where is the boundary between the pleasure 
 and emotion inspired by music and the joy and spiritual engagement that we 
 encounter in prayer? <br>Is listening a spiritual experience?<br><br>Curate
 d by musician and scholar Jeremiah Lockwood\, Listen is a liturgical music 
 series that will help us explore these questions in the context of a unique
  Friday evening service. Jeremiah will draw on his connections to world-ren
 owned musicians working in diverse genres to present profound and soulful m
 usical experiences. Listen will offer an opportunity to engage in deep list
 ening\, hear virtuosic performances\, and learn about sacred music traditio
 ns—both our own Jewish traditions and those of the people we share homeland
 s with today and in other periods in our history.<br><br><u>December 20:</u
 >&nbsp\;<br><br>We welcome back blues and soul singer Terrie Odabi for an i
 ntimate performance of blues and gospel\, accompanied by guitarist and seri
 es curator Jeremiah Lockwood. Terrie's appearance on the Listen series in 2
 018 resonated deeply and was followed by her playing an integral role in th
 e music-oriented alternative Rosh Hashanah service at CBS last Fall.&nbsp\;
 <br><br>According to&nbsp\;Lee Hildebrand\, contributor to the San Francisc
 o Chronicle\,&nbsp\;"Terrie Odabi is easily the most dynamic blues and soul
  woman to have emerged in the Bay Area since Etta James came out of San Fra
 ncisco’s Fillmore District in the Fifties. Terrie has a powerful set of pip
 es\, writes terrific tunes\, leads a kicking band\, and has onstage movemen
 ts that perfectly match the rhythms of her material. Surely stardom awaits 
 her."
LAST-MODIFIED:20200717T002810Z
LOCATION:Gronowski Family Chapel
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY: LISTEN - Kabbalat Shabbat Service
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
