DESCRIPTION:Note for 2015:\nPlan for ~50-60 attendees \nHave sign in sheet 
 ready\nNo wine –in the 9 days before Tisha B’Av it is customary to refrain 
 from meat and wine except for Shabbat\n\nATTENTION: THIS EVENT WAS A GREAT 
 SUCCESS WITH A GREATER TURNOUT THAN HAS BEEN SEEN IN OVER A DECADE. BARUCH 
 HASHEM!\n\nMonday evening August 4th:\n \n6 p.m. Minyan in Chapel (as usual
 )\n \n6:15-7 p.m. Makor Or Meditation in Makom Sholom (need room set-up fro
 m Ellen S.)\nSet-up: Set: Clean room\nCoat rack\,\nextension cord as usual 
 plugged into Jason's office\nEllen will set-up the cushions.\n \n7-8 p.m. L
 ight supper in Main Meeting Room prepared by Debra. Rabbi Glazer will give 
 a drash. \nMenu: red lentil soup\, bread\, salad\, grape juice/wine for 40 
 people.\nSet-up: (5) 60" round tables with 8 folding chairs each and have e
 xtra folding chairs available. Gold tablecloths. Paper plates\, cups\, soup
  bowls\, plastic silverware and wine glasses. Need coffee/tea\, juice\, and
  water. Need hand-washing station (4' tables with hand-washing bowl). Long 
 table with gold linen for refreshments.\n \n8:15-9:30 p.m. reading of Eicha
  /Lamentations in the Chapel by candle-light. Participants will sit on the 
 floor or the built in benches.\nSet-up: Remove pews. Take large black cushi
 ons from Makom Sholom during the dinner and arrange them on the floor of th
 e Chapel. Need small tables with votive candles outside the Chapel. Partici
 pants will carry the lit candles into the Chapel.\n\n\n!
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T075436Z
LOCATION:Makom Shalom\, Main Meeting Room\, Chapel
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Tisha B'Av Observance
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
