CREATED:20210924T200305Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><b>ScholarStream: Cultivating Our Relationships</b></p><p>Bi
 blical stories can inform our understanding of our own relationships. The l
 ife lessons of our ancestors influence our personal\, communal\, and world 
 values.</p><p><b>Liza Bernstein\, “Gendered Gaps: Remembering Sarah Where S
 he is Most Erased”&nbsp\;</b><br></p><p>When we study the Akeidah\, the bin
 ding of Isaac\, we often focus on the dynamics between Abraham\, Isaac\, an
 d God. We rarely ask: where was Sarah? In this session\, we will use tradit
 ional sources and gender theory to open up questions of gender\, community\
 , and parenting. Through our questioning\, we will remember Sarah's story a
 nd re-member Sarah\, in all her complexities\, as a full part of our tradit
 ion.<br></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220617T000918Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:ScholarStream: Liza Bernstein\, “Gendered Gaps: Remembering Sarah W
 here She is Most Erased”
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
