CREATED:20181130T040247Z
DESCRIPTION:Kabbalat Shabbat Service - LISTEN\nWhat is the role of music in
  experiencing the sacred? \nWhere is the boundary between the pleasure and 
 emotion inspired by music and the joy and spiritual engagement that we enco
 unter in prayer? \nIs listening a spiritual experience?\n\nCurated by music
 ian and scholar Jeremiah Lockwood\, Listen is a liturgical music series tha
 t will help us explore these questions in the context of a unique Friday ev
 ening service. Jeremiah will draw on his connections to world-renowned musi
 cians working in diverse genres to present profound and soulful musical exp
 eriences. Listen will offer an opportunity to engage in deep listening\, he
 ar virtuosic performances\, and learn about sacred music traditions—both ou
 r own Jewish traditions and those of the people we share homelands with tod
 ay and in other periods in our history.\n\nNovember 15—Grammy Award-winning
  musician Laurie Lewis is internationally renowned as\na singer\, songwrite
 r\, fiddler\, bandleader\, producer and educator. Laurie has twice been vot
 ed\n“Female Vocalist of the Year” by the International Bluegrass Music Asso
 ciation and has won the respect and admiration of her peers. Linda Ronstadt
  speaks for many when she says of Laurie: “Her voice is a rare combination 
 of grit and grace\, strength and delicacy. Her stories are always true.” A 
 pioneering woman in bluegrass\, Laurie has paved the way for many young wom
 en today\, always guided by her own love of traditional music and the style
 s of her heroes that came before.
LAST-MODIFIED:20200717T002810Z
LOCATION:Gronowski Family Chapel & Main Meeting Room
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY: LISTEN - Kabbalat Shabbat Service
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
