DESCRIPTION:<p><strong>WHEN:</strong> Two Mondays\, August 23 and 30\, 7-9 
 p.m.</p><p><strong>WHERE</strong>: Gronowski Family Chapel at Beth Sholom <
 /p><p>terrible times (ימים נוראים) is a series of art-rituals for the Hebre
 w New Year. Congregation Beth Sholom joins forces with performance group fo
 reignfire in three High Holy Days events that redraw the boundaries of syna
 gogue observance.</p><p><b><a href="https://www.bethsholomsf.org/upcoming-e
 vents/2021/8/16/foreignfire-workshops-8jkc7" target="_blank">Click here for
  details and registration.</a></b> </p><br><br><hr><br><br><p>Join us for t
 wo trial runs and feedback sessions led by David Israel Katz\, and Contribu
 te hands-on to developing two of these timespace-bending Jewish art-rituals
 :</p><p>FACE: An integrated sound and movement ceremony of reflection and c
 hange based on the Kol Nidre text (Monday\, August 23rd)</p><p>BLARE: An ex
 tended horn-blowing ceremony to welcome the Hebrew New Year (Monday\, Augus
 t 30)</p>
