DESCRIPTION:<p dir="ltr">Sacred Drumming as a Gate into the G!dzone (<i>Dve
 ikut</i>) with Rabbi Tsvi Bar-David.</p><p dir="ltr">The path I love the mo
 st is the path of music: rhythm\,&nbsp\;<i>niggun&nbsp\;</i>- wordless melo
 dy\, and simple repetitive words. Your body and spirit are the instrument! 
 Let's learn how to play it together.&nbsp\;</p><p dir="ltr">In these&nbsp\;
 <b>4 sessions</b>\, we focus on the intersection of Jewish and Middle Easte
 rn rhythm\, including: Maqsoum\, Sufi Maqsoum\, Baladi and Chiftetelli. The
 re are no prerequisites for this class. The goal for you is deeper particip
 ation in spiritual events and services.</p><p dir="ltr"><b><br></b></p><p d
 ir="ltr"><b>WHEN</b>: August 24\, 31 &amp\; September 7\, 14</p><p dir="ltr
 ">7:30 p.m. - 8:30 p.m.</p><p dir="ltr"><b>WHERE</b>: Zoom&nbsp\;<i>(</i><a
  href="mailto:tsvi.bardavid@gmail.com"><u><i><u>Email Reb Tsvi</u></i></u><
 /a><i>&nbsp\;</i><a href="mailto:tsvi.bardavid@gmail.com"><u><i><u>tsvi.bar
 david@gmail.com</u></i></u></a><i>&nbsp\;to register/pay and receive Zoom l
 ink)</i></p><p dir="ltr"><i>Money is no barrier to enter this class!</i></p
 >
LAST-MODIFIED:20220810T190422Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Sacred Drumming Class on Zoom
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
