DESCRIPTION:<br><p>A Speaker Series of Dynamic and Diverse Leaders in the J
 ewish World - come learn with incredible people as a part of Beth Sholom's 
 commitment to Organizational Change around Anti-Racism\, Diversity\, Equity
  and Inclusion. Let's live our foundational Jewish values and be the commun
 ity that represents all of our people!</p><p><strong>These events are virtu
 al\, free\, and open to all!</strong></p><p><strong>Rabbi Gershom Sizomu</s
 trong> is the spiritual leader of the Abayudaya Jews of Uganda. Gershom is 
 the leader of the 100-year old Abayudaya community of almost 2\,000 Jews li
 ving in rural villages in Eastern Uganda. As a visionary leader\, Gershom’s
  dream was to attend a rabbinic seminary to better understand ancient and m
 odern egalitarian Judaism and bring the Ugandan community into mainstream J
 ewish life.</p><p><a href="https://www.bethsholomsf.org/upcoming-events/202
 1/6/27/dei-speaker-series-with-rabbi-gershom-sizomu"><b>Visit the event on 
 our website for more information and to register via Zoom.</b>&nbsp\;</a></
 p>
