DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:91mtr5b73145rj432o3q7mgc5r@google.com
CREATED:20201112T232916Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>* Please note\, the start time of this event has shifted to 
 6 p.m.</b><br><br>Join us this week for Kabbalat Shabbat with <b>Dr. Lockwo
 od</b>. Sing some of your favorite tunes to set the mood for entering into 
 Shabbat.<br><br><u><strong>HEALTH AND SAFETY PROTOCOLS<br><br>Capacity Prot
 ocols</strong></u><ul><li>SFDPH guidelines dictate that attendance at indoo
 r worship be limited to 50% of a room’s capacity and that congregants from 
 different households sit at least six feet from one another.&nbsp\;</li><li
 >HOWEVER\, because much of our service is sung or chanted\, we have decided
  to space congregants/pods at a twelve foot distance from one another.&nbsp
 \;</li><li>Given the above constraints\, our sanctuary has space for approx
 imately 50 congregants\, depending on how many people cluster by family/pod
 .&nbsp\;</li></ul><br><u><strong>Attendance Protocols</strong></u><ul><li>S
 ervice attendance at CBS is at your own risk\, and you must agree to follow
  all rules and instructions.</li><li>Attendee vaccination is not required b
 ut is strongly encouraged. Just as we honored the most vulnerable among us 
 during the shelter-in-place\, we are going to honor those individuals among
  us who - for medical reasons - are not able to take the vaccine. We will b
 e continuing to follow social distance and safety measures to keep everyone
  protected and to remain as inclusive as possible.&nbsp\;</li><li>Individua
 ls or families must sign up in advance to join each Shabbat service.</li><l
 i>Walk-ins will not be permitted. This allows us to ensure that gatherings 
 remain small\, and enhances our ability to conduct contact tracing in the e
 vent that someone becomes ill (because we do not write on Shabbat at shul\,
  we cannot maintain a complete record of attendees if we allow walk-ins).</
 li><li>When you sign up you will complete a health screening survey based o
 n SFDPH requirements. If you answer “yes” to any of the questions you must 
 stay home.</li><li>Priority will be given&nbsp\;<u>only</u>&nbsp\;to those 
 observing Yahrtzeit. Otherwise\, all congregants can sign up until we reach
  capacity.</li></ul><br><u><strong>Protocols for being on-site</strong></u>
 <ul><li>All attendees must bring their own&nbsp\;<em>kippah&nbsp\;</em>and<
 em>&nbsp\;talit.</em></li><li>When you arrive at shul you will be met by tr
 ained greeters who will take each person’s temperature\, verbally walk them
  through the health screening questionnaire\, and reiterate the rules for b
 eing on-site.</li><li>The rules for being on-site will be posted and hand s
 anitizer will be available throughout the shul.&nbsp\;</li><li>Masks must b
 e worn at all times and physical distancing must be maintained.</li><li>We 
 strongly encourage people to use restrooms before coming. &nbsp\;Anyone who
  uses the Beth Sholom restrooms please wash your hands properly (with soap 
 for at least 20 seconds) before you leave the bathroom.</li></ul><br><u><st
 rong>Protocols for being in the sanctuary</strong></u><ul><li>Shabbat Morni
 ng Services will be two hours long\, from 10 am-noon. Please arrive on time
 .&nbsp\;</li><li>During the services\, all congregants must stay in their s
 eats and wear masks (If you need to take a break please use the lower plaza
 ). However\, standing\, clapping\, singing\, and participating in the Torah
  discussion is allowed...and encouraged!</li><li>During the Torah service\,
  Rabbi Ain will take the Torah from the Ark. There will be no processional 
 or recessional.</li><li>There will only be one person (or family group) at 
 the&nbsp\;<em>Bimah</em>&nbsp\;at a time.&nbsp\;</li><li>The sanctuary will
  be set up to allow the appropriate distance between the&nbsp\;<em>gabbaim<
 /em>&nbsp\;(those helping to facilitate the Torah reading) including provid
 ing for honors such as&nbsp\;<em>hagbah</em>&nbsp\;and&nbsp\;<em>gelilah</e
 m>.&nbsp\;</li><li>During the Torah service\, you can expect the blessing f
 or the aliyah to be recited by the same person who will be chanting the Tor
 ah\; with Rabbi Ain on the other end of the Sanctuary engaging everyone in 
 dialogue and conversation in between&nbsp\;<em>aliyot</em>.&nbsp\;</li><li>
 To increase ventilation\, all internal leading sanctuary doors will be open
  and a series of air filters will be running inside the sanctuary during th
 e service.</li></ul><br>Be on the lookout for more information and details 
 on how to sign-up for in-person Shabbat morning services. If you have quest
 ions\, please contact Vered Cohen at&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:vcohen@bethsholo
 msf.org"><strong>vcohen@bethsholomsf.org</strong></a>.
LAST-MODIFIED:20210526T165303Z
LOCATION:Sanctuary
SEQUENCE:5
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Kabbalat Shabbat 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
