UID:91mtr5b73145rj432o3q7mgc5r_R20210529T010000@google.com
CREATED:20201112T232916Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>* Please note\, the start time of this event has shifted to 
 6 p.m.</b><br><br><br><u><strong>HEALTH AND SAFETY PROTOCOLS<br><br>Capacit
 y Protocols</strong></u><ul><li>SFDPH guidelines dictate that attendance at
  indoor worship be limited to 50% of a room’s capacity and that congregants
  from different households sit at least six feet from one another.&nbsp\;</
 li><li>HOWEVER\, because much of our service is sung or chanted\, we have d
 ecided to space congregants/pods at a twelve foot distance from one another
 .&nbsp\;</li><li>Given the above constraints\, our sanctuary has space for 
 approximately 50 congregants\, depending on how many people cluster by fami
 ly/pod.&nbsp\;</li></ul><br><u><strong>Attendance Protocols</strong></u><ul
 ><li>Service attendance at CBS is at your own risk\, and you must agree to 
 follow all rules and instructions.</li><li>Attendee vaccination is not requ
 ired but is strongly encouraged. Just as we honored the most vulnerable amo
 ng us during the shelter-in-place\, we are going to honor those individuals
  among us who - for medical reasons - are not able to take the vaccine. We 
 will be continuing to follow social distance and safety measures to keep ev
 eryone protected and to remain as inclusive as possible.&nbsp\;</li><li>Ind
 ividuals or families must sign up in advance to join each Shabbat service.<
 /li><li>Walk-ins will not be permitted. This allows us to ensure that gathe
 rings remain small\, and enhances our ability to conduct contact tracing in
  the event that someone becomes ill (because we do not write on Shabbat at 
 shul\, we cannot maintain a complete record of attendees if we allow walk-i
 ns).</li><li>When you sign up you will complete a health screening survey b
 ased on SFDPH requirements. If you answer “yes” to any of the questions you
  must stay home.</li><li>Priority will be given&nbsp\;<u>only</u>&nbsp\;to 
 those observing Yahrtzeit. Otherwise\, all congregants can sign up until we
  reach capacity.</li></ul><br><u><strong>Protocols for being on-site</stron
 g></u><ul><li>All attendees must bring their own&nbsp\;<em>kippah&nbsp\;</e
 m>and<em>&nbsp\;talit.</em></li><li>When you arrive at shul you will be met
  by trained greeters who will take each person’s temperature\, verbally wal
 k them through the health screening questionnaire\, and reiterate the rules
  for being on-site.</li><li>The rules for being on-site will be posted and 
 hand sanitizer will be available throughout the shul.&nbsp\;</li><li>Masks 
 must be worn at all times and physical distancing must be maintained.</li><
 li>We strongly encourage people to use restrooms before coming. &nbsp\;Anyo
 ne who uses the Beth Sholom restrooms please wash your hands properly (with
  soap for at least 20 seconds) before you leave the bathroom.</li></ul><br>
 <u><strong>Protocols for being in the sanctuary</strong></u><ul><li>Shabbat
  Morning Services will be two hours long\, from 10 am-noon. Please arrive o
 n time.&nbsp\;</li><li>During the services\, all congregants must stay in t
 heir seats and wear masks (If you need to take a break please use the lower
  plaza). However\, standing\, clapping\, singing\, and participating in the
  Torah discussion is allowed...and encouraged!</li><li>During the Torah ser
 vice\, Rabbi Ain will take the Torah from the Ark. There will be no process
 ional or recessional.</li><li>There will only be one person (or family grou
 p) at the&nbsp\;<em>Bimah</em>&nbsp\;at a time.&nbsp\;</li><li>The sanctuar
 y will be set up to allow the appropriate distance between the&nbsp\;<em>ga
 bbaim</em>&nbsp\;(those helping to facilitate the Torah reading) including 
 providing for honors such as&nbsp\;<em>hagbah</em>&nbsp\;and&nbsp\;<em>geli
 lah</em>.&nbsp\;</li><li>During the Torah service\, you can expect the bles
 sing for the aliyah to be recited by the same person who will be chanting t
 he Torah\; with Rabbi Ain on the other end of the Sanctuary engaging everyo
 ne in dialogue and conversation in between&nbsp\;<em>aliyot</em>.&nbsp\;</l
 i><li>To increase ventilation\, all internal leading sanctuary doors will b
 e open and a series of air filters will be running inside the sanctuary dur
 ing the service.</li></ul><br>Be on the lookout for more information and de
 tails on how to sign-up for in-person Shabbat morning services. If you have
  questions\, please contact Vered Cohen at&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:vcohen@bet
 hsholomsf.org"><strong>vcohen@bethsholomsf.org</strong></a>.
LAST-MODIFIED:20210526T165303Z
LOCATION:Sanctuary
SEQUENCE:5
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Kabbalat Shabbat 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
