DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><span>With the up
 coming Israeli election on November 1\,&nbsp\; Beth Sholom is proud to offe
 r another opportunity to hear from Professor Eran Kaplan Ph.D. on this rele
 vant topic:&nbsp\;</span><span><br></span><br><ul><li><u></u>How does the I
 sraeli political system differ from the US political system?<u></u></li></u
 l><ul><li><u></u>How does the Israeli political system work?<u></u></li></u
 l><ul><li><u></u>Why are elections being held now?<u></u></li></ul><u></u><
 br>Professor Kaplan will guide us through the intricacies of Israeli politi
 cs and educate us on how the upcoming Israeli elections will determine the 
 next government of Israel.<u></u><br><u></u><br><u></u><br><u></u>We realiz
 e there are many similar virtual presentations available at this moment\, w
 hich is why we have chosen to host this event in person. We hope this will 
 foster a more intimate setting for questions and discussion.&nbsp\;<br><br>
 <b>Light snacks will be provided</b>. The event is free for Beth Sholom mem
 bers and an $18 donation is suggested &nbsp\;for the community.<br><br><b>W
 HERE</b>: CBS Main Meeting Room<br><br><u></u><b><a href="https://www.beths
 holomsf.org/israeli-elections">More Details and Registration</a></b><u></u>
 <u></u></html-blob>
