DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20190517T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20190517T193000
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:3r35k1sqn0bu4gv5u786gk6c43@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20190517T183000
CREATED:20181130T040247Z
DESCRIPTION:Kabbalat Shabbat Service - LISTEN\nWhat is the role of music in
  experiencing the sacred? \nWhere is the boundary between the pleasure and 
 emotion inspired by music and the joy and spiritual engagement that we enco
 unter in prayer? \nIs listening a spiritual experience?\n\nCurated by music
 ian and scholar Jeremiah Lockwood\, Listen is a liturgical music series tha
 t will help us explore these questions in the context of a unique Friday ev
 ening service. Jeremiah will draw on his connections to world-renowned musi
 cians working in diverse genres to present profound and soulful musical exp
 eriences. Listen will offer an opportunity to engage in deep listening\, he
 ar virtuosic performances\, and learn about sacred music traditions—both ou
 r own Jewish traditions and those of the people we share homelands with tod
 ay and in other periods in our history.\n\nLISTEN Kabbalat Shabbat service 
 with guests Rob Reich\, Daniel Fabricant and Jeremiah Lockwood.\n\nOn Frida
 y May 17\, the Listen series welcomes pianist and composer Rob Reich\, a ve
 rsatile artist whose work represents what makes the San Francisco music sce
 ne a vibrant and vital mecca for independent music\; he’s become one of its
  stalwart underground artists. We are pleased to announce that Rob will be 
 the keyboard player on the special musical High Holiday services at Beth Sh
 olom this coming September! \n\nFor this event\, Rob will be accompanied by
  bassist Daniel Fabricant and will collaborate with series curator Jeremiah
  Lockwood on several numbers.\n\nRob Reich has performed in concert halls\,
  circus tents\, dance clubs\, and chapels. Mirroring  his range of professi
 onal experience\, Reich's music defies genre\, combining strong melodic ide
 as\, rhythmic drive\, and a spirit of irreverence and experimentation. His 
 many musical projects include serving as long-time musical director for Cir
 cus Bella. Reich recently released an album of original swing music\, "Swin
 gs Left". He's also known for his work with Tin Hat & Gaucho. More info at 
 http://www.robreich.com
LAST-MODIFIED:20200717T002810Z
LOCATION:Gronowski Family Chapel
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Kabbalat Shabbat Services - LISTEN
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
