UID:5qmi88atn6oke7emog7c8p41m8@google.com
CREATED:20201022T224815Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Jews in Eastern Europe&nbsp\;in the period before the Holoca
 ust are&nbsp\;often&nbsp\;imagined as&nbsp\;having been traditionally obser
 vant—bearded pious men\, and women with their heads covered.&nbsp\;In this 
 class&nbsp\;we&nbsp\;will explore&nbsp\;Eastern European&nbsp\;stories&nbsp
 \;of modern\, secular trends in Jewish life\, and why they&nbsp\;have been 
 forgotten in popular memory.&nbsp\;</p><p>With&nbsp\;<a href="http://www.jt
 sa.edu/david-fishman">Dr. David Fishman</a>\, Professor of Jewish History\,
  JTS.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20201022T225010Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Scholar Stream: The Tevye Syndrome: How Religious Were East Europea
 n Jews?
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
