DESCRIPTION:Have you ever skipped out on Shabbat services because you feare
 d your kids would be disruptive?&nbsp\;<br><br>Have you ever looked around 
 and wished there were more families during times of prayer?&nbsp\;<br><br>T
 his is the service for you!<br><br>The youth and our families are the futur
 e! Please join us for what will be an inter-generational Shabbat service. A
  space where children can be themselves\, where parents can pray alongside 
 their children and congregants of all ages can feel at home.<br><br>Rabbi A
 manda Russell joined our team full-time in July after serving as the Rabbin
 ic Intern for four years. She has a young family and truly appreciates the 
 structure of a “traditional” Shabbat service. She is excited to explore the
  merging of these two Jewish values\, family and prayer\, into a service th
 at will be inviting for all! Rabbi Russell will be joined by some of our mo
 st loved CBS staff and musicians.<br><br>Our musicians will use instruments
  through Kabbalat Shabbat and we will pray from a family-friendly&nbsp\;<em
 >siddurim&nbsp\;</em>(prayer books).&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br><br>Dinner will be se
 rved in advance of each service. This event is free to the community but pl
 ease register in advance to help us prepare the appropriate amount of food.
 <br><br>L’dor Vador...please JOIN us!<br><br><b>DATE: </b>Fourth&nbsp\;Frid
 ay of every month<br><b>TIME:</b> 5:30pm dinner (KG)\, 6:00pm service (SANC
 )<br><b>LOCATIONS: </b>Koret Hall &amp\; Sanctuary<br><b>REGISTER HERE</b>:
LAST-MODIFIED:20200717T002835Z
LOCATION:Koret Hall and Sanctuary
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:JOIN Kabbalat Shabbat Services
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20220326T163000Z
DTEND:20220326T193000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:5hlfgpbl771j9b9pg5reua8fu8@google.com
CREATED:20220305T015814Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><p>Join Congregation Beth Sholom for a conversation 
 between Senior Rabbi Dan Ain and Daniel Sokatch\, author of <em>Can We Talk
  About Israel: A Guide for the Curious\, Confused\, and Conflicted</em> and
  CEO of the New Israel Fund.</p><p>Sokatch’s book explores why so many peop
 le feel so strongly about Israel and the Israeli-Palestinian conflict. Why 
 does this issue alone turn some classic Jewish liberals into uber-conservat
 ives? Why do compassionate and judicious intellectuals single Israel out fo
 r boycotts\, sanctions\, and a level of opprobrium they do not apply to the
  dozens of other state actors out there? Why do Evangelical Christians who 
 have never even met actual Jews\, or for whom Jews are basically souls to b
 e saved\, feel such fierce loyalty towards Israel? Why does it sometimes se
 em like Israel is the answer to “what’s wrong with the world” for half of t
 he people in it\, and “what’s right with the world” for the other half?</p>
 <p>Daniel Sokatch will join Rabbi Ain for a bima dialogue during Shabbat se
 rvices.&nbsp\; Following services\, congregants and guests are invited to c
 ontinue the conversation and ask questions over a light kiddush meal.</p><p
 ><b><u><a href="https://www.bethsholomsf.org/sokatch" id="ow1868" __is_owne
 r="true">Click here for more details.</a></u></b></p></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220315T184507Z
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:CAN WE TALK ABOUT ISRAEL?  - Rabbi Ain in Conversation with Daniel 
 Sokatch
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20220122T201500Z
DTEND:20220122T211500Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:2hlun4h7cq90nq449jsav8p8qh@google.com
CREATED:20211116T195243Z
DESCRIPTION:<h2><strong>*Please note\, this week’s class will be held in th
 e Zweifach Meditation Garden at 12:15 p.m.</strong></h2><p>Traditional and 
 meditative</p><p>This 12-session class on structures of consciousness from 
 a Jewish perspective uses meditation and chant as well as cognitive teachin
 g\, learning and dialogue.</p><p>Class begins after the weekly Shabbat morn
 ing services and Kiddush at Beth Sholom.</p><br>Each week will feature a sp
 ecific topic\; some topics will span two weeks. We hope you’ll join us ever
 y week\, but it’s not required.<br><b><br></b><br><b><a href="https://www.b
 ethsholomsf.org/rejoicehome">Click Here for details.&nbsp\;</a></b>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220113T004245Z
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:REJOICE - Structures of Consciousness from a Jewish Perspective
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
