BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20191018T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20191018T193000
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:3r35k1sqn0bu4gv5u786gk6c43@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20191018T183000
CREATED:20181130T040247Z
DESCRIPTION:Kabbalat Shabbat Service - LISTEN\nThird Friday of each month \
 n\nWhat is the role of music in experiencing the sacred? \nWhere is the bou
 ndary between the pleasure and emotion inspired by music and the joy and sp
 iritual engagement that we encounter in prayer? \nIs listening a spiritual 
 experience?\n\nCurated by musician and scholar Jeremiah Lockwood\, Listen i
 s a liturgical music series that will help us explore these questions in th
 e context of a unique Friday evening service. Jeremiah will draw on his con
 nections to world-renowned musicians working in diverse genres to present p
 rofound and soulful musical experiences. Listen will offer an opportunity t
 o engage in deep listening\, hear virtuosic performances\, and learn about 
 sacred music traditions—both our own Jewish traditions and those of the peo
 ple we share homelands with today and in other periods in our history.\n\nO
 ctober 18—True Life Trio features the vocal talents of three dynamic perfor
 mers whose\nmusical collaboration was forged in Kitka Women’s Vocal Ensembl
 e. This Bay Area–based trio\ndelves deep into a vast array of folk music th
 at lends itself to three-part vocal harmony\,\nmassaging and expanding the 
 boundaries of traditional styles. Their concerts take audiences on a\nborde
 rless journey through the villages of Ukraine\, the mountains of Bulgaria a
 nd Louisiana’s\nCajun country\, demonstrating the beauty\, power and divers
 ity of vocally driven folk music from\nEastern Europe and North America. Tr
 ue Life Trio honors these traditions while adding their\nown unique spin vi
 a innovative arrangements and folk-inspired compositions. The trio’s fiery\
 nand supple vocals bridge musical worlds and deliver them right to the list
 eners’ ears.
LAST-MODIFIED:20200717T002810Z
LOCATION:Gronowski Family Chapel
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:LISTEN Kabbalat Shabbat Services
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20110929T013000Z
DTEND:20110929T030000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:2bruh95gurvlano5svdo2d46gs@google.com
CREATED:20110429T203346Z
DESCRIPTION:There is no ticket needed for the following services: \nErev Ro
 sh Hashanah Service\nSecond Day Rosh Hashanah Service\nYizkor Service\nMinc
 ha and Ne'ila Service\n\nFor more information and tickets for First Day Ros
 h Hashanah Service\, Kol Nidre Service\, and Yom Kippur Service please call
  the office at 415.221.8736\, ext. 111\, or Tickets@bethsholomsf.org.\n\nWI
 LL-CALL TICKETS \nCheck-in for will-call tickets will be at the main entran
 ce. Photo identification is required for pick-up of will-call tickets. \n\n
 SERVICE DESCRIPTIONS \nOur Sanctuary service will preserve the holidays’ cl
 assic character with traditional hazzanut. \nOur Koret Hall service will be
  a participatory davening experience interspersed with teachings. \n\nSECUR
 ITY \nHigh Holidays tickets are required for admission to services for memb
 ers\, guests\, and nonmembers. Security guards and staff will be at the ent
 rances to the building. Staff will have the names of all ticket holders and
  will be there to assist you. \n\nPUBLIC TRANSPORTATION \nMuni bus lines se
 rvicing the synagogue include the 1\, 2\, 28\, and 38. Detailed directions 
 for using public transportation from within the Bay Area are available onli
 ne at tripplanner.transit.511.org. \n\nPARKING \nPlease remember that parki
 ng in our neighborhood is very limited and those attending services should 
 provide adequate time to find parking. Street cleaning and neighborhood par
 king restrictions during the High Holidays have been lifted for specific st
 reets. Specific information regarding affected blocks will be sent with Hig
 h Holiday tickets.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T075505Z
LOCATION:Sanctuary
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Erev Rosh Hashanah Service
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
