CREATED:20181130T035629Z
DESCRIPTION:\nDAVEN - on the first Friday of each month\n\nFor 500 years\, 
 Jews have used the Kabbalat Shabbat service to\nmake a transition from busy
  weekdays to the calm spaciousness\nof Shabbat. In the DAVEN service\, we w
 ill explore the Hebrew\nliturgy\, using niggun (wordless melody)\, chant\, 
 song\, and silence\nto engage this joyous tradition with our friends and fa
 milies.\n\nDavid Malman has been a CBS member since 1998. He has led\nShabb
 at\, daily minyan\, and High Holy Days services. He is an\nactive participa
 nt in Makor Or\, the meditation group started by\nRabbi Alan Lew (z”l). Dav
 id and his wife Ellen Shireman taught\na successful Learner’s Minyan for se
 veral years\, and he attended\nJoey Weisenberg’s “Building Singing Communit
 ies” multi-day\nworkshops in 2013 and 2014. He is honored and pleased to be
 \nwelcoming Shabbat with the CBS community.
LAST-MODIFIED:20200717T002848Z
LOCATION:Gronowski Family Chapel
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:DAVEN Kabbalat Shabbat Service
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
