DESCRIPTION:<p>Join the JFCS Holocaust Center and greater Bay Area communit
 y for Holocaust Remembrance Day.&nbsp\;</p><p>We invite you on April 8th an
 d 9th to participate in a series of commemorative workshops\, including Hol
 ocaust survivor testimony and expert-led conversations focused on the lesso
 ns and legacies of the Holocaust.</p><p>Attend one or all sessions.&nbsp\;R
 egistrants will receive links to join each session via email prior to the d
 ay’s events.</p><p></p><ul><li><strong>11 am&nbsp\;—&nbsp\;</strong>George 
 Elbaum\, Holocaust Survivor and Member of the JFCS &nbsp\;William J. Lowenb
 erg Speakers Bureau</li><li><strong>12 pm&nbsp\;—&nbsp\;</strong>The Holoca
 ust by Bullets with Yahad in Unum</li><li><strong>2 pm&nbsp\;—&nbsp\;</stro
 ng>The Future of Memory Continued: An Intergenerational Conversation with A
 uthor Elizabeth Rosner</li><li><strong>3 pm&nbsp\;—&nbsp\;</strong>Painting
  Kaddish: A Conversation with Artist Esti Dunow and The Contemporary Jewish
  Museum</li></ul><p></p><p><b><a href="https://yhs2021.eventbrite.com/?aff=
 BethSholom" id="ow18868" __is_owner="true">Register for the Yom HaShoah Day
 s of Commemoration</a></b><strong><br></strong></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20210308T194127Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Yom HaShoah 2021: A Virtual Commemoration - Workshops
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
