DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Due to travel 
 and family needs\, Rabbi Richman will teach her first "Mai Hanukkah?" class
  IN PERSON after Shabbat morning services\, Saturday\, December 10.</b><u><
 /u><br><u></u><b><br></b><b>The second session will be as schedule Thursday
 \, December 15 via</b>&nbsp\;<b><a href="https://us02web.zoom.us/j/32768337
 79"><u>Zoom</u></a></b><b><br></b><br>Join Rabbi Richman for a two-session 
 interactive exploration of this winter holiday. Is Hanukkah a historical ho
 liday? Pagan? Nationalistic? Spiritual? Commercial? Yes! And so much more.&
 nbsp\;<br><br>We will look at Hanukkah through ancient texts to contemporar
 y videos to find resonant ways to connect to Hanukkah this year. Prepare yo
 urself\, body\, mind and spirit for the Festival of Lights and Darkness wit
 h our Beth Sholom learning community.<u></u><br><u></u><br><b>WHEN:</b>&nbs
 p\;Saturday\, December 10 (IN PERSON after Shabbat morning service) <b>and 
 </b>Thursday\, December 15\, 12 p.m. - 1 p.m. via<b>&nbsp\;<a href="https:/
 /us02web.zoom.us/j/3276833779">Zoom</a>.</b><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u>
 </u><u></u></html-blob>
