CREATED:20220624T164753Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><p>Rabbi Lew (z"l) wrote: Tisha B'Av commemorates th
 e fall of the first and second Temples in Jerusalem and\, by extension the 
 whole gamut of disasters that have befallen the Jewish people. Tisha B'Av i
 s not about victimization. Both as individuals and as a people\, we are cal
 led by Tisha B'Av to acknowledge the dark side of our existence and to take
  responsibility for it as well.</p><br>As such\, it makes an excellent star
 ting point for our High Holy Days preparations. Tisha B'Av is about our est
 rangement from God\, from ourselves and from others. Rosh Hashanah and Yom 
 Kippur\, which begin exactly seven weeks after Tisha B' Av\, are about reco
 nciliation\, atonement and <i>teshuvah</i>. On the deepest level\, Tisha B'
 Av and the High Holy Days are part of the same process.</html-blob><br><htm
 l-blob><br></html-blob><br><html-blob>Erev Tisha B'Av<br><br>WHEN: Saturday
 \, August 6\, 7:30 p.m. - 11 p.m.<br><br>WHERE: Eva Gunther Plaza<br><br>Jo
 in Rabbi Amanda Russell and our Lay Leaders in person at Congregation Beth 
 Sholom for a Tisha B'Av service\, including a study session and a reading o
 f Eicha (Book of Lamentations). Dress warmly\, and if you are able\, bring 
 a flashlight or a reading light as we will be outside.<br><br>7:30 p.m. - S
 tudy Session with Rabbi Russell<br><br>8:30 p.m. - Seudat Shlishi\, pre-fas
 t meal (please register)<br><br>9 p.m. - Service and Reading of Eicha<br></
 html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220721T233724Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Tisha b'Av Services
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
