DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20091107T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20091107T182000
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;UNTIL=20100314T010000Z;BYDAY=SA
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:n40jiatqhok0u7d8cur2tuv2ks@google.com
CREATED:20100312T175214Z
DESCRIPTION:Main Meeting Room\, Gronowski Family Chapel\n\nMincha in the Ch
 apel 5:00 pm\nClass and Seudah Shlishit (Third Meal of Shabbat) 5:30 pm\nMa
 ariv and Havdallah 6:00 pm\n\nFrom Birth to Eternity\nTeachings and Lively 
 Discussion\nLed by Rabbi Pam Frydman Baugh\nShabbat afternoons Nov. 7\, 200
 9 through March 20\, 2010\n\nFrom 5:30 to 6 pm\nIn the Main Meeting Room ne
 xt to the Chapel\nAccording to Judaism\, the soul is eternal\, never born a
 nd never dying. For half an hour each shabbat afternoon\, we will read\, th
 ink\, and enter into lively discussion about how our souls are implicated i
 n our everyday lives\, our relationships and our journey after death. Texts
  will be studied in English. \n\nRabbi Pam Frydman Baugh is a Jewish renewa
 l rabbi and member of Congregation Beth Sholom. She was founding rabbi of O
 r Shalom Jewish Community in San Francisco\, she is a founding leader in OH
 ALAH\, an international trans-denominational association of Jewish Renewal 
 rabbis and cantors and she is presently working on a book on the holocaust.
  
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T080442Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Mincha\, Shiur\, Ma'ariv Service
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
