BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20110612T193000Z
DTEND:20110613T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:8r1nv56o3p2tuhltoosmb4hmsc@google.com
CREATED:20110603T171602Z
DESCRIPTION:Summer Sundays" : "Hairspray" at The Mountain Theater (on Mt. T
 amalpais)\nSunday\, June 12\, 12:30- 5:30 p.m. (estimate)\nSan Francisco & 
 Marin\n \nAs part of our "Summer Sundays" community activities offering\, C
 ongregation Beth Sholom invites members to join congregant Howard Haberman 
 for an afternoon of outdoor theater! The group will travel to The Mountain 
 Theater\, an open-air amphitheater located in a lovely grove on Mt. Tam\, f
 or a performance of "Hairspray."\n\n"Hairspray" is set in Baltimore\, Maryl
 and\, circa 1962.  Plump teenager Tracy Turnblad's dream is to dance on "Th
 e Corny Collins Show\," a local TV dance program based on the real-life "Bu
 ddy Deane Show."  When Tracy wins a role on the show\, she becomes a celebr
 ity overnight.  She then launches a campaign to integrate the show.  "Hairs
 pray" offers social commentary on the injustices of 1960s American society.
   Winner of 8 Tony Awards including Best Musical\, "Hairspray" features a h
 eart pounding score of such favorites as "Welcome to the 60s\," "Good Morni
 ng\, Baltimore\," "Mama\, I’m a Big Girl Now\," and "You Can’t Stop the Bea
 t."  (For more information on the venue or play\, please visit www.mountain
 play.org .)\n\nPlease contact Howard Haberman (415-641-0850 or via email) i
 f you are interested in attending.  He will arrange for a meeting place\, c
 ar pool\, and other relevant logistics based on the number of r.s.v.p.'s. P
 lease contact Howard before purchasing tickets. Participants are responsibl
 e for covering their own ticket costs\, but tickets may be purchased in bul
 k. The regular ticket price is $40\, and senior tickets are $35.  "Junior" 
 ticket price (for ages 4-21) are $30\, and children ages 3 and under attend
  for free.\n\n(Those familiar with The Mountain Theater will be happy to le
 arn that the performance will begin at 2pm this year\, allowing for more sh
 aded seats!) 
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T080544Z
LOCATION:Mountain Theatre\, Marin
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Summer Sundays: "Hairspray" at the Mountain Play
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
