UID:e6f2pgp88lo3ge9hfr3gm7su1c@google.com
CREATED:20090810T183029Z
DESCRIPTION:This series of classes from October 2009 through May 2010 offer
 s an opportunity to learn about the foundations of the Jewish tradition\, i
 ncluding calendar\, life cycle\, history\, philosophy\, liturgy\, theology\
 , and Israel. \n\nTonights class will have a special showing of the film Fa
 ces of Israel. A Discussion about Marriage\, State\, and Religion in the Je
 wish Homeland\nThursday\, January 14\, 2010\n7:30 p.m.\nFree/ All are welco
 me\n\nFaces of Israel is an exciting and interactive documentary intended f
 or a wide audience\, from shul-goers to university and high school students
  to unaffiliated members of the Jewish community. The film poses a series o
 f questions on hot topics surrounding what it means to live in both a Jewis
 h and a democratic state. It answers these questions through interviews wit
 h Israelis\, ranging from openly gay secular university students to leaders
  in the Conservative movement to Ultra-Orthodox Jews\, including exclusive 
 footage with Israel’s Ashkenazi Chief Rabbi.\n\n\nClasses continue through 
 May 2010.\n\nFor more information\, please contact the office at 415.221.87
 36\, ext. 101.
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T075806Z
LOCATION:Koret Hall
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Intro to Judaism
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
