CREATED:20100311T230856Z
DESCRIPTION:Our sacred space symposium is a weekend dedicated to study\, le
 arning\, and celebration of sacred space. The Torah portion is Vayakhel\, w
 hich describes the construction of our first holy structure\, the Mishkan. 
 \n\nShabbat morning service (Saturday). The featured speaker is Gary Gilber
 t\, Associate Professor of Religious Studies at Claremont McKenna College. 
 Professor Gilbert’s courses and research focus on Jewish art and architectu
 re in antiquity. His talk will address issues contemporary architects face 
 including building construction\, funding\, and the notion of what makes sp
 ace sacred\, weaving today’s relevant topics with those of ancient times.\n
 \n For more information call  the office at 415-221-8736\, ext. 101.
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T080218Z
LOCATION:301 14th Ave.\, San Francisco\, CA
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:THOU SHALT BUILD HOLINESS: Sacred Space Symposium - Shabbat Service
 s
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
