BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20191215T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20191215T140000
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;WKST=SU;COUNT=1;BYDAY=SU
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:5k3lpbcel3iuoshr7hpa0bh7h5_R20191215T200000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=bethsh
 olomsf@gmail.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:bethsholomsf@gmail.com
CREATED:20190913T185431Z
DESCRIPTION:The Kitchen Hevruta\nwith Gabi Moskowitz & Evan Wolkenstein\n\n
 One of the great things about Torah is that every story operates both as a 
 narrative and as a kind of metaphorical filter to help us see and name the 
 world around us. Whenever you’re studying the Torah\, in other words\, you’
 re also studying human nature and unpacking an ancient and wise way of unde
 rstanding the world.\n\nOther disciplines operate in the same way: when you
  learn how to cook\, you’re not just learning how to combine ingredients to
  make a great dish. You’re learning ways to see the world. How to find bala
 nce. How to surprise\, delight\, nourish\, and satisfy. And you’re learning
  that it’s not just the food - but also who feeds us - that gets us fed.\n\
 nThis four part series will use a structure of 1) hands on prep\, 2) while 
 waiting for the food to cook/heat/rise/sit\, a lively and spirited text dis
 cussion\, and 3) finishing the food - tasting and reflecting on the lessons
  of the day - both culinary and intellectual/spiritual.\n\nCaramel and the 
 Sticky Path to Redemption\nCauliflower Crust Pizza and the Holy Trickster\n
 Crispy Korean Chicken Wings/Tofu and Mirroring at Sinai\nYay\, Leftovers & 
 Mining/Undermining\n\nPrice: Public $360 | CBS Members $72\nLocation: CBS K
 itchen & Main Meeting Room\nTime: 2 p.m.\nDates: Sundays. Nov 17 & 24 and D
 ec 8 & 15
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T080049Z
LOCATION:KT\, CBS-1-Kitchen (KT) (20)
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:The Kitchen Hevruta
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
