UID:i838e57c8b5fl0qvrihvscc4og@google.com
CREATED:20170404T182542Z
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for a unique study session with visiting Israeli
  community building experts to help us re-imagine what it means to “belong”
  in our synagogues and spiritual communities.\n \nCommunity Building “Hacka
 thon” for Stronger Synagogues and Spiritual Communities\nWednesday\, April 
 19\, 9:30-11:30am\nCongregation Beth Sholom\, 301 14th Ave.\, San Francisco
 \n \nLearn and brainstorm with 24 visiting Israeli Community Center leaders
 \, exploring ways that intentional community building practices and mindset
 s can transform our communities.  Please feel free to bring others (profess
 ionals or lay leaders) who might be interested in this opportunity.\n \nThe
  Israeli’s are visiting the Bay Area with Dr. Sarale Shadmi-Wortman\, the c
 ommunity building scholar from Israel who helped transform the whole nation
 al ICC system from service delivery models into community building hubs. Th
 anks to Varda Rabin and the Jewish Community Federation\, we have been lear
 ning about intentional community building practices with Sarale over the pa
 st year\, and wanted to offer this opportunity to you all – to share your o
 wn community building expertise\, and expand your toolkit for doing even mo
 re.  \n \nPlease RSVP  to Wendy Verba at wendyv [at] sfjcf [dot] org  (incl
 ude names and email addresses for all attending)\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T080005Z
LOCATION:Koret Hall
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Community Building "Hackathon"
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
