CREATED:20090722T235020Z
DESCRIPTION:Dr. Ernest M. Weitz Breakfast Club\nNewman Fisher\, President\n
 \nThe Breakfast club currently meets one Sunday of each month (except summe
 r months). There is a brief business meeting followed by an informal talk o
 n topics of interest to the Jewish Community. Speakers have included many c
 ommunity leaders of the San Francisco Jewish Community\, along with members
  of Beth Sholom. Meetings are held at 9 a.m. and start with a free breakfas
 t.\n\nThe moths guest speaker is Professor Mel Gordon from UC Berkely\, giv
 ing an illustrated lecture about Marc Chagall.
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T075831Z
LOCATION:Koret Hall
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Dr. Ernest M. Weitz Breakfast Club
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20100425T170000Z
DTEND:20100425T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:iqelc27o42489v6eglmjpo1ono@google.com
CREATED:20100312T182053Z
DESCRIPTION:CARING FOR THE PEOPLE YOU LOVE BY PLANNING AHEAD!\n\nThinking o
 r talking about estate planning is often difficult. The reality is that it 
 is hard to think about our own mortality and even harder to think about the
  incapacity and/or the loss of those we love. But\, taking the initiative t
 o plan ahead is a loving thing to do for you and your loved ones.\n\nTo lea
 rn more about protecting your estate\, naming guardians for your children\,
  setting up special needs trusts for incapacitated family members\, creatin
 g trusts to provide for your family in the event of your incapacity or deat
 h\, and preparing powers of attorney and advanced health care directives\, 
 this program will provide an excellent overview.  \n\nRebekah Jackson Sapir
 stein is an estate planning attorney\, a member of Congregation Beth Sholom
  and an expert in her field.\n\nPlease join us to learn about estate planni
 ng and to ask your important questions.
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T075717Z
LOCATION:Main Meeting Room
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Caring For The People You Love By Planning Ahead!
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
