CREATED:20100312T180614Z
DESCRIPTION:MAKOR OR: A JEWISH MEDITATION\n“PREPARING FOR THE HIGH HOLIDAYS
 ”\nA Spiritual Intensive led by NORMAN FISCHER\nspiritual teacher and co-fo
 under of Makor Or\n\nThis will be a 21-day period of concentrated spiritual
  practice\, including meditation\, prayer\, and study\, in order to prepare
  for the High Holidays. No knowledge of meditation\, Jewish practice\, or H
 ebrew is required. All levels are welcome. Expect a wonderful immersion in 
 spiritual practice for the newcomer and a deepening of ongoing practice for
  those with experience.\n\nParticipants will commit to:\n·         Classes\
 , Retreats\, and Events \n·          Regular Schedule of Meditation\n·     
      Private Interview Session with Norman Fischer\n\nCLASSES\, RETREATS\, 
 EVENTS\nFriday\, Aug 27\, 4:15-6:15 pm – Opening Session at Beth Sholom fol
 lowed by Kabbalat Shabbat service\nTuesday\, Aug 31\, 6:30-8:30 pm – Class 
 with Norman Fischer at Beth Sholom\nSunday\, Sept 5\, 10 am–5:00 pm – One-d
 ay retreat at the JCCSF with Norman Fischer and Rabbi Aaron Philmus\nMonday
 \, Sept 6\, 6:30-8:30 pm – Class with Norman Fischer at Beth Sholom\nTuesda
 y\, Sept 7\, 7:00-9:00 pm – Community-wide meditation at the JCC\, led by N
 orman Fischer\, in Fisher Hall\nThursday\, Sept 8-10 — Erev Rosh Hashanah a
 nd Rosh Hashanah services\, congregation of your choice\nWednesday\, Sept 1
 5\, 6:30 - 9:30 pm — Class with Norman Fischer at Beth Sholom \nSaturday\, 
 Sept. 18\, 2:00-5:00 pm – Meditation Program as part of Yom Kippur afternoo
 n programming at Beth Sholom\, open to all (optional)\n\nDAILY  MEDITATION\
 nIn addition to the above\, all participants will commit to sitting five ti
 mes a week\, at least twice with the Makor Or community. The other three ma
 y be with another community or at home. All sessions\, except where indicat
 ed\, are at Beth Sholom\, 301 14th Avenue (at Clement) SF\n\nWeek #1\nShabb
 at 8/28 5:00-5:50pm\nM 8/30\, 5:00-5:50pm\nT 8/31\, 6:20-6:50am\nW 9/1\, 5:
 00-5:50pm\nTh 9/2\, 8:00-8:50am (JCCSF)\nTh 9/2\, 5:00-5:50pm\n\nWeek #2\nF
  9/3\, 5:50-6:20pm (Kabbalat Shabbat)\nShabbat 9/4\, 5:00-5:50pm\nT 9/7\, 6
 :20-6:50am\nTh 9/9\, 5:00-5:50pm\n\nWeek #3\nF 9/10\, 5:50-6:20 pm (Kabbala
 t Shabbat)\nShabbat 9/11\, 5:00-5:50pm\nM 9/13\, 5:00-5:50pm\nT 9/14 6:20-6
