DESCRIPTION:Ephraim Margolin is well known to the Jewish community as an ex
 traordinary scholar\, reconteur\, and successful attorney. He is admired fo
 r his intelligence\, meticulous research skills\, and engaging style\, incl
 uding 50+ years of annual Yom Kippur lectures at Congregation Beth Sholom. 
 In this presentation\, taken from his autobiography\, Ephraim will discuss 
 his own experiences enrolling in school when his family immigrated to pre-s
 tate Palestine and what it was like to participate in classes when he didn'
 t speak Hebrew. He also will discuss the pioneering work of Eliezer Ben Yeh
 uda\, the driving spirit behind the revival of Hebrew as a spoken language.
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T080109Z
LOCATION:Gronowski Family Chapel\, CBS-1-Gronowski Family Chapel (GFC) (100
 )
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Achshav Yisrael: Ephraim Margolin on “The Education of One Israeli”
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
