UID:4qbqjh8gkj7j1g033a6vcut3ic@google.com
CREATED:20090914T221303Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us for three classes on Yom Kippur afternoon:\n\nLife and 
 After-Life in Hebrew Poetry\nPresenter: Ephraim Margolin\n2-3 p.m.\, Gronow
 ski Family Chapel\n \nIn his 41st time teaching on Yom Kippur\, Ephraim Mar
 golin will use poetry to throw light on what is happening in Israel current
 ly. \n \nMr. Margolin is a past chairman of the Jewish Community Relations 
 Council\, attorney for the Israeli Consulate\, and lecturer at University o
 f California Hastings College of the Law. \n \n\n\nThe World to Come in Isr
 ael: The Ideal and the Real \nPresenter: Zack Bodner\n3-4 p.m.\, Main Meeti
 ng Room\n \nWe all want to see peace in the Middle East\, but will it come 
 in our lifetime?  Is the time ripe for an Arab-Israeli peace deal under the
  new Obama Administration?  Is Netanyahu ready to do what it takes?  What a
 bout the Palestinian leaders and the Arab world - are they ready to accept 
 a Jewish State?  Are they ready to take the steps necessary for peace with 
 Israel?  And how will Iran figure into the mix\, with their regime's bellig
 erence toward the West\, pursuit of a nuclear weapon and illegitimacy in th
 e eyes of their own people?  Come explore these questions and many more wit
 h Zack Bodner\, Pacific Northwest Director for the American Israel Public A
 ffairs Committee.\n \nAs one of only ten Regional Directors in the country 
 for AIPAC\, Zack Bodner has overseen an unprecedented period of accomplishm
 ent and growth for America's top pro-Israel lobby in the Pacific Northwest.
  Zack has a Master's degree in Philosophy of Religion and Theology\, with a
  focus on Zionist thought and Jewish history\, from Claremont Graduate Univ
 ersity.  Zack has written articles on Israel\, Zionism and Judaism that hav
 e been published in various publications throughout the country.  Zack live
 s in San Francisco with his wife and two children\, and currently serves on
  the Board of Directors of Congregation Beth Sholom.\n \n  \n\nFacing the W
 orld to Come as a Family: Talking About the End of Life. \nPresenter: Cheri
 e Golant\, LCSW\n4-5 p.m.\, Board Room\n \nCherie Golant\, LCSW will facili
 tate this discussion on starting a conversation with your loved ones about 
 your choices for the end of life.  Though many fear these discussions\, the
 y can be as rich and varied as each human life!  Bring your questions as th
 e group will be tailored to participant needs.  Cherie is a Licensed Clinic
 al Social Worker in practice in the bay area since 1996.  Her practice has 
 encompassed the life span\, from disabled children to Holocaust Survivors. 
  She is currently the director of client services at Arcadia Health Care.  
 \n
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T075907Z
LOCATION:301 14th Avenue\, San Francisco\, CA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Classes on Yom Kippur 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
