BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20090523T023000Z
DTEND:20090523T043000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:1235087898-a0fa918-20802@www.bethsholomsf.org
CREATED:20090219T235818Z
DESCRIPTION:The next Keshet dinner ibegins immediately following the conclu
 sion of Friday night services. The guest speaker will be Beth Hillman\, pro
 fessor of law at UC Hastings\, who will speak on "where we are right now: t
 he current state of don't ask/don't tell\, same sex marriage\, and other le
 gal topics of interest to the GLBT community". Beth is an expert on US mili
 tary law and has been very active in efforts to overturn don't ask/don't te
 ll. All are welcome to attend.\n\nR.S.V.P. to Bob Numerof at bnumerof@hotma
 il.com\, by the end of the day on Tuesday May 19. The cost of the vegetaria
 n/kosher dinner is $18. If you mail your check to the Beth Sholom office\, 
 please note "Keshet\, May 22" on the memo line. If you would like to come\,
  but can't afford the cost right now\, just let Bob know so he can still re
 serve a spot for you.\n\nFor more information contact Beth Jones at 415.221
 .8736\, ext. 105\, or BJones@bethsholomsf.org.\n\nThe Keshet Chavurah is Co
 ngregation Beth Sholom's community of lesbian\, gay\, bisexual and transgen
 der Jews\, their friends\, families and supporters. All are welcome to join
  our activities! Beth Sholom welcomes and affirms people of all sexual orie
 ntations and gender identities.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T075711Z
LOCATION:Main Meeting Room
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Keshet Dinner
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
