CREATED:20100311T230856Z
DESCRIPTION:Ten Commandments of Community Event\n\nTHOU SHALT SING - Shabba
 t Shirah \n\nShabbat Shirah ("Sabbath of song") is the name given to the Sh
 abbat when we chant Shirat haYam\, the poetic “Song of the Sea” that Israel
  sang after escaping Pharoah’s army by crossing through the sea of Reeds.\n
 \nJoin CBS for a musical Kabbalat Shabbat followed by a traditional Ma'ariv
  service\, and oneg (Kiddush) to honor and welcome new and prospective memb
 ers. On Saturday morning Dr. Erin Hyman will give a drash on poetry (shirah
 ) and the Torah. On Saturday evening we will have a singing Mincha service 
 Camp Ramah- style\, followed by a class on song in Jewish prayer\, PJ Havda
 llah\, dairy vegetarian potluck dinner and a Saturday Night Live Talent sho
 w. Please contact Rabbi Philmus if you would like to play in the Saturday N
 ight Live Band (especially bass\, keys\, brass and sax) or if you have othe
 r talents you would like to share.\n\nSaturday\, January 15\n\nMorning Shab
 bat Service:\n•Dr. Erin Hyman will give a drash on poetry (shirah and the T
 orah)\n\nFor more information call  the office at 415-221-8736\, ext. 101.
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T080218Z
LOCATION:Sanctuary
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Shabbat Services
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
