UID:sdkrrr1alf9omhn55ng470csb0@google.com
CREATED:20091022T231045Z
DESCRIPTION:A Sunday Afternoon with Rabbi Gedaliah Fleer\nDecember 6 and 27
 \, 2009\n\nRabbi Gedaliah Fleer is acknowledged as a leading authority on J
 ewish Mysticism and Breslov Chassidut who has lectured widely on Kabbalah a
 nd the teachings of Rabbi Nachman of Breslov.  Rabbi Fleer lives in Jerusal
 em and travels annually to cities across the United States to teach. His le
 ctures offer a wealth of profound information and deep insights which can b
 e applied to daily life. \n\nMemory and Forgetfulness:  How we interpret th
 e past sets the stage for our future. How one looks back at his or her life
 \, its meaning and quality\, success or failure is most often a by-product 
 of what one remembers or has chosen to forget. The subtle\, far reaching\, 
 and profound ramifications of the workings of memory and forgetfulness.\n\n
 Cost:  One class: $60\, two classes: $100. Please bring payment to class wi
 th checks payable to Gedaliah Fleer.\n\nFor more information or to register
  contact Lisa Berkelhammer at 415.666.0880 or lisabwellness@gmail.com. R.S.
 V.P. is appreciated but not required.\n\nBeth: Lisa said they do not need a
 nything\, but I bet they would want coffee at least.
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T080554Z
LOCATION:301 14th Avenue\, San Francisco\, Ca\, Gronowski Family Chapel
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:A Sunday Afternoon with Rabbi Gedaliah Fleer
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
