UID:3mgisi08ef1pkoi2kt1i82kdng@google.com
CREATED:20110920T175412Z
DESCRIPTION:What is the difference between letting go and giving up? How do
  you express the abstract truths about your individual\, human experience o
 f teshuvah during this holiday period? Where can you deposit this process o
 f turning inward and discovering the crevices of your behaviors over the pa
 st year\, as you look with vulnerability to who you have been and where you
  veered off your path of integrity and ethics? How do you express forgivene
 ss – for yourself\, for others\, for God? How do you ask for it? With all t
 he subtle\, internal activity of the High Holiday season\, where will you f
 ind your marker in time that sets this process apart from the rest of your 
 year? Where and how will you begin to integrate it all?\n\nUsing simple tec
 hniques used to generate non-verbal material for theater\, we will ask and 
 answer some of these questions\, and then deposit them into our bodies with
  behavioral and expressive gestures that easily and spontaneously come from
  you. The workshop is run like a theatrical rehearsal\, with open\, explora
 tory discussion followed by simple physical exercises that allow you to non
 -verbally articulate what most stuck to you from the discussion. Put togeth
 er\, we create a tapestry of movements that talk about the prayer and intro
 spection of the past 10+ days. Because the body cannot lie. It can only com
 municate honestly with you.\n\nLeah Hermann has been working in theatre in 
 the Bay Area and New York for over 20 years.
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T075724Z
LOCATION:School Building 2nd Floor (Dance Studio)
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:(Yom Kippur) Leah Hermann Theatre/Movement Workshop
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
