BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20130716T013000Z
DTEND:20130716T050000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:2d16dpahgnbc2a8kv4qq0lqvk0@google.com
CREATED:20130715T164722Z
DESCRIPTION:Tisha B'Av Meditation Session\nMonday\, July 15\n\nSchedule:\n~
 6:30-7:30 p.m. Meditation led by Norman Fischer\n~7:30-8:45 p.m. light supp
 er and talk given by Rabbi Zelony\n~8:45-10 p.m. Ma'ariv service and the re
 ading of the Book of Lamentations/Eicha\n\nMakor Or will be holding a Tisha
  B'Av meditation session. The session will include meditation and teaching 
 from Norman Fisher followed by davening with the Beth Sholom congregation a
 nd the candlelight reading of Eicha\, Lamentations. There is no charge for 
 this session.\n\nRabbi Lew wrote\, "Tisha B'Av commemorates the fall of the
  first and second Temples in Jerusalem and\, by extension\, the whole gamut
  of disasters that have befallen the Jewish people. Tisha B'Av is not about
  victimization. Both as individuals and as a people\, we are called by Tish
 a B'Av to acknowledge the dark side of our experience and to take responsib
 ility for it as well. As such\, it makes an excellent starting point for ou
 r High Holiday preparations\, Tisha B'Av is about our estrangement from God
 \, from ourselves and from others. Rosh HaShanah and Yom Kippur\, which beg
 in exactly seven weeks after Tisha B'Av\, are about reconciliation\, atonem
 ent\, and teshuvah. On the deepest level\, Tisha B'Av and the High Holidays
  are part of the same process."\n\nCongregation Beth Sholom (in the Makom S
 holom meditation room)\n301 14th Avenue\, SF\, CA 94118\nTel: 415-221-8736\
 n\nAdditional information:\nThe Tisha B'Av observance will include a light 
 supper and candlelight reading of Eicha\, the Book of Lamentations. Minyan 
 will be held at 6 p.m. at Congregation Beth Sholom following our meditation
  session.\n\nPlease RSVP to Ellen Shireman at ellenshireman@aol.com.
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T075906Z
LOCATION:Gronowski Family Chapel 
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Erev Tisha B'Av 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
