BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20101110T030000Z
DTEND:20101110T050000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:90rbaeq8lvan2hnn10fnbrpp1c@google.com
CREATED:20100802T191309Z
DESCRIPTION:Tonight there will be a special class\, information below:\n\nT
 HREE RABBIS WALK INTO A ROOM:\nRELIGION\, PEOPLEHOOD AND ZIONISM\nWith Rabb
 is Micah Hyman\, Jonathan Jaffe\, and Joshua Strulowitz\nTuesday\, November
  9\, 7 p.m.\, Fisher Family Hall\, JCCSF\nMembers $10 • Public $12 • Studen
 ts $10\n\nThree rabbis hailing from the Conservative\, Reform\, and Orthodo
 x movements share their thoughts on some of the thorniest issues they face 
 as rabbis within their respective movements. What does “community” mean? Wh
 at does it mean to be a Jew? How does each rabbi view his responsibilities 
 to the “other”? And how does each address the challenges of moral and legal
  issues like capital punishment\, abortion and euthanasia? Difficult questi
 ons\, candid answers\, this is a conversation you don’t want to miss.\nSess
 ion one in a series of two.This series of classes from September 2010 throu
 gh May 2011 offers an opportunity to learn about the foundations of the Jew
 ish tradition\, including calendar\, life cycle\, history\, philosophy\, li
 turgy\, theology\, and Israel. \n\nClasses continue through May 2011. For c
 omplete schedule visit http://www.bethsholomsf.org/conversion/conversion.ht
 ml\n\nFor more information\, please contact the office at 415.221.8736\, ex
 t. 101.
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T080118Z
LOCATION:JCCSF: 3200 California St\, SF\, CA 94118 
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Intro to Judaism
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
