CREATED:20090219T235818Z
DESCRIPTION:Board Room (note room change)\, Gronowski Family Chapel\n\nMinc
 ha in the Chapel 5:00 pm\nClass and Seudah Shlishit (Third Meal of Shabbat)
  5:30 pm\nMaariv and Havdallah 6:00 pm\n\nFrom Birth to Eternity\nTeachings
  and Lively Discussion\nLed by Rabbi Pam Frydman Baugh\nShabbat afternoons 
 Nov. 7\, 2009 through March 20\, 2010\n\nFrom 5:30 to 6 pm\nIn the Main Mee
 ting Room next to the Chapel\nAccording to Judaism\, the soul is eternal\, 
 never born and never dying. For half an hour each shabbat afternoon\, we wi
 ll read\, think\, and enter into lively discussion about how our souls are 
 implicated in our everyday lives\, our relationships and our journey after 
 death. Texts will be studied in English. \n\nRabbi Pam Frydman Baugh is a J
 ewish renewal rabbi and member of Congregation Beth Sholom. She was foundin
 g rabbi of Or Shalom Jewish Community in San Francisco\, she is a founding 
 leader in OHALAH\, an international trans-denominational association of Jew
 ish Renewal rabbis and cantors and she is presently working on a book on th
 e holocaust. 
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T075752Z
LOCATION:301 14th Avenue\, San Francisco\, CA
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Mincha\, Shiur\, Ma'ariv Service
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
