DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:2d86vphqugpjhj5ik3djir91hf@google.com
CREATED:20180117T184200Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>For years\, immigrant congregations organized through Faith 
 in Action Bay Area\, a network of congregations and community groups\, have
  been accompanying their neighbors in struggle\, offering presence and soli
 darity. The message: <i>you’re not alone.&nbsp\;</i>More recently\, Faith i
 n Action\, together with a coalition of immigrant and human-rights groups \
 , set up a hotline to respond to the increased threat of ICE raids. We trai
 ned nearly a thousand people in Rapid Response\, giving those targeted by I
 CE raids not only legal support\, but a network of people ready to come imm
 ediately to the sites of raids as witnesses. The message: <i>you’re not alo
 ne.</i></p><p>Now we’re training more people to keep showing up.&nbsp\;Inte
 rgenerational\, cross-class\, multiracial and multilingual\, our accompanim
 ent teams make our communities’ mutual support visible and tangible. We lea
 rn to accompany those facing detention or deportation\, and fight alongside
  them for freedom and dignity. We give each other strength and build long-t
 erm relationships through shared experience. Our trainings include practica
 l teaching about the immigration system\, legal briefings as needed\, and p
 resentations by immigrants on the specific needs of those fighting deportat
 ion.&nbsp\;</p><p>The teams\, along with lawyers\, go to deportation hearin
 gs\, immigration check-ins\, and court. They accompany immigrants resisting
  unfair bosses or landlords. They pray\, talk\, break bread\, share stories
  and reflect together on strategy. They are personal\, practical and politi
 cal: and their message is: <i>you’re not alone.</i></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T080345Z
LOCATION:Sanctuary
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Faith in Action Training
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
