BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20120909T163000Z
DTEND:20120909T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:14qasl5ea9gs2ocrtsu6njpvp0@google.com
CREATED:20120820T201405Z
DESCRIPTION:Members of Congregation Beth Sholom are starting a new book clu
 b.  All are welcome to join us.  We hope to have all kinds of readers:  men
 \, women\, students\, teenagers.\n \nWe plan to meet at Beth Sholom once a 
 month on Sundays\, after morning Minyan\, at about 9:30 a.m.  Current plans
  include the following titles:\n  \nTIME:  Sunday\, September 9th:   \nBOOK
 :Yehoshua\, Abraham B.:  A woman in Jerusalem\; trans. from Hebrew by Hille
 l Halkin.  2006\nSUMMARY:\nA woman in her forties is a victim of a suicide 
 bombing at a Jerusalem market. Her body lies nameless in a hospital morgue.
  She had apparently worked as a cleaning woman at a bakery\, but there is n
 o record of her employment. When a Jerusalem daily accuses the bakery of "g
 ross negligence and inhumanity toward an employee\," the bakery's owner\, o
 verwhelmed by guilt\, entrusts the task of identifying and burying the vict
 im to a human resources man. This man is at first reluctant to take on the 
 job\, but as the facts of the woman's life take shape-she was an engineer f
 rom the former Soviet Union\, a non-Jew on a religious pilgrimage to Jerusa
 lem\, and\, judging by an early photograph\, beautiful-he yields to feeling
 s of regret\, atonement\, and even love.\n\nAt once profoundly serious and 
 highly entertaining\, A. B. Yehoshua astonishes us with his masterly\, ofte
 n unexpected turns in the story and with his ability to get under the skin 
 and into the soul of Israel today.\n\nSAMPLE TEXT:\nhttp://www.loc.gov/catd
 ir/enhancements/fy0659/2005033435-s.html\n \nPlease join us if you are inte
 rested.  We welcome the suggestion of other titles.\n \nStuart Blecher\, So
 l Silver\, Howard Gordon\, Marilyn Kohn.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T075807Z
LOCATION:Library
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:CBS Book Club
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
