UID:o8kr9hs69v8bb6d92h8ppkdmuo@google.com
CREATED:20091125T224901Z
DESCRIPTION:Rededication Keshet Hanukkah \n \nHanukkah is the holiday of re
 dedication\, and so it is for Keshet. What does 2010 hold for Keshet? The a
 nswer lies with us. Come join us to discuss what we want from Keshet in 201
 0\, and how we will make it happen. We want to hear from you so Keshet more
  accurately reflects the needs and desires of its members.\n\nJoin us at th
 is next important Keshet meeting which will be held at Congregation Beth Sh
 olom on Friday\, December 18\, 7:30 p.m.\, immediately following Kabbalat S
 habbat services.\n\nFor dinner we will be hosting a dairy vegetarian potluc
 k\; so brush up your culinary skills and bring a “Fabulous” dish to be shar
 ed by all. Food for the potluck should be dropped off in the Main Meeting R
 oom before services. There will be separate food tables for kosher and non-
 kosher foods.*\n\nR.S.V. P. to Sanford Friedman at esnjays@gmail.com by Wed
 nesday\, December 16 if you’ll be attending\, what you will bring and if it
  was prepared in a kosher kitchen or not.*\n\n*This separation of food is n
 ecessary to honor member’s who keep kosher.\nKeshet (meaning "rainbow")\, t
 he Gay and Lesbian Chavurah/Outreach Program of Congregation Beth Sholom\, 
 was formed in December of 1997 for the purpose of socializing and discussin
 g issues related to being lesbian\, gay\, bisexual\, and/or transgendered i
 n the context of the Conservative movement of Judaism.\n\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T080451Z
LOCATION:Main Meeting Room
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Keshet Dinner
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
