CREATED:20090428T220634Z
DESCRIPTION:The Women's Book Group meets on the third Thursday of the month
 . Books are selected by consensus of the members and generally are written 
 by Jewish authors or are popular novels or works of nonfiction.\n\n\n\nThis
  month's selection is Triangle by Katharine Weber\n\n(242 pp.\, 2006\, Fict
 ion)\n\nOn March 25\, 1911\, 146 sweatshop workers\, most of them women\, p
 erished in the Triangle Shirtwaist fire in New York City. In Weber's novel 
 readers meet 106-year-old Esther\, the last survivor\, her geneticist grand
 daughter Rebecca\, Rebecca's composer partner George\, and Ruth\, a feminis
 t historian determined to unravel the contradictions in Esther's court test
 imony after the fire.\n\nStories\, interviews\, and court records alternate
 \, at last revealing the mystery behind Esther's unlikely survival. This bo
 ok will be provided by the Bureau of Jewish Education Library.\n\n\n\nFor m
 ore information\, contact Jean Tepper at jpt@rwhitesf.com.
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T080534Z
LOCATION:Rabin Library
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Women's Book Group
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
