UID:nq26hi040jg60jf77gcqn01f64@google.com
CREATED:20090810T194107Z
DESCRIPTION:The Fabulous Fillmore\nMain Meeting Room\n\nSan Francisco’s lar
 gest and most vibrant Jewish neighborhood was dense with synagogues\, schoo
 ls\, mutual aid societies\, kosher butchers and restaurants\, cultural cent
 ers\, and much more from the 1906 earthquake to the mid-1960s\, and especia
 lly during the interwar period. It included the Orthodox\, of course\, but 
 also Yiddishists\, Zionists\, Socialists\, and Communists. But the diverse 
 Fillmore was also the entertainment mecca for the whole city\, boasting mov
 ie theaters\, vaudeville houses\, ice skating rinks\, dance halls\, and jaz
 z clubs. Many of the founders of Beth Sholom moved to the Richmond District
  from the Fillmore in the 1930s and ’40s.\n\nThis event is free.\n\nFred Ro
 senbaum\, author of Cosmpolitans: A Social and Cultural History of the Jews
  of the San Francisco Bay Area (UC Press\, 2009)\, brings to light this viv
 id chapter of local Jewish history. The founding director of Lehrhaus Judai
 ca\, Fred is an award-winning educator\, teacher\, and author.\n\n\nThis cl
 ass is cosponsored with Lehrhaus Judaica. To find out more about this and o
 ther classes copy this link into your browser: http://www.lehrhaus.org/cata
 log/course.asp?code=H300-CBS-F09.
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T075905Z
LOCATION:Main Meeting Room
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:The Fabulous Fillmore
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
