UID:nu9flrhrbva1mmhh89r3ui2h0o@google.com
CREATED:20100312T175719Z
DESCRIPTION:Congregation Beth Sholom Community Shabbat Dinner\nIn memory of
  Sarah Horowitz and in conjunction with AJWS’ Global Hunger Shabbat\n\nFrid
 ay\, March 19\, Koret Hall\, Free.\nShabbat Service: 5:20 p.m. (note time c
 hange)\, Shabbat Dinner: 6:30 p.m.\n\nSarah Horowitz was a poet\, (we read 
 her prayer for our country each shabbat)\, a social activist\, a deeply com
 mitted Jew\, and a beloved congregant. Her ties to Beth Sholom continue to 
 give us strength and blessing as we remember her on this Shabbat. At this c
 ommunity dinner\, sponsored by The Horowitz family\, we are weaving her lov
 e for CBS and the work of AJWS. We hope to honor her by our study\, meditat
 ion and action this Shabbat and for many years to come.  \n\nRe-connect wit
 h fellow congregants and make new acquaintances over dinner. Program will i
 nclude activities and learning to increase awareness about global hunger an
 d how we can respond as individuals and a community.  Appropriate for all a
 ges.\n\nLook for more information in March editions of the weekly HaLuach.\
 n\nReservations required.  R.S.V.P. information is Beth Jones at 415.221.87
 36 or dinner@bethsholomsf.org.\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T080601Z
LOCATION:Sanctuary
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Kabbalat Shabbat Service
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
