CREATED:20110603T172116Z
DESCRIPTION:"Summer Sundays (on a Thursday!)": "Seeing Gertrude Stein: Five
  Stories" at the CJM\nThursday\, June 23\, 7-9:30 p.m.\nContemporary Jewish
  Museum (CJM) and The Grove\nJoin fellow Beth Sholom congregants at the Con
 temporary Jewish Museum for an informal tour of "Seeing Gertrude Stein\," a
 n exhibition exploring illuminating "Stein's life and pivotal role in art d
 uring the 20th century.  Focusing on Stein's life from the end of World War
  I through World War II\, the exhibition explores her evolving public perso
 nae\, lifestyle\, relationships\, landmark 1934-35 tour of the United State
 s\, and life in France during WWII."  After the museum visit\, all are welc
 ome to share a glass of wine\, cup of tea\, or other libation and good conv
 ersation at The Grove\, a restaurant very near the CJM.  (The CJM is locate
 d at 736 Mission Street\, between 3rd and 4th.  The Grove is located at 690
  Mission Street.). R.S.V.P. to summer@bethsholomsf.org.
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T075905Z
LOCATION:Contemporary Jewish Museum and The Grove
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Summer Sundays (on a Thursday!): "Seeing Gertrude Stein: Five Stori
 es" at the CJM
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
