UID:00e38u3lh61sm6907b69qtsk4o@google.com
CREATED:20090729T194322Z
DESCRIPTION:Guest speaker\, Gal Szekely\, will present this talk. Gal is a 
 Marriage Family Therapist Intern\, originally from Israel. He graduated fro
 m CIIS University and recently opened a practice on Clement Street. He crea
 ted a talk called: Between two cultures: Cultural differences as reflected 
 in In Treatment.\n\nIn Treatment is an award-winning daily series on HBO\, 
 now in its second season\, that follows psychoanalyst Paul Weston (Gabriel 
 Byrne\, who won a Golden Globe® for his role) working with his clients. The
  original series was created in Israel and was bought and produced by HBO. 
 Although the text in the two versions is often word-by-word\, the differenc
 es are significant and provide a unique opportunity to compare the Israeli 
 and American cultures. \n\nIn this talk present in short pieces from both v
 ersions and together with the audience Gal will analyze and understand the 
 cultural differences and the way they play out in daily life. \n\nGal has p
 resented this talk to the Jewish Community Federation\, Hillel house at Sta
 nford University and at UC Santa Cruz and will be presenting it to UC Berke
 ley\, UC Davis\, and SF State in the fall.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T080042Z
LOCATION:Koret Hall
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Between Two Cultures: Cultural Differences as Reflected in "In Trea
 tment"
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
