CREATED:20100902T233945Z
DESCRIPTION:Ten Commandments of Community Event\n\nTHOU SHALT SING - Shabba
 t Shirah \n\nShabbat Shirah ("Sabbath of song") is the name given to the Sh
 abbat  when we chant Shirat haYam\, the poetic “Song of the Sea” that Israe
 l sang after escaping Pharoah’s army by crossing through the sea of Reeds.\
 n\nJoin CBS Friday for a musical Kabbalat Shabbat followed by a traditional
  Ma'ariv service\, and oneg (Kiddush) to honor and welcome new and prospect
 ive members. On Saturday morning Dr. Erin Hyman will give a drash on poetry
  (shirah) and the Torah. On Saturday evening we will have a singing Mincha 
 service Camp Ramah- style\, followed by a class on song in Jewish prayer\, 
 PJ Havdallah\, dairy vegetarian potluck dinner and a Saturday Night Live Ta
 lent show. Please contact Rabbi Philmus if you would like to play in the Sa
 turday Night Live Band (especially bass\, keys\, brass and sax) or if you h
 ave other talents you would like to share.\n\nFriday\, January 14\n•5:45 p.
 m.- Wine and cheese welcome\n•6:30 p.m.- Musical Kabbalat Shabbat with Rabb
 i Philmus\, Ben Kramarz\, and Ben Krames\n•7 p.m.- Traditional Ma'ariv serv
 ice with Rabbi Hyman\n•7:45 p.m.- Oneg (Kiddush)\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T080600Z
LOCATION:Sanctuary\, Main Meeting Room
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:THOU SHALT SING: Shabbat Shirah
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
