RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;UNTIL=20100321T000000Z;BYDAY=SA
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:1235087898-a09a3d4-20802@www.bethsholomsf.org
CREATED:20090219T235818Z
DESCRIPTION:Main Meeting Room\, Gronowski Family Chapel\n\nMincha in the Ch
 apel 5:00 pm\nClass and Seudah Shlishit (Third Meal of Shabbat) 5:30 pm\nMa
 ariv and Havdallah 6:00 pm\n\nFrom Birth to Eternity\nTeachings and Lively 
 Discussion\nLed by Rabbi Pam Frydman Baugh\nShabbat afternoons Nov. 7\, 200
 9 through March 20\, 2010\n\nFrom 5:30 to 6 pm\nIn the Main Meeting Room ne
 xt to the Chapel\nAccording to Judaism\, the soul is eternal\, never born a
 nd never dying. For half an hour each shabbat afternoon\, we will read\, th
 ink\, and enter into lively discussion about how our souls are implicated i
 n our everyday lives\, our relationships and our journey after death. Texts
  will be studied in English. \n\nRabbi Pam Frydman Baugh is a Jewish renewa
 l rabbi and member of Congregation Beth Sholom. She was founding rabbi of O
 r Shalom Jewish Community in San Francisco\, she is a founding leader in OH
 ALAH\, an international trans-denominational association of Jewish Renewal 
 rabbis and cantors and she is presently working on a book on the holocaust.
  
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T075752Z
LOCATION:301 14th Avenue\, San Francisco\, CA
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Mincha\, Shiur\, Ma'ariv Service
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20130119T180000Z
DTEND:20130120T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:defgafgqki47rc3fk3knvlbof4@google.com
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20120201T235700Z
DESCRIPTION:Silence and Belonging: Shabbat Retreat\nCo-sponsored by Congreg
 ation Beth Sholom and Makor Or. Norman Fischer\, Rabbi Dorothy Richman\, an
 d Rabbi Jonathan Slater lead a Shabbat-long meditation intensive.\n\nSelf-r
 enewal often comes from quieting the action of the mind and body. The Genes
 is creation story states "On the seventh day God renewed God's self." So do
  we when we observe the Sabbath. In this retreat we will practice silent me
 ditation\, returning to the source of all being where we belong and find tr
 ue rest. We will eat silent meals\, pray\, read\, study torah\, and sing. M
 akor Or Shabbat retreats have always been our favorite\, full of joy\, dept
 h and fellowship. No experience with meditation or knowledge of Hebrew nece
 ssary. Please come and bring your family and friends.\n \nThis is a two-day
  retreat held at Congregation Beth Sholom:\n\n    Friday\, Jan 18\, 5:00 - 
 9:00 p.m.\n    Saturday\, Jan 19\, 10:00 a.m. - 6:00 p.m.\n\nREGISTRATION I
 S LIMITED TO THE FIRST 35 PEOPLE\, SO SIGN UP NOW TO RESERVE YOUR PLACE. \n
 \n*$55 Special Rate for Members of Beth Sholom* \nQuestions: Call 415.221.8
 736 
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T080508Z
LOCATION:MMR\, Makom Sholom and Rainbow Courtyard
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Torah of Silence: Meditation Retreat
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
