UID:1235087898-a09a3d4-20802@www.bethsholomsf.org
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20100227T170000
CREATED:20090219T235818Z
DESCRIPTION:Board Room\, Gronowski Family Chapel\n\nMincha in the Chapel 5:
 00 pm\nClass and Seudah Shlishit (Third Meal of Shabbat) 5:30 pm\nMaariv an
 d Havdallah 6:00 pm\n\nFrom Birth to Eternity\nTeachings and Lively Discuss
 ion\nLed by Rabbi Pam Frydman Baugh\nShabbat afternoons Nov. 7\, 2009 throu
 gh March 20\, 2010\n\nFrom 5:30 to 6 pm\nIn the Board Room (tonight only) n
 ext to the Chapel\nAccording to Judaism\, the soul is eternal\, never born 
 and never dying. For half an hour each shabbat afternoon\, we will read\, t
 hink\, and enter into lively discussion about how our souls are implicated 
 in our everyday lives\, our relationships and our journey after death. Text
 s will be studied in English. \n\nRabbi Pam Frydman Baugh is a Jewish renew
 al rabbi and member of Congregation Beth Sholom. She was founding rabbi of 
 Or Shalom Jewish Community in San Francisco\, she is a founding leader in O
 HALAH\, an international trans-denominational association of Jewish Renewal
  rabbis and cantors and she is presently working on a book on the holocaust
 . 
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T075752Z
LOCATION:301 14th Avenue\, San Francisco\, CA
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Mincha\, Shiur\, Ma'ariv Service
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
