DESCRIPTION:Louis Newman has been thinking\, teaching\, and writing about J
 ewish ideas for over 30 years. He is one of the country’s leading scholars 
 of Jewish ethics that address contemporary moral issues from a range of Jew
 ish perspectives. \n\nDr. Newman is the John M. and Elizabeth W. Musser Pro
 fessor of Religious Studies\, the Humphrey Doermann Professor of Liberal Le
 arning and the Director of the Perlman Center for Learning and Teaching at 
 Carleton College in Northfield\, Minnesota.  \n\nFor more information\, ple
 ase visit his website at www.louisnewman.net.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T080552Z
LOCATION:Gronowski Family Chapel
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Guest Speaker: Louis Newman
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20101113T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20101113T120000
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:citgq6mod8aueta981fkaphnvg@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20101113T090000
CREATED:20100311T230856Z
DESCRIPTION:Ten Commandments of Community Event\nTHOU SHALT PUN: Word Play 
 in Jewish Literature\nSponsored by the Cherin Family Lectureship Fund\n\nPe
 ople never take things literally. Jewish people must first learn the text t
 o get the straight read. However Sholom\, “Peace”\, is the understanding th
 at Torah does not limit the few that observe. When our congregation builds 
 together meaning from our sacred letters and our sacred lives\, we create a
  wonderland of context. That is the context of our Community.  \n\nCome and
  play with words when we will have traditional Shabbat services (beginning 
 at 9 a.m.) and alternative Shabbat programming for all ages. Guest speaker 
 Robert Alter\, professor of Hebrew language and comparative literature at U
 C Berkeley\, will give a lecture on word play in Jewish literature. \n\nAlt
 ernative Programming: Adults\n9 a.m. - Meditation\n9:30–11 a.m. - Yoga\, mu
 sic jam\, or word games\n11 a.m. - Join Shabbat service with Robert Alter \
 n(Meditation and yoga will be led by Rachel Yellin of one-moon.com)\n\nB'na
 i Mitzvah Program:\n9:30 a.m. - Teen Shacharit service\n10:20 a.m. - Torah 
 study and music jam\n11 a.m. - Join Shabbat service with Robert Alter\n\nCh
 ildren: (Preschool-5th grade)\n9 a.m. PJ Shabbat breakfast\n9:30 a.m.-12 no
 on - Musical Shacharit services\, Hebrew word games\, yoga\, and more.\n\n1
 2 noon - Special Kiddush for everyone.\n\nTzedakah\nWe had asked for donati
 ons of school supplies for Ulloa Elementary School. It has come to our atte
 ntion that this requires carrying school supplies on Shabbat. In the spirit
  of Shabbat\, we are shifting the request to make a monetary donation eithe
 r before or after Shabbat. Checks may be made out to Congregation Beth Shol
 om\, with a note allocating the funds go to Ulloa Elementary School. If you
  have already purchased school supplies for donation\, please bring them to
  Beth Sholom during the week\, or on Sunday from 9 a.m.-1 p.m. \n\n\nBring 
 a friend! \nIn keeping with our commitment of chaver (friendship)\, we want
  to bring new friends into the Beth Sholom community and share our spirit. 
 Please invite family members\, friends\, business colleagues\, casual acqua
 intances\, or anyone who might enjoy becoming a part of the Beth Sholom com
 munity. \n\nR.S.V.P. by Wednesday\, November 10 to: http://thoushaltpun.eve
 ntbrite.com\n\nThis event is free and everyone is welcome!\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T080218Z
LOCATION:301 14th Avenue\, San Francisco\, CA
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Shabbat Services and Special Event: Thou Shalt Word Play
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
