UID:he5vmhe8u53k1e1iqd9hktv2q8@google.com
CREATED:20100312T175729Z
DESCRIPTION:Congregation Beth Sholom Community Shabbat Dinner\nIn memory of
  Sarah Horowitz and in conjunction with AJWS' Global Hunger Shabbat\nFriday
 \, March 19\, Koret Hall\, No charge\nShabbat Service: 5:20 p.m. (Note time
  change)\nShabbat Dinner: 6:30 p.m.\n\nJoin us for a community Shabbat dinn
 er focused on global hunger and inspired by the life of former congregant S
 arah Horowitz (z"l)\, the program\, in conjunction with AJWS\, will include
  a full evening of meditation\, prayer\, food for the mind heart and soul. 
  \n\nPoteach et Adecha\, umasbia lechol hai ratzon\, open your hand so that
  all can be full.\n\nSchedule:\n4:40 p.m.: meditation\n5:20 p.m.: candle-li
 ghting and kabbalat shabbat \n6:30 p.m.: Shabbat dinner and program\n\nRese
 rvations required by March 12.  R.S.V.P. to Beth Jones at 415.221.8736\, ex
 t. 105\, or dinner@bethsholomsf.org.
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T081229Z
LOCATION:Koret Hall
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Community Shabbat Dinner
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20110227T023000Z
DTEND:20110227T063000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:t2eb9kl1l7rug5qfuk6haus9d8@google.com
CREATED:20101215T214002Z
DESCRIPTION:Our sacred space symposium is a weekend dedicated to study\, le
 arning\, and celebration of sacred space. The Torah portion is Vayakhel\, w
 hich describes the construction of our first holy structure\, the Mishkan. 
 \n\nSaturday Evening's Schedule:\n\n 6:30 p.m.:  Tapas Buffet and Tour of B
 eth Sholom’s award winning sanctuary\, designed by Stanley Saitowitz of Nat
 oma Architects of San Francisco.\n7 p.m.:  Traditional Havdallah service.\n
 7:15 p.m.:  Featured presenter Susan Solomon\, author of Lewis Kahn’s Jewis
 h Architecture: Mikveh Israel and the Midcentury American Synagogue. Ms. So
 lomon will discuss Beth Sholom’s sanctuary in the context of the continuum 
 of sacred space design. \n8:30 p.m.: Screening of the Academy Award nominat
 ed documentary film My Architect: A Son’s Journey\, directed by Nathaniel K
 han\, son of Louis Kahn.\n\nFor more information call the office at 415.221
 .8736\, ext. 101.
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T080832Z
LOCATION:301 14th Ave.\, San Francisco\, CA
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:THOU SHALT BUILD HOLINESS: Sacred Space Symposium
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
