CREATED:20090526T235334Z
DESCRIPTION:“Nachamu\, Nachamu” (Comfort\, Comfort):\nBuilding a Caring Com
 munity for Mental Illness\n\nJoin us for an afternoon of learning and spiri
 tual healing as we draw on social support services and Jewish tradition to 
 create a caring community for those struggling with mental health issues\, 
 as well as their families and friends. The day will be comprised of a diver
 se panel of speakers including those living with mental illness\, family me
 mbers\, mental health professionals\, and spiritual care givers followed by
  small-group discussions and a healing service.\n\nTHIS CONFERENCE IS FREE 
 AND OPEN TO EVERYONE.\nLIGHT REFRESHMENTS WILL BE PROVIDED.\n\nTO R.S.V.P.\
 , OR FOR MORE INFORMATION\nPLEASE CALL CONGREGATION BETH SHOLOM 415.221.873
 6\, EXT. 101 OR E-MAIL MAUREENSAMSON@COMCAST.NET R.S.V.P.’S ARE REQUESTED B
 UT NOT REQUIRED.\n\nCo-Sponsored by Bay Area Jewish Healing Center\, affili
 ated with the Institute on Aging\, and a beneficiary of the Jewish Communit
 y Federation of San Francisco\, the Peninsula\, Marin and Sonoma counties. 
 We thank the Newhouse Fund of the Jewish Community Federation Endowment for
  its gracious support to the Bay Area Jewish Healing Center to provide spir
 itual care to those who live with mental illness.
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T080711Z
LOCATION:Congregation Beth Sholom\, Koret Hall\, Sanctuary\, Main Meeting R
 oom\, Board Room\, Gronowski Family Chapel\, Rabin Library
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Mental Illness Awareness Conference
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
