BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20100212T030000Z
DTEND:20100212T050000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:hpqj8tokg250ofip9eumg0gmhg@google.com
CREATED:20091103T203127Z
DESCRIPTION:Everything Is God with Jay Michaelson\nThursday\, February 11\,
  2010\n7-9 p.m. \nKoret Hall\nCost: $4 members\;  $5 advance\; $8 door\n\nA
  unique evening of learning\, connection celebration in honor of two new bo
 oks Forward 50 honorees Jay Michaelson\, Everything Is God: The Radical Pat
 h of Nondual Judaism\, and Rabbi Jill Jacobs There Shall Be No Needy.\n\n• 
    Learn about new forms of Jewish spirituality and social justice activism
  with Rabbi Jill Jacobs\, Dr. Jo Ellen Green Kaiser (Zeek) and Jay Michaels
 on. BuJus\, Queer Jews\, CuJus\, EcoJews — what do these have in common? Wh
 at's new\, and what's not so new? Are spirituality and activism enemies . .
  . or allies?\n\n•    Connect at a “county fair” of Jewish innovators\, inc
 luding Bay Area Learning Initiative\, Chochmat HaLev\, East Bay Minyan\, G-
 dcast\, Makom Sholom\, Nehirim\, Netivot Shalom\, NITA\, Progressive Jewish
  Alliance\, Wilderness Torah\, Zeek\, and more.\n\n•    Celebrate at a rece
 ption and book-signing with plenty of time to meet the people responsible f
 or this new flowering of Jewish creativity!\n\nPresented by Zeek\, Congrega
 tion Beth Sholom\, and two dozen cosponsoring organizations.  For more info
 rmation\, go to www.everythingisgod.com.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T081151Z
LOCATION:Koret Hall
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Jay Michalson guest speaker
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
