UID:1s6hjdfgnrjunenibetqq1gn70@google.com
CREATED:20110112T201556Z
DESCRIPTION:Message from Judah Rosen\, Chair of Congregation Beth Sholom Je
 wish Prisoners Outreach Project\n\nFor several years now\, Beth Sholom has 
 had a Prison Outreach Program\, where our members interact with inmates at 
 Folsom Prison who are part of the Jewish prison population. Our program has
  two separate aspects: one where our members can become "pen pals" with ind
 ividual inmates\; and one where we as a group visit the prison.\nThe Jewish
  program for those inmates who are interested includes courses in Jewish th
 eology\, Hebrew reading and speaking\, as well as individual counseling. Th
 ey of course have services and celebrate holidays as well. As a person who 
 both visits and has pen pals\, I find this program to be intensely gratifyi
 ng. The core group of prisoners who attend are a varied lot\; some Jewish\,
  some conservative Christians who want to learn more about the "grandfather
 " of their religion\; and some because of Jewish members in their family. I
  have met prisoners who were Israeli\, a Black Christian man who was studyi
 ng as his son was preparing for his Bar Mitzvah\, a physician’s assistant\,
  a son of one of the leading Jewish philanthropic families in the Bay Area\
 , and a Latino who was studying Hebrew though he could not speak English. A
 nd they were all so warm and welcoming and appreciative of the contact with
  us as members of the Jewish community.We are preparing to visit Folsom aga
 in. The actual prison visit lasts from 1-3 p.m.\, and of course it takes a 
 couple hours to drive to Folsom\, so we usually leave around 10am and are h
 ome by 6pm. We hope to increase the number of members of Beth Sholom who wi
 ll attend this time\, so please feel free to contact me if you have an inte
 rest in reaching out to this community of Jews who have no option for reach
 ing out themselves. Recently many prisoners in Folsom were on a lock-down f
 or almost two months\, meaning they could not leave their cells or take par
 t in any of the Jewish activities. And our group has not visited in 8 month
 s. Please join us and help this make a special visit for those inmates who 
 desire a connection to the Jewish community. Sunday\, February 6th is the d
 ate of our next visit. Please let me know \nASAP if you would like to join 
 us. Judah Rosen judahr@comcast.net.
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T080718Z
LOCATION:Folsom Prison
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Folsom Prison Visit
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
