DESCRIPTION:301 14th Avenue\, Koret Hall\n\n2009 Film Series at Congregatio
 n Beth Sholom \nNot Only Written in Stone: the Ten Commandments as Living P
 oetry\nWith Richard Adler and Rabbi Micah Hyman\n\nFour Sundays\, 7–9 p.m.:
 \nMarch 22\nApril 5\nMay 3\nMay 17\n\nDo we produce as well as receive the 
 10 Commandments? Can we look at them as a poetic guide? Do we continue to r
 eceive as well as create these laws every day as we live in the world? \n\n
 Join us as we look at an artist's response in the Decalogue (Poland\, 1989)
 \, a series of hour-long films that have been widely praised as among the g
 reatest cinematic achievements of the last 50 years. Over the course of the
  series we will view and discuss four of the ten dramatic films\, which fea
 ture dazzlingly-told contemporary stories. Light refreshments will be serve
 d. \n \nRichard Adler is a CBS congregant who has led the Beth Sholom film 
 series for three years. He has taught filmmaking and was a staff member of 
 the California Institute of the Arts. For several years he made independent
  documentaries and informational films\; many on issues and developments in
  medicine.\n\nFor more information contact Ariana Barth at 415.221.8736\, e
 xt. 111 or ABarth@bethsholomsf.org.
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T081126Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Film Series
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
