DESCRIPTION:Our congregation has been invited to participate in Project Rec
 onnections\, as part of the Year of Civil Discourse (YCD) Initiative\, a jo
 int project of the JCRC and the Jewish Community Federation\, in partnershi
 p with the Northern California Board of Rabbis.  Under the guidance of faci
 litator\, Rachel Eryn Kalish\, a group of 18-25 congregants will get a chan
 ce to listen to each other talk about controversial subjects\, including Is
 rael\, issues facing Conservative Judaism\, etc.\, learn to accept disagree
 ment without demonizing the other\, and help build a stronger community her
 e at Beth Sholom.  \n \nYou are invited to join in the kickoff event on Sun
 day\, March 20th from 1:30 - 5pm.  \n \nThe goal of Project Reconnections i
 s to encourage the substantive conversation about difficult topics within B
 eth Sholom\, beginning with Israel.  We hope to begin a civil conversation 
 among members that is:\n \n1.       Open to everyone and includes the entir
 e range of views represented within CBS\n2.      Where each person is treat
 ed B'tselem Elohim-- valued and appreciated as a unique spark of the Divine
 \n3.       Focused on building relationships\, and understanding each other
 's stories long before deliberating particular political views\n4.      Saf
 e and well facilitated with very clear guidelines for having respectful\, o
 pen\, vibrant conversations\n5.       Not about Congregation Beth Sholom ta
 king particular political positions \n6.      Creates an environment where 
 intelligent\, informed conversations occur and where everyone is open to le
 arning from others\n \nCongregation Beth Sholom Project Reconnections Kick 
 Off Event Schedule\nMarch 20th 1:30 to 5pm\n \n1:30 -2:00:  Refreshments an
 d Schmoozing \n \n2:00 -2:30 Opening \n•        Welcome\, drash and prayer-
 - Rabbi Micah Hyman\n•        Ground rules for a safe dialogue space --  Ra
 chel Eryn Kalish JCRC Project Reconnections Facilitator \n•        Making t
 he case for why this is important for Congregation Beth Sholom. \n•        
 Details of Project Reconnections and The Year of Civil Discourse-what\, whe
 n\, where\, how and logistics for today-Rachel Eryn Kalish \n \n2:30 - 3:15
  Experience Project Reconnections\n•        Small group dialogues-your back
 ground and experiences talking about Israel and the Israeli-Palestinian rel
 ationship within Congregation Beth Sholom\, in wider Jewish community\, in 
 wider community.\n \n3:15 - 3:30 Break\n \n3:30 - 4:15 Experience Project R
 econnections \n•        Small group dialogues-round two rotate to new group
 .\n \n4:15 - 5:00 Debrief\n•        Reporting back on the small group dialo
 gue. Impressions of the experience. Would you like to participate in furthe
 ring this conversation?\n•        Next Steps:  Explanation of the Congregat
 ion Beth Sholom Project Reconnections Cohort and proposed meeting schedule:
   \n  \n  5:00 Closing Prayer\n \nPlease RSVP to the CBS Project Reconnecti
 ons Planning Committee to save your place at this event:\n Janet Frost     
           frostj@sfusd.edu    415. 517.6822\n   Alan Rothstein   alan-r@sbc
 global.net  650.994.9941         \nIf you would like more information about
  the event\, please contact Janet Frost or Alan Rothstein.  \n \nFor more i
 nformation about The Year of Civil Discourse please go to: www.jcrc.org/ycd
 _about.htm\n \nThank you and we look forward to seeing you on March 20th.  
  \n \n \n
