BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20091206T203000Z
DTEND:20091207T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:rlrdai0hen0nsvppr96cnbe5is@google.com
CREATED:20091022T230843Z
DESCRIPTION:Two Sunday Afternoons with Rabbi Gedaliah Fleer\nDecember 6 and
  27\, 2009\n\nRabbi Gedaliah Fleer is acknowledged as a leading authority o
 n Jewish Mysticism and Breslov Chassidut who has lectured widely on Kabbala
 h and the teachings of Rabbi Nachman of Breslov.  Rabbi Fleer lives in Jeru
 salem and travels annually to cities across the United States to teach. His
  lectures offer a wealth of profound information and deep insights which ca
 n be applied to daily life. \n\nSunday\, December 6 \nThe Stages of Life:  
 A traditional Jewish view of the dynamics of human birth\, growth and devel
 opment. Defining the concept of life as opposed to mere existence. Spiritua
 l awareness and self actualization. The caliber of a soul and its ability t
 o fulfill its potential. The secret of aging and how the limitations of lin
 ear time allow us to access the infinite.\n\n\nSunday\, December 27 \nMemor
 y and Forgetfulness:  How we interpret the past sets the stage for our futu
 re. How one looks back at his or her life\, its meaning and quality\, succe
 ss or failure is most often a by-product of what one remembers or has chose
 n to forget. The subtle\, far reaching\, and profound ramifications of the 
 workings of memory and forgetfulness.\n\nCost:  One class: $60\, two classe
 s: $100. Please bring payment to class with checks payable to Gedaliah Flee
 r.\n\nFor more information or to register contact Lisa Berkelhammer at 415.
