DESCRIPTION:CBS' First Gallery Exhibit is Here\n\nPhotographer Evvy Eisen's
  visually arresting exhibit Multiply By Six Million: Portraits and Stories 
 of Holocaust Survivors is on display through April 30 in the Congregation B
 eth Sholom Gallery\, adjacent to the Gronowski Family Chapel. The exhibit f
 eatures portraits of local Holocaust survivors and their stories of loss an
 d bravery\, as documented by Ms. Eisen. \n \nThe exhibit is open during all
  service times\, and on Monday-Friday\, 10 a.m.-3 p.m.
