DESCRIPTION:Making Prayer Real and Relevant\n\nJoin Rabbi Micah Hyman\, Rab
 bi Aaron Philmus\, and CBS congregant Rabbi Pam Frydman Baugh for a weekly 
 Shabbat Mincha Shiur (text/study and discussion) on the transformative powe
 r of Jewish prayer. Each rabbi will focus on the teachings of one great Jew
 ish teacher from either the medieval\, modern\, or postmodern period to hel
 p us discover how contemporary Jews can make prayer real and relevant in th
 eir lives.\n•November 13–December 18: Rabbi Hyman will teach Maimonides on 
 tefillah (medieval).\n•January 1–29: Rabbi Philmus will teach the Baal Shem
  Tov on tefillah (modern).\n•February 5–March 12: Rabbi Frydman Baugh will 
 teach Reb Zalman Schachter-Shalomi (postmodern).\nFor more information\, co
 ntact Rabbi Aaron Philmus at 415.221.8736\, ext. 106 or RabbiPhilmus@bethsh
 olomsf.org.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T081827Z
LOCATION:Gronowski Family Chapel/ Main Meeting Room
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Mincha/Shiur/Ma'ariv Service
TRANSP:OPAQUE
