UID:501de7akhnu4khf64299avefhk@google.com
CREATED:20090325T233455Z
DESCRIPTION:THE 2008–2009 DAVID LEVINSON SPEAKER SERIES\nAT CONGREGATION BE
 TH SHOLOM\n\nFree and open to the public.\n\nMULTIPLY BY SIX MILLION: \nAn 
 Afternoon with Evvy Eisen\nPhotographer of Holocaust Survivors\nSponsored b
 y the David Levinson Memorial Lecture Series Endowment Fund\n\nBay Area pho
 tographer Evvy Eisen has spent fifteen years creating portraits of Holocaus
 t Survivors. In a special commemoration of Yom HaShoah (Holocaust Remembran
 ce Day) Ms. Eisen will show a film based on her creation of the Multiply By
  Six Million exhibit. After the film\, we will have a special opportunity t
 o participate in small-group discussions with Holocaust Survivors from Cong
 regation Beth Sholom and the Bay Area. \n\nCBS’ First Gallery Exhibit Has A
 rrived\nPhotographer Evvy Eisen’s visually arresting exhibit Multiply By Si
 x Million: Portraits and Stories of Holocaust Survivors is on display in th
 e Congregation Beth Sholom Gallery (adjacent to the Gronowski Family Chapel
 ) until April 30. This exhibition features portraits of local Holocaust sur
 vivors and their stories of loss and bravery. The project works are include
 d in the archives of the US Holocaust Memorial Museum in Washington D.C. an
 d the Centre de Documentation Juive Contemporaine in Paris\, France. \n\nTo
  learn more about the event\, contact Ariana Barth in the CBS office\, ABar
 th@bethsholomsf.org\, 415.221.8736\, ext. 111.
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T080638Z
LOCATION:Koret Hall
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:David Levinson Speaker Series
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
