UID:1235087898-a0e7f8c-20802@www.bethsholomsf.org
CREATED:20090219T235818Z
DESCRIPTION:2009 Film Series at Congregation Beth Sholom \nNot Only Written
  in Stone: the Ten Commandments as Living Poetry\nWith Richard Adler and Ra
 bbi Micah Hyman\n\nFour Sundays\, 7–9 p.m.:\nMarch 22\nApril 5\nMay 3\nMay 
 17\n\nDo we produce as well as receive the 10 Commandments? Can we look at 
 them as a poetic guide? Do we continue to receive as well as create these l
 aws every day as we live in the world? \n\nJoin us as we look at an artist'
 s response in the Decalogue (Poland\, 1989)\, a series of hour-long films t
 hat have been widely praised as among the greatest cinematic achievements o
 f the last 50 years. Over the course of the series we will view and discuss
  four of the ten dramatic films\, which feature dazzlingly-told contemporar
 y stories. Light refreshments will be served. \n \nRichard Adler is a CBS c
 ongregant who has led the Beth Sholom film series for three years. He has t
 aught filmmaking and was a staff member of the California Institute of the 
 Arts. For several years he made independent documentaries and informational
  films\; many on issues and developments in medicine.\n\nFor more informati
 on contact Ariana Barth at ABarth@bethsholomsf.org.
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T081308Z
LOCATION:301 14th Avenue\, Koret Hall
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Film Series
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
