CREATED:20101215T223900Z
DESCRIPTION:The 2010 Pulitzer-Prize winning Broadway musical\, “Next to Nor
 mal\,” is coming to the Curran Theater on national tour\, and Beth Sholom i
 s a co-sponsor of the Sunday 2 p.m. matinee production on January 30\, 2011
 . Also the winner of New York’s “The Best of 2009\,” this emotionally inten
 se\, yet smart and witty musical\, cleverly depicts the fragmenting effects
  of mental illness within a family. Actress Alice Ripley\, as the family’s 
 mother who suffers from manic depression\, gives a Tony-award winning\, “tr
 uly gutsy tour de force performance\,” according to Charles McNulty of the 
 L.A. Times. “Riveting\,” “Shocking\,” “Brave\,” Agonizingly Beautiful” are 
 only a few of the critics’ accolades lavished upon the play. \n\nBeth Sholo
 m is working with four other Bay Area synagogues (Congregation Beth Am\, Co
 ngregation Beth Jacob\, Temple Isaiah\, and Congregation Rodef Sholom) and 
 The Bay Area Jewish Healing Center\, to provide the Jewish community with a
  fun and enjoyable way to learn more about mental illness. A special welcom
 e and discussion will follow immediately after the performance. \n \nTicket
 s are $100\, $65\, and $50 per person. Order yours today at \nhttp://next2n
 ormal.eventbrite.com/. For more information\, please contact Pamela Brown \
 nBay Area Jewish Healing Center\, pbrown@ioaging.org or 415.750.3436.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T080951Z
LOCATION:Curran Theatre
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Next to Normal
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
