UID:e4ge3lj52e4mgpmeottm6ma4vs@google.com
CREATED:20130128T210411Z
DESCRIPTION:Kula Minyan  \nMARK YOUR CALENDARS!\nThe Kula Minyan\, a new mo
 nthly Shabbat service for you and your family\nBegins Saturday\, February 2
 3 at 9:15 a.m.\n\nWhat is Kula?\nKula means\, “leniency” in the Talmud\, an
 d the goal of the Kula Minyan is to create accessibility and invite partici
 pation through lenience.  This service compliments our traditional Shabbat 
 service. Together they create a richer environment for Shabbat worship.\n\n
 Why are we starting the Kula Minyan?\nWe honor you for your commitment to y
 our children’s Jewish education. Honor yourself in the same way. Speak to G
 od in their presence. Share the experience with other families who are doin
 g the same.\n\nWhat if I don’t like being in shul? \nWe get it.  When you t
 hink about Shabbat Services you say\, “I feel uncomfortable with what I don
 ’t know\, and why on earth does the service have to take 3 hours?!” Kula Mi
 nyan is the perfect place to embrace the awkwardness of not knowing. Ask yo
 ur questions. Experiment with an ancient tradition. Sing and laugh your way
  through it.  We’ll guide you the whole way.\n\nWhat does the schedule look
  like?\nThe new service dovetails with our Shabbat school model of teaching
  prayer through participation\, learning and singing.  Adults participate t
 he whole time while children begin in the service and continue learning in 
 their classrooms. See schedule below for timing: \n\nWho?                  
       How long?         Which prayers?\nK & 1st Grade           20 minutes 
         Pesukei d’Zimra\n2nd/3rd/4th Grade      40 minutes         Pesukei 
 d’Zimra & Shacharit\n5th/6th Grade            60 minutes         Pesukei d’
 Zimra\, Shacharit & Torah Reading\nAdults                       60 minutes 
         Pesukei d’Zimra\, Shacharit & Torah Reading + Optional Torah Study 
 \n\nWhen does it start? \nThis year’s dates:\n•    Saturday\, February 23\n
 •    Saturday\, March 23\n•    Saturday\, April 27\n•    Saturday\, May 18\
 n\nHow do I participate?\nMost importantly\, attend with an open spirit rea
 dy to learn and sing along. Ready to take the next step? We’re looking for 
 Torah readers to chant 3 verses.  Rabbi Zelony will provide an MP3 to help 
 you practice as well as in person assistance if needed. \n\nWe look forward
  to praying with you!  \n  
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T080708Z
LOCATION:Gronowski Family Chapel
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Kula Minyan
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
