UID:qdpr89hlnchnsmqouhlhu88jm0@google.com
CREATED:20100312T180711Z
DESCRIPTION:2nd Night Pesach Community Seder\nKosher Feast of Freedom with 
 Rabbi Micah Hyman and Rabbi Aaron Philmus\nTuesday\, March 30\, 6 p.m.\, Ko
 ret Hall\n\n“Everyone must experience Passover as if you were taken out of 
 Egypt.” —Haggadah\n\nIf you experienced Tu B’Shevat with CBS\, you know we 
 have been working hard to provide a Jewish ritual life that is meaningful f
 or children\, parents\, and everyone who desires a tradition that speaks to
  modern life. This Passover we will offer a seder that is filled with learn
 ing\, song\, activities for all ages\, and of course four cups of wine (or 
 grape juice). The seder is both a children’s adventure story\, a philosophi
 cal symposium\, and a holy bacchanal wrapped into one. Please consider CBS 
 your second home for the second-night seder this year. It will be an experi
 ence you will never forget.\n  \nMembers: Adults\, $50\; children ages 3–12
 \, $25\; children ages 0–2\, free\nNonmembers: Adults\, $60\; children ages
  3–12\, $25\; children ages 0–2\, free\nTo R.S.V.P. or for information\, co
 ntact Beth Jones at 415.221.8736\, ext. 105\, or seder@bethsholomsf.org.\n\
 n\nLOVE TO COOK? PLEASE SIGN UP!\n\n•All hands on deck for Beth Sholom’s fi
 rst annual home-cooked second seder!\n•All you culinary do-it-yourselfers\,
  sign on!\n•If you long to get your hands in the matzah meal\, sign on! \n•
 If you just like working with others in a convivial atmosphere\, sign on!\n
 •Volunteers needed:\nSunday\, March 28\, 10 a.m. to 2 p.m.: we need 6 peopl
 e   \nMonday\, March 29\, 9 a.m. to noon: we need 4 people\nTuesday\, March
  30\, noon to 3 p.m.: we need 5 people\n\nPlease respond to Debra Surkin Pe
 rloff at 415.221.8736\, ext. 126\, or DSPerloff@bethsholomsf.org.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T081352Z
LOCATION:Koret Hall
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:2nd Night Community Seder
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
