BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20110522T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20110522T110000
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:91ck5usj9trhp2jq4n1d8d39pc@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20110508T090000
CREATED:20100602T185519Z
DESCRIPTION:Dr. Ernest M. Weitz Breakfast Club\nNewman Fisher\, President\n
 \nThe Breakfast club currently meets one Sunday of each month (except summe
 r months). There is a brief business meeting followed by an informal talk o
 n topics of interest to the Jewish Community. Speakers have included many c
 ommunity leaders of the San Francisco Jewish Community\, along with members
  of Beth Sholom. Meetings are held at 9:30 a.m. and start with a breakfast.
 \n\nThis month's speaker is Rabbi Avi Novis-Deutsch. The topic is "Why Maso
 rti is essential for Israel and America."\n\nIn his talk Rabbi Avi will exp
 lore Masorti as a Jewish concept and will emphasize the main values that ch
 aracterize it. We will than look at these values implications for the kind 
 of  Israel we should have.\n\nRabbi Avi Novis-Deutsch is a Conservative (Ma
 sorti) Rabbi. He served six years as  a pulpit rabbi in Israel\, as well as
  a Talmud and Halacha teacher at the Israeli Rabbinical Seminary. Prior to 
 his Rabbinical training\,  Avi spent eight years in an Orthodox Yeshiva. He
  is spending the year in the East Bay area as the Bay area Masorti visiting
  scholar  where his wife is undertaking  post-doctoral research. Avi is a n
 ative-born Israeli and he and Nurit have three children\n\nCost: $40 per co
 uple\, $25 per individual\, $5 drop-in\n\nFor more information call the off
 ice 415.221.8736.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T081139Z
LOCATION:Koret Hall
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Dr. Ernest M. Weitz Breakfast Club
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
