DESCRIPTION:<p><strong>Join us for an evening of torah exploration\, song\,
  schmooze and light nosh.</strong> </p><p>The holiday of <em>Shavuot</em> m
 arks the moment <i>Torah</i>\, a sacred scroll of divine teachings\, was re
 ceived by the Jewish people on Mount Sinai. Today we honor the <em>Shavuot<
 /em> traditions of gathering in community to celebrate learning and discuss
 ion as a way to discover together and seek new truths. </p><p><span>Join us
  as we partner with the The Kitchen and The JCC for an evening of <i>Torah<
 /i>\, music and cheesecake for our whole community!</span></p><p><strong>Sc
 hedule: <br>7 p.m.</strong> <strong>- 11 p.m.</strong></p><p>7 p.m. - Famil
 y Program</p><p>8 p.m. - Adult Learning</p><p>8 p.m. - Young Adult Program 
 (25-early 40’s) with Young(ish)\, Kitchen Social Club\,  and The JCC </p><p
 ><strong>Location: Congregation Beth Sholom</strong></p><p><strong>Date: Ma
 y 25\, 2023</strong></p><p><b><a href="https://www.bethsholomsf.org/shavuot
 5783">Click here for more information! </a></b></p><p><strong><a href="http
 s://thekitchen.shulcloud.com/event/shavuot-2023">Register Here</a></strong>
 </p><p><br>More information on sessions\, topics and teachers coming soon! 
 You won't want to miss this fantastic evening. To plan for food and space\,
  we appreciate your advance registration.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230509T193057Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Shavuot Community Celebration
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
