DESCRIPTION:<span>Perhaps the joy of Purim doesn’t seem right this year? </
 span><i>Ta’anit Esther </i><span>(</span><a href="https://www.myjewishlearn
 ing.com/article/the-fast-of-esther-a-minor-fast-day/"><u>the Fast of Esther
 </u></a><span>) comes to counterbalance or re-center us in this moment. Joi
 n Rabbi Russell for a</span><span> traditional Mincha Minyan with added com
 mentary to meet the moment. </span><br><span><br></span><br><span>Note: </s
 pan><span>Unlike the fast of Yom Kippur\, which is observed from sunset to 
 sunset\, the fast of Esther begins with daybreak and lasts till sunset.</sp
 an><br><span><br></span><br><b>5:00 - 6:00 p.m. in The Chapel </b>(and on Z
 oom)<br><br>Join Zoom Meeting<br><a href="https://us02web.zoom.us/j/8673067
 0699">https://us02web.zoom.us/j/86730670699</a><br>Meeting ID: 867 3067 069
 9
