DESCRIPTION:<p>Join Young(ish) for a traditional\, egalitarian Shabbat dinn
 er on the <strong><b>Third Friday of each month</b></strong> at Congregatio
 n Beth Sholom. We’ll eat\, sing\, talk\, bless and celebrate! Both Young(is
 h) members and new friends alike in the mid-20s to 40-ish range are welcome
  and encouraged to attend. If you&#39\;re a seasoned Shabbat pro\, great! I
 f not\, even better - all are welcome.</p><p>For more information\, please 
 email <a href="mailto:thirdfridays@bethsholomsf.org" target="_blank"><u>thi
 rdfridays@bethsholomsf.org</u></a>. </p><p><a href="https://www.google.com/
 url?q=https://forms.gle/b2erVcLL7qRqhGjM7&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&am
 p\;ust=1698870756792907&amp\;usg=AOvVaw3W4wxftlgCGdfewWdE6t2P" target="_bla
 nk">Advance registration required.</a> We close registration on Wednesday\,
  November 15th.</p><p><span>We look forward to seeing you!</span></p><p><sp
 an><br></span></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20231027T203250Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Young(ish) Third Friday Shabbat
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20231209T183000Z
DTEND:20231209T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:5nr1s272n515gfs0i8rbjnidpv@google.com
CREATED:20231204T035111Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><strong><b><a href="https://www.bethsholomsf.org/hanukkah-20
 23#hadar">FULL SHABBATON SCHEDULE</a></b></strong></p><p><i>The following e
 vents are free and open to the public.</i></p><p><strong><b>Hanukkah: A Hol
 iday for Parents</b></strong><br></p><p>10:30 a.m. in the Board Room</p><p>
 The word Hanukkah is related to the Hebrew word for ‘education\,’ hinukh. B
 ut what does this holiday have to do with that hallmark Jewish value?<br><e
 m>For parents of Shabbat school-aged children (approx. 30 minutes)</em></p>
 <p><strong><b>Joseph: An Archetype of Jewish Leadership in Exile<br></b></s
 trong>~11:30 a.m. <span>Join Rabbi Kasher for a d’var Torah</span><span> in
  the Sanctuary</span></p><p><strong><b>Dreaming Our Way Into the Future</b>
 </strong><br></p><p>Lunch-n-learn\, ~12:30 p.m.</p><p>Joseph’s story is fil
 led with dreams. From his youth\, he is a vivid dreamer himself\, and soon 
 he becomes a master of dream interpretation. This is the skill that will la
 unch him to great power and will guide his use of that power. From Joseph o
 ur people learned how to dream their way into the future.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20231204T035111Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:A Hanukkah Shabbaton with Hadar and Rabbi David Kasher
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
