DTEND:20230727T050000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:3gp63qp5hhkbfjfud6fa20u0g5@google.com
CREATED:20230711T221949Z
DESCRIPTION:<span><b>Tisha B'Av</b></span><br><b><br></b><br><b>Makom Shalo
 m</b><br>Rabbi Lew (z"l) taught us that Tisha b'Av is the perfect starting 
 point for our High Holy Days preparations. It is about our estrangement fro
 m God\, from ourselves and from others. Rosh Hashanah and Yom Kippur\, whic
 h begin exactly seven weeks after Tisha B' Av\, are about reconciliation\, 
 atonement and teshuvah. On the deepest level\, Tisha B'Av and the High Holy
  Days are part of the same process.<br><br>Join Rabbi Amanda Russell\, Rabb
 i Dorothy Richman and our Lay Leaders for Tisha B'Av\, including learning\,
  a meal and the traditional chanting of Eicha (Lamentations).<br><br><b>7:3
 0 p.m. - Light pre-fast meal and Interactive Learning with Rabbi Richman <a
  href="https://forms.gle/79ZzGCQkUa3rqkis8">(registration required for dinn
 er)</a></b><br><b><br>8:30 p.m. - Reading of Eicha</b><br><b><br>After the 
 reading (approx 9:30 p.m.) - Meditation with Rabbi Richman</b>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230711T221949Z
LOCATION:Congregation Beth Sholom\, 301 14th Ave\, San Francisco\, CA 94118
 \, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Tisha B'Av
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
