UID:0je7hfqfra5pbgofvdp091ndeh@google.com
CREATED:20240715T133945Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><b>Monday\, August 12 - Erev Tisha b’Av</b></p><p>6:45 p.m. 
 - Study Session with Rabbi Richman</p><p>7:30 p.m. - <i>Seudah Mafseket</i>
 \, pre-fast meal (please register <a href="https://forms.gle/qLvFurvKdGFewp
 1PA" target="_blank"><u>here</u></a>)</p><p>8:05 p.m. <i>Maariv</i> Service
  and Reading of <i>Eicha</i> / Lamentations</p><p>~9 p.m. (after the readin
 g) Join Norman Fisher and Rabbi Richman to continue to commemorate Tisha B’
 av in quiet meditation</p><p>On <i>Tisha b'Av</i>\, we commemorate disaster
 s that have befallen the Jewish people\, including\, but not limited to the
  destruction of the First and Second Temples in Jerusalem. The Babylonian T
 almud teaches that the second devastating destruction of the Temple happene
 d because of <i>sinat hinam</i> - baseless hatred. Today\, in a world in wh
 ich there is so much suffering and polarization\, hatred seems to be growin
 g. </p><p>So many of us have so much to mourn\, individually and as a peopl
 e. We will come together on <i>Tisha b'Av</i> to mourn\, to allow the sadne
 ss and grief to be felt\, expressed and witnessed together. Rav Kook\, the 
 great mystic and first Chief Ashkenazi Rabbi of British Mandate Palestine\,
  wrote: “If we were destroyed\, and the world with us\, due to baseless hat
 red\, then we shall rebuild ourselves\, and the world with us\, with basele
 ss love — <i>ahavat hinam</i>.” (Orot HaKodesh vol. III\, p. 324).<br></p><
 p><i>Tisha b'Av</i>\, as Rabbi Lew <i>z’l</i> reminds us\, is the beginning
  of the High Holy Day season. Let us mourn together and rebuild better-- fr
 om love.<br></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20240812T185555Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Erev Tisha b'Av
TRANSP:OPAQUE
