DESCRIPTION:Join Jennifer Lang née Friedman\, who will discuss her book "<a
  href="https://www.vineleavespress.com/places-we-left-behind-by-jennifer-la
 ng.html">Places We Left behind: A memoir-in-miniature</a><span>". </span>Sh
 e will be discussing her core topics of marriage and relationships with our
  acting executive director and trained psychologist\, Dr. Alan Schnur.<br><
 br>American by birth\, French by marriage\, Israeli by choice\, Jennifer La
 ng has written a love story<br>with a lot of conflict—inner and personal\, 
 marital and geopolitical—about home. In Places We Left Behind\, Jennifer pu
 ts her marriage under a microscope\, examining commitment and<br>compromise
 \, faith and family while moving between prose and poetry\, playing with la
 nguage<br>and form\, daring the reader to read between the lines.<br>Free f
 or members\, $18 for guests.<br><a href="https://cbssf.shulcloud.com/form/c
 bs-authors-series-20242jfl.html">Register here</a>.
