UID:2k1msu9bq8pg2jimkg62elq2i9@google.com
CREATED:20230322T161416Z
DESCRIPTION:<br>Pre-Pesach <i>Siyyum Bekhorot</i> (fast of the first born) 
 <br><br>It is an ancient and widespread custom for the firstborn to fast on
  the day before Passover. This commemorates the miracle which spared the fi
 rstborn Jewish sons from the plague which struck down the firstborn sons of
  the Egyptians. <br><br>It is customary to arrange for a <i>siyyum </i>(com
 pletion of learning) to take place at the synagogue after morning minyan on
  the fourteenth of Nissan. The firstborn who are present participate in thi
 s festive meal and\, having broken their fast\, may continue to eat for the
  rest of the day. Since this session is on Zoom\, you will be permitted to 
 have a small bite in your own homes!<br><br>Join Zoom Meeting: <a href="htt
 ps://us02web.zoom.us/j/81632373785">https://us02web.zoom.us/j/81632373785</
 a> <br><br>Meeting ID:  816 3237 3785
LAST-MODIFIED:20230405T044340Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Pre-Pesach Siyyum Bekhorot with Rabbi Amanda Russell on Zoom
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
