UID:4ue20vmvpktlvp52a1tpvf5vtc@google.com
CREATED:20240715T131350Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>Fillmore District Walking Tour</b><br><br>Description:  In t
 he early 20th Century\, San Francisco’s multicultural Fillmore District hos
 ted the second largest Jewish neighborhood west of the Mississippi River.  
 Once known for it’s kosher bakeries\, markets and restaurants\, the Jewish 
 quarter is now gone.  Most Jews departed by the 1950’s\, and the Redevelopm
 ent Agency’s subsequent demolition campaign left most of the area unrecogni
 zable.<br><br>Join Howard Freedman\, Jewish Community Library Director and 
 a Beth Sholom congregant as he leads a walking tour of the neighborhood and
  discusses the Jewish Community that once existed there.  The walk will be 
 about 2.2 miles long and will last around 1 and 1/2 hours. <br><br>Sign up 
 <a href="https://forms.gle/RxTTUVNVwHfc6o5t8">here</a>.  Limited number of 
 spaces.  Members only.
LAST-MODIFIED:20240715T131350Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:SAGES Fillmore District Walking Tour 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
