DESCRIPTION:<br>Sun Feb 25\, 2024 <br>4 - 5:30 p.m.\, in person<p><b><a hre
 f="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1AaElfR2HpBYaEC5RvoaPCTwtRo4SQ_tX8Ynd_Z9
 y35o/viewform?edit_requested=true"><u>Registration Appreciated</u></a></b><
 /p><p><br></p><br>Aging with Dignity: What Questions Should I Be Asking? <b
 r>This session will be facilitated by Rabbi Dorothy Richman and Mary Hulme\
 , geriatric social worker and Founder of Moonstone Geriatrics<br><p>This se
 ssion is for both older adults and adult children or friends who are trying
  to navigate how best to care for the aging folks in their life. It is free
  and open to the public. Please feel welcome to invite friends from outside
  the Beth Sholom community you think could benefit from this conversation.<
 /p><p>After some introductions and Jewish framing\, most of our time togeth
 er will be in active questions and answers. If there are questions that <em
 >you </em>are thinking about that you would like us to know in preparing fo
 r this session\, please submit them <a href="mailto:rabbirichman@bethsholom
 sf.org?subject=Question(s)%20About%20Aging%20with%20Dignity"><u>here</u></a
 >.</p><p><b><br></b></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20240221T052355Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Aging with Dignity - Death Over Dinner Session 1
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
