CREATED:20110720T174855Z
DESCRIPTION:Join fellow Beth Sholom congregants at the Jewish Film Festival
 ! We will see Intimate Grammar (see below for description) at the JCCSF on 
 Sunday\, July 31 at 6:30 p.m.  Meet in the lobby of the JCCSF at 6 p.m. nea
 r the foot of the staircase to then find seats together. After the film\, j
 oin us for coffee\, dessert and a discussion of the film. Please purchase y
 our own ticket by going to www.sfjff.org\, and also r.s.v.p. to summer@beth
 sholomsf.org so we know to look for you. For more information on the film f
 estival\, which begins Thursday\, July 21\, including how to purchase ticke
 ts please see www.sfjff.org.\n\nIntimate Grammar\nAharon\, the teenage son 
 of the dysfunctional Kleinfeld family of early 1960s Jerusalem\, refuses to
  grow up\, instead cultivating an exaggerated inner world in Nir Bergman’s 
 poignant feature\, based on a 1991 novel by David Grossman. Both author (Se
 e Under: Love\, Someone to Run With) and filmmaker (Broken Wings\, In Treat
 ment) excel at telling a moving story from the point of view of a troubled 
 adolescent.   
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T082223Z
LOCATION:JCCSF\, 3200 California St\, San Francisco\, CA 94118
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Summer Sundays: SF Jewish Film Festival "Intimate Grammar"
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
