CREATED:20230329T164421Z
DESCRIPTION:80 years ago—on April 19\, 1943\, Jews in Warsaw rose up agains
 t their oppressors.<br>  <br>They made a choice—to die with dignity\, to no
 t stand idly by. W<span>hat inspiration do we draw from their heroic action
 s? </span><span>What does resistance look like today as we confront new wav
 es of antisemitism?</span><br><span><br></span>Please join us for a <b>virt
 ual </b>commemoration of Holocaust Remembrance Day and program\, including 
 Bay Area rabbis\, California civic leaders\, and discussion with the co-cre
 ators of Ken Burns’ new PBS docuseries\, “The U.S. and The Holocaust”. <br>
 <br><b>WHEN</b>: <br><strong>3:30 p.m.</strong><span> - Reading of the Name
 s </span><br><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScxt561tf_bb
 LF4-AQdmUWM_agM9nz0LGTjeMlLEuSQvEESIg/viewform">Submit names here</a><br><b
 r><strong>6 p.m.</strong> - Memorial Commemoration and Program – “The U.S. 
 and the Holocaust – Past\, Present\, and Future” <br><em>*Rabbi Russell con
 tributed to this virtual program with the singing of Hatikva\, The National
  Anthem of Israel</em><br><b>WHERE</b>: <a href="https://donate.jfcs.org/ev
 ent/yom-hashoah-holocaust-remembrance-day-or-april-17-2023/e475412?c_src=so
 cial&c_src2=instagram">Virtual</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230403T170441Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Yom HaShoah | Holocaust Remembrance Day
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
