CREATED:20231206T063812Z
DESCRIPTION:Hanukkah in a Time of Danger<br>Monday\, December 11\, ~ 8:30 a
 .m. (following minyan — in person and on Zoom)<br><br><br>We are taught in 
 the Mishnah to place our Hanukkiah (Hanukkah menorah) in the window or outs
 ide of the door in order to publicize the miracle of Hanukkah — but with on
 e exception. If we feel that we are in a time of danger\, we are taught tha
 t while publicizing the miracle is the central reason of the holiday\, step
 s need not be taken if one perceives dangerous consequences. Are we in such
  a moment right now? How can we outwardly show our Jewish pride while takin
 g steps to make us feel safe?<br><br><a href="https://us02web.zoom.us/j/816
 32373785"><u><u>https://us02web.zoom.us/j/81632373785</u></u></a> <blockquo
 te><br><center></center></blockquote>
LAST-MODIFIED:20231211T163142Z
LOCATION:https://us02web.zoom.us/j/81632373785 
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Learning with Rabbi Russell: Hanukkah in a Time of Danger
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20231029T170000Z
DTEND:20231029T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:1ria88p03lvk6hsj1i8ucsdptt@google.com
CREATED:20231027T033311Z
DESCRIPTION:<p dir="ltr"><b>Sages of the Ages</b>\, an informal social grou
 p for congregants 55 years of age and older.  </p><p dir="ltr"><br></p><p d
 ir="ltr">I<span>n the face of tragedy\, one thing is clear - we need our Je
 wish community. It has always been true that events in Israel have a deep e
 ffect on how we live as Jews in America\, and it could not be more true tod
 ay. We are heartsick over the horrific loss of so many lives in Israel and 
 Gaza and we know that strengthening our community here and at Beth Sholom i
 s one thing that we can do to build for a stronger Jewish future. </span></
 p><p dir="ltr">It is with that <i>kavanna </i>(intention)<i> </i>that we in
 troduce Beth Sholom’s newest group:  <b>Sages of the Ages</b>\, an informal
  social group for congregants 55 years of age and older.  We are excited to
  launch a Beth Sholom social group focusing on the interests of those at th
 is marvelous age!</p><p dir="ltr">The group’s first event is <b>Sunday\, Oc
 tober 29\, from 10:00 a.m. to Noon at Beth Sholom.  </b>Brunch will be serv
 ed.  (What\, a gathering without food\; not a chance!)  The first session w
 ill be devoted to discussing the interests of those in attendance\, their h
 opes for the group\, ideas for upcoming events\, and\, possibly\, the devel
 opment of a schedule of activities.</p><p><b><a href="https://docs.google.c
 om/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSc149L9sXuvCcLsWZO8aZymqsry8c5Cf66WoKOwPkeO9pm9XA/viewf
 orm">RSVP HERE</a></b></p><br>Our hope is to create a vibrant group that\, 
 together\, will build a wonderful\, engaging\, informal and fun social comm
 unity of Beth Sholom sages.  We hope you’ll plan to join us for our inaugur
 al event on <b>Sunday\, October 29\, at 10:00 a.m.</b>
LAST-MODIFIED:20231027T033311Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Sage of the Age: Beth Sholom's Newest Group
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
