BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20230911T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20230911T140000
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:0lbi5mo503r35g65bum9nnjjkn@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20230912T120000
CREATED:20230801T201836Z
DESCRIPTION:The God we pray to on the High Holy Days is often imagined as a
  King writing in the books of Life and Death. But what if we are praying to
  Water\, Voice\, Fire\, Rock\, Cloud\, or even Becoming? How might that cha
 nge us and our ability to connect to our liturgy? To the Divine? To our own
  still small voice? Reading Rabbi Toba Spitzer&#39\;s accessible book of th
 eology\, we will explore different possiblilites for relating to the Divine
 \, in theory and in practice. Join Rabbi Dorothy Richman for an interactive
  exploration of this  fascinating and relevant book to prepare for the High
  Holy Days.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230911T164220Z
LOCATION:https://us02web.zoom.us/j/89339986828
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Elul Book Group: God Is Here - Reimagining the Divine by Toba Spitz
 er with Rabbi Dorothy Richman
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
