UID:367283jvre7k09p7jfh3t1n368@google.com
CREATED:20240624T165929Z
DESCRIPTION:Joanne Greene will discuss her memoir <a href="https://www.joan
 ne-greene.com/book" target="_blank">"By Accident</a>": A Memoir of Letting 
 Go at the Koret Hall\, during kiddush following services.<br><br>Joanne Gre
 ene's life story unfolds against the backdrop of a transformative era for w
 omen in America. Growing up in Boston during the liberating 1960s and '70s\
 , she seized opportunities in San Francisco's media scene\, excelling in ra
 dio and television. Her career in producing feminist and socially relevant 
 content spanned decades\, all while striving for a fulfilling marriage and 
 parenthood. However\, beneath her outward success lay a struggle with a rel
 entless desire for control. A pivotal accident shattered her sense of maste
 ry\, leading Joanne on a profound journey of self-discovery. She learned th
 at true strength emerges not from control\, but from vulnerability and acce
 ptance of fragility. "By Accident" is her testament to realizing that relin
 quishing the illusion of control can unveil inner resilience and guide us t
 o more solid ground. <br>Purchase your copy in advance at the Beth Sholom o
 ffice.<br>Free for members\, $18 for guests.<br>More information <a href="h
 ttps://www.bethsholomsf.org/home/cbs-authors-series-joanne-greene" target="
 _blank">here</a>.<br>Please register <a href="https://cbssf.shulcloud.com/f
 orm/cbs-authors-series-2024-Joanne%20Greene.html" target="_blank">here</a>.
LAST-MODIFIED:20240729T162105Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Author's Series: Joanne Greene
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
