DTEND:20230603T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:7jshq8g298ua26pdigqvc9b7t4@google.com
CREATED:20230519T154335Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>5 p.m. - </b>Gather and dinner<br><b>6 p.m. - </b>1-hr Kabba
 lat Shabbat<br><b>7 p.m. - </b>Lila tov!<br><br>On Friday\, June 2\, come j
 oin us at 5 p.m. for the Family and Community Dinner and Kabbalat Shabbat. 
  <br><br>This joyous and festive gathering is for families and community me
 mbers of all ages. The evening will begin with a few experiential learning 
 spaces that will offer the opportunity for us to connect to the Hebrew mont
 h of Sivan and to Parashat Nasso\, the longest portion in the Torah!  <br><
 br>A delicious meal prepared by Beth Sholom’s Executive Chef Marlene will b
 e served for all to enjoy as you build relationships with others\, shmooze 
 and unwind from the week.  <br><br>After dinner\, we will all head into the
  Gronowski Chapel for a traditional\, musical Kabbalat Shabbat service led 
 by Rabbi Amanda Russell and Jonathan Bayer.  <br><br>Dessert will be enjoye
 d upon the completion of the service and we will all walk out into the San 
 Francisco night full of Shabbat goodness\, community belonging and joy.  <b
 r> <br><strong><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://forms.gle/WU4w
 WH6Y8cFJYwbXA&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;ust=1684942995788383&amp\
 ;usg=AOvVaw3MaJf3PkulhXV7GUxRojZT" target="_blank"><u>Please register for t
 his event in advance</u></a></strong>\, so we can be sure to have enough Sh
 abbos food for all!
LAST-MODIFIED:20230519T154335Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Family and Community Shabbat Dinner
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20230204T170000Z
DTEND:20230205T023000Z
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:1420q9phm29fpmlq7l418idhce@google.com
CREATED:20230109T223307Z
DESCRIPTION:Join Norman Fischer and Rabbi Richman for an in-person Jewish M
 editation Shabbaton retreat at Beth Sholom beginning Friday\, February 3 at
  5 p.m. through Saturday\, February 4\, 6:30 p.m. <br><br>We will sit\, sin
 g\, eat\, pray\, study\, and celebrate Shabbat in community. <strong>This i
 s a non-residential retreat— we will conclude around 9 p.m. on Friday night
  and return at 9 a.m. on Saturday morning</strong>. Three meals are include
 d in your registration. <br><br>Makor Or Shabbat retreats have always been 
 our favorite: full of joy\, depth and community. No experience with meditat
 ion or knowledge of Hebrew necessary. Join us and experience the sweetness 
 and soulfulness of Shabbat- body\, mind\, and spirit. <br><br>Explore with 
 us what Norman calls “religious life as a song\, a melody\, maybe without w
 ords." <br><br>Any questions? Please email Rabbi Richman: <a href="mailto:r
 abbirichman@bethsholomsf.org"><strong>rabbirichman@bethsholomsf.org</strong
 ></a>.<br><br><b><a href="https://www.bethsholomsf.org/makor-or-shabbat-shi
 ra">Learn More and Register Here</a></b><br><br><strong>WHEN</strong>: Frid
 ay\, February 3\, 5 p.m. - 9 p.m. <strong>and </strong>Saturday\, February 
 4\, 9 a.m. - 6:30 p.m. <br><br><strong>WHERE</strong>: CBS Makom Sholom\, M
 editation Room
LAST-MODIFIED:20230111T000538Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Makor Or Shabbat Shira Shabbaton: Song and Silence Shabbos
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
