UID:16jhldgrldgsc4o9p9h7m9ffgk@google.com
CREATED:20100812T214810Z
DESCRIPTION:Ten Commandments of Community Event\nTHOU SHALT PARTY Oneg Shab
 bat and Rabbi Micah Hyman’s Birthday\n \n“If you refrain from doing your bu
 siness on My holy day\, and call Shabbat a PARTY! (ONEG)… \nthen you will h
 ave heavenly bliss…” (Isaiah 58:13-14)\n\nHOW DO JEWS PARTY? The Talmud say
 s: With GOOD FOOD and Torahs!\n\nJoin us for guest speaker Sue Fishkoff\, w
 ho will talk about \nher new book\, Kosher Nation.\n\nProgramming for ALL a
 ges:\n6–6:30 p.m.  Kabbalat Shabbat services with music for all ages\, Sanc
 tuary\n                  (Please note service time change)\n6:30–7:30 p.m. 
            Pizza birthday party for children ages preschool to 13\, Koret H
 all\n                                  followed by age-appropriate activiti
 es\n\nProgramming for Adults:\n6:30–7 p.m.  Ma’ariv service\, Sanctuary \n7
 –7:30 p.m.  Guest speaker Sue Fishkoff\, author of Kosher Nation\, Sanctuar
 y\n7:30–8:30 p.m.            Oneg Shabbat with tapas\, bar\, and community 
 for everyone\, Koret Hall\n\nHe doesn’t want everyone to know\, but we sure
  do – Oct 22 is also Rabbi Hyman’s birthday!!! In lieu of gifts a contribut
 ion to the Kiddush Fund will be welcome.\n\nIn the spirit of supporting the
  San Francisco community we are a part of\, please consider bringing new pr
 esents we can donate to low-income families (the children will wrap them du
 ring the party).\n\nIn the spirit of “haver” (friendship)\, we want to brin
 g new friends into the Beth Sholom community and share our spirit. Please c
 onsider inviting a family member\, friend\, business colleagues\, casual ac
 quaintances\, or anyone who might enjoy becoming a part of the Beth Sholom 
 community. \n\nWe are hosting an intimate special pre-event reception for h
 ost members and their guests before the party. This is a great time to schm
 ooze with the rabbis\, staff\, and members and learn more about our congreg
 ation. Childcare is available during the pre-event reception only. \n\nR.S.
 V.P. required by Tuesday\, October 19 to http://onegshabbat.eventbrite.com\
 nThis event is free and everyone is welcome!\n\nSee our website for all of 
 the Ten Commandments of Community Events: http://www.bethsholomsf.org/event
 s/ten-commandments-of-community.html
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T081935Z
LOCATION:Sanctuary and Koret Hall
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Thou Shalt Party: Oneg Shabbat\, Lecture\, and Rabbi Hyman's Birthd
 ay Party
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
