DESCRIPTION:<p>Services will begin at 9:00 a.m. with options for <strong>tr
 aditional morning service </strong>in the Sanctuary or <strong>music and me
 ditation</strong> in Makom Shalom. <em>Yizkor</em> will be at 11:00 a.m. an
 d will be followed by <em>Musaf</em> at 12:00 p.m.</p><p><br></p><p>The aft
 ernoon brings a range of opportunities to learn\, meditate and/or listen an
 d share. We are especially pleased to have <strong>guest scholar Naomi Seid
 man </strong>with us to offer teaching during this time. <em><strong>Mincha
  and Ne’ila</strong></em> will begin at 4:30 p.m. in the Sanctuary. After w
 e conclude with <em><strong>Ma’ariv and Havdalah</strong></em>\, we invite 
 you to <strong>break-the-fast</strong> in community in Koret Hall.</p>
