DESCRIPTION:<em>Shamati</em> is Hebrew for\, “I heard [you].” Wouldn’t the 
 world be a better place with more validated and compassionate listening? Le
 t our community model what it means to be open and to receive from others\,
  simply by opening our hearts. <strong><b>As we continue to grieve the loss
  of so many lives in Israel and Gaza and pray for peace and safety for all\
 , this is an opportunity to share and reflect.</b></strong><br><b><br></b><
 br><strong><b>We are excited to be joined by</b></strong> <a href="https://
 www.benkramarz.com/"><u><strong><b>Ben Kramarz</b></strong></u></a><strong>
 <b> for this special and spiritual evening.</b></strong><b><br></b><br><p>B
 reathe. Share. Listen. Reflect. Let’s be there for each other. </p><p>5 p.m
 . — Chapel opens for quiet sitting<br>5:15 p.m. — Sharing begins<br>6 p.m. 
 — Kabbalat Shabbat and Maariv</p><p><a href="https://www.bethsholomsf.org/s
 hamati"><b>More Event Information</b></a></p><br><b>WHERE</b>: CBS Chapel
LAST-MODIFIED:20250819T211955Z
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Shamati: An Evening of Listening
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
