DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://us06web.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_OE6Mc5NXSe
 2q1i8fAE7Oow#/registration">https://us06web.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_OE6
 Mc5NXSe2q1i8fAE7Oow#/registration</a><br><br>Join us for a powerful online 
 program marking International Holocaust Remembrance Day. Award-winning auth
 or Elizabeth Rosner\, whose widely acclaimed book Survivor Café explores in
 tergenerational trauma and memory\, will be joined by her relative\, Ezra B
 rettler\, a third-generation descendant and member of the JFCS William J. L
 owenberg Speakers Bureau. Together\, they will reflect on how their family 
 carries forward the memory\, legacy\, and lessons of the Holocaust\, and ho
 w these stories continue to shape and inspire future generations.This Progr
 am is presented in partnership with: American Jewish Committee\, Consulate 
 General of Israel\, Consulate General of Germany\, Consul General of Greece
 \, and is supported by our community partners: the Anti-Defamation League\,
  Congregation Beth Jacob\, Congregation Beth Sholom\, Congregation Chevra T
 hilim\, Congregation Emanu-El\, Congregation Sherith Israel\, The Contempor
 ary Jewish Museum\, JCCSF\, JCRC Bay Area\, Jewish Community Library\, Jewi
 sh Federation Bay Area\, JIMENA: Jews Indigenous to the Middle East and Nor
 th Africa\, Manny’s\, Repair the World\, San Francisco Campus for Jewish Li
 ving\, and StandWithUs Northern California.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260127T172720Z
LOCATION:https://us06web.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_OE6Mc5NXSe2q1i8fAE7Oow
 #/registration
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:JFCS Zoom Webinar for International Holocaust Remembrance Day
TRANSP:OPAQUE
