DESCRIPTION:<p><a href="http:///" target="_blank"></a>In these days of conf
 lict and upheaval\, how can we find freedom?</p><p>What is the freedom that
  can be renewed inside?</p><p>And how might the Passover seder and rituals 
 help us to celebrate freedom - for ourselves and for everyone?</p><p>Join N
 orman Fischer and Rabbi Dorothy Richman for a day-long meditation retreat t
 o prepare your heart and soul for Passover. We will sit\, chant and study t
 ogether. Familiar tunes and new questions\, included.</p><p>No meditation e
 xperience necessary. All are welcome. Please join us in person at Congregat
 ion Beth Sholom in San Francisco or on Zoom.<br>A recording of the retreat 
 will be sent to everyone who registers.</p><p><b><i><a href="https://cbssf.
 shulcloud.com/form/makor-or-meditation-retreat-for-passover1.html">Register
  here</a></i></b></p><p><b><b>When: Sunday\, April 6\, 10:00 am - 5:00 pm (
 Pacific Time)<br>Where: Congregation Beth Sholom in San Francisco\, CA or o
 n Zoom</b></b><br><br><b><b>Zoom fee: $36 </b></b><strong><b>(<b><b>the Zoo
 m link will be sent to you on Friday\, April 12)</b></b></b></strong><br><b
 ><b>In-person fee: $54 (space is limited)<br>Sponsor: Please consider a con
 tribution to support folks for whom cost is a barrier</b></b></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250307T162453Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Renewing Freedom: Makor Or Meditation Retreat for Passover in Perso
 n or on Zoom
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
