DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://hadar.org/learn/classes-events/hadar-west-art-
 havruta" target="_blank">https://hadar.org/learn/classes-events/hadar-west-
 art-havruta</a><br><br><p><strong>The Art of Havruta: A Mishnah Study Serie
 s with Hadar</strong></p><p>Join our SF Beit Midrash for three months of le
 arning through a blend of independent havruta-learning and three in-person 
 Beit Midrash sessions\, open to everyone. </p><p>At each Beit Midrash sessi
 on\, Rabbi Kasher will offer brief teachings on the philosophy of havruta s
 tudy and guide us through the themes and structure of the Mishnah chapters 
 from <a href="https://www.projectzug.org/" target="_blank"><u><u>Hadar’s Pr
 oject Zug</u></u></a> Course “The Mishnah In Context”. This is an opportuni
 ty to get to know a core genre of Jewish text while developing the skills a
 nd spirit of classical havruta learning.</p><p> <a href="https://www.projec
 tzug.org/" target="_blank"><u><u>Project Zug</u></u></a> registration is fr
 ee to Beth Sholom and Emanu-El members participating in this Beit Midrash.<
 /p><p><i><b>Note: The first and third session will be at Congregation Beth 
 Sholom. The second session will be at Congregation Emanu-el. (2 Lake St\, S
 an Francisco\, CA 94118)</b></i></p><b>Date and Time</b><br><br><u></u>Tue\
 , Jan 27\, 6:30<u></u> - <u></u>8:30 PM Pacific<u></u><br><u></u>Tue\, Feb 
 24\, 6:30<u></u> - <u></u>8:30 PM Pacific<u></u><br><u></u>Tue\, Mar 24\, 6
 :30<u></u> - <u></u>8:30 PM Pacific<u></u><br><br><b>Location</b><br>Congre
 gation Beth Sholom<br><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/1JYpfbypW7NHNxPf9" t
 arget="_blank"><u>301 14th Ave\, San Francisco\, CA 94118</u></a><br><br><b
 >Cost</b><br>Free
