DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><h2><br></
 h2><u></u>The minyan also meets at 8:30 a.m. on the following national holi
 days: Martin Luther King Jr\, Day\; Memorial Day\; Presidents’ Day\; Indepe
 ndence Day\; Labor Day\; Thanksgiving\; Day after Thanksgiving.&nbsp\;<br><
 br></html-blob><br><html-blob>We are excited to announce that both Monday a
 nd Thursday in-person minyanim will take place in the Grownoski Chapel at C
 BS using a hybrid model (Zoom for those not attending in person). Masks are
  required and social distancing will be in effect. All attendees will also 
 be required to attest to their vaccination status &nbsp\;before entering.<u
 ></u><br><u></u><br><u></u><br><u></u>The definition of a minyan for Thursd
 ay is 10 people in person\, based on which he will lead the minyan services
  that will include kaddish\, barchu\, and a heicha kedusha (during Amidah)\
 , as well as Torah leyning. If we do not have 10 people in person then we w
 ill revert to only reading Torah from Chumash\, and a pastoral kaddish.<u><
 /u><br><u></u><br><b>Join Zoom Meeting</b>:&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<a href="https://u
 s02web.zoom.us/j/238145044"><u>https://us02web.zoom.us/j/238145044</u></a>&
 nbsp\;<br><br>Meeting ID: 238 145 044<br><br><br>------------<u></u><u></u>
 <u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
