DESCRIPTION:Torah Trope class with Kenny Altman\nSundays June 14-August 9\,
  6:30 p.m.\n\nCongregation Beth Sholom prides itself on being a congregatio
 n whose Torah service is a participatory experience and not a spectator spo
 rt.  From parents and siblings reading at their families' B'nai Mitzvot\, t
 o adults reading for the first time to commemorate a special occasion\, or 
 just for the joy of learning\, to those of us who have become seasoned\, re
 gular readers\, there is room for everyone on our Bimah and at the Torah!\n
 \nIn this nine-week class you will learn to chant Torah and you'll be assig
 ned a reading for an upcoming Shabbat as the class celebrates its graduatio
 n day as a group. \n\nThe only prerequisite to this class is that you know 
 how to read Hebrew.  \n\n$100 for members of Congregation Beth Sholom\, $12
 5 for nonmembers\, no one turned away due to lack of ability to pay.  Fee f
 or class includes instructional CD and other materials.\n\nRegistration for
  this class is not being handled through the Beth Sholom office. For inform
 ation\, or to register\, contact Kenny Altman at 415.377.6350 or kennyaltma
 n@earthlink.net.  \n\nKenny Altman is a stand-up comic and Torah trope inst
 ructor living in San Francisco. Over the past ten years he has taught hundr
 eds of people how to chant Torah\, and made countless others laugh. Often a
 t the same time.
LAST-MODIFIED:20250830T140601Z
LOCATION:Rabin Library
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Torah Trope
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
