DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://hadar.org/learn/classes-events/hadar-west-art-
 havruta" target="_blank"><u>https://hadar.org/learn/classes-events/hadar-we
 st-art-havruta</u></a><br><br><p><strong>The Art of Havruta: A Mishnah Stud
 y Series with Hadar</strong></p><p>Join our SF Beit Midrash for three month
 s of learning through a blend of independent havruta-learning and three in-
 person Beit Midrash sessions\, open to everyone. </p><p>At each Beit Midras
 h session\, Rabbi Kasher will offer brief teachings on the philosophy of ha
 vruta study and guide us through the themes and structure of the Mishnah ch
 apters from <a href="https://www.projectzug.org/" target="_blank"><u><u><u>
 Hadar’s Project Zug</u></u></u></a> Course “The Mishnah In Context”. This i
 s an opportunity to get to know a core genre of Jewish text while developin
 g the skills and spirit of classical havruta learning.</p><p> <a href="http
 s://www.projectzug.org/" target="_blank"><u><u><u>Project Zug</u></u></u></
 a> registration is free to Beth Sholom and Emanu-El members participating i
 n this Beit Midrash.</p><p><i><b>Note: The first and third session will be 
 at Congregation Beth Sholom. The second session will be at Congregation Ema
 nu-el. (2 Lake St\, San Francisco\, CA 94118)</b></i></p><b>Date and Time</
 b><br><br><u></u>Tue\, Jan 27\, 6:30<u></u> - <u></u>8:30 PM Pacific<u></u>
 <br><u></u>Tue\, Feb 24\, 6:30<u></u> - <u></u>8:30 PM Pacific<u></u><br><u
 ></u>Tue\, Mar 24\, 6:30<u></u> - <u></u>8:30 PM Pacific<u></u><br><br><b>L
 ocation</b><br>Congregation Beth Sholom<br><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl
 /1JYpfbypW7NHNxPf9" target="_blank"><u><u>301 14th Ave\, San Francisco\, CA
  94118</u></u></a><br><br><b>Cost</b><br>Free
