UID:29hgfhdp94nam33ig5p27fpjbu@google.com
CREATED:20250710T035452Z
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the end of summer by reconnecting with your Beth Shol
 om community* for Shabbat. Dinner\, song\, and joy will be provided.  <a hr
 ef="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfwbD1KtwdYjaVwKgi0m1g3ydL8zcc
 bAOYdI5HUkXNszMspjQ/viewform?usp=sharing&ouid=110435845811667505673" target
 ="_blank">Please register</a> in advance\, so we can be sure to have enough
  food for all!<br><p><b>Chesed v'Tzedek School Supply Drive</b></p><p>Every
  day\, people fleeing conflict or persecution arrive in the Bay Area. Many 
 come with next to nothing\, but their hope and determination. Create a back
 -to-school kit for children who have sought safe refuge in the Bay Area by 
 bringing supplies to donate to Jewish Family and Children's Services at the
  Welcome Back to Shul Community Shabbat. Feel free to bring one or more sup
 plies or make a full backpack with one of each item on the list! Gift cards
  to Target are also welcome in addition to or instead of supplies.<br></p><
 ul><li>Backpack</li><li>18-month 2025-26 monthly planner notebook</li><li>S
 piral bound lined paper notebook</li><li>Highlighter pens</li><li>Zippered 
 pencil pouch</li><li>Insulated soft sided lunchbox</li><li>Ball point pens<
 /li><li>Gift card</li></ul><br>Questions or want to help out more Contact B
 eth Sholom’s Chesed v’Tzedek Committee at <a href="mailto:chesed@bethsholom
 sf.org"><u>chesed@bethsholomsf.org.</u></a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250730T195144Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Welcome Back to Shul Community Shabbat
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
