CREATED:20240820T192946Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Introducing <strong><b>Ofri Reiner</b></strong>\, a resilien
 t Israeli survivor of the Nova massacre. At just 21\, she's faced tragedy\,
  losing her brother in combat. Through her art and passionate speaking\, sh
 e shares her journey\, finding healing and inspiring others to find strengt
 h. A combat soldier herself\, Ofri's message of resilience echoes: AM ISRAE
 L CHAI—Israel lives on\, stronger than ever.</p><p><em>“I have embarked on 
 a deeply personal journey towards healing\, driven by the power of creativi
 ty and narrative. I firmly believe that my purpose in this world is to tran
 sform the pain I carry into a beacon of hope for Jewish communities worldwi
 de”</em></p><p>Join Ofri as she shares her story and be a part of her heali
 ng journey.</p><p><strong><b><em>Registration <a href="https://cbssf.shulcl
 oud.com/form/cbs-Elul-Erev%20Shmia2024.html">here</a></em></b></strong></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20240822T163858Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:We Are Israel-Healing through Story
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
