BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20240813T071500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20240813T081500
DTSTAMP:20260318T055329Z
UID:gi2065ie3s6onl184o5ihqt6v0_R20230425T143000@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20240813T073000
CREATED:20200515T231455Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>Morning Minyan &amp\; Tisha b'Av</b><br><br>Join for morning
  minyan and reading of <i>Eicha/</i>Lamentations<br><i><br></i><br><i>In pe
 rson and on zoom </i>    <br><br>Join Zoom Meeting: <a href="https://us02we
 b.zoom.us/j/81632373785" target="_blank"><u>https://us02web.zoom.us/j/81632
 373785</u></a> <br><br>Meeting ID:  816 3237 3785<br><br><p dir="ltr">On <i
 >Tisha b'Av</i>\, we commemorate disasters that have befallen the Jewish pe
 ople\, including\, but not limited to the destruction of the First and Seco
 nd Temples in Jerusalem. The Babylonian Talmud teaches that the second deva
 stating destruction of the Temple happened because of <i>sinat hinam</i> - 
 baseless hatred. Today\, in a world in which there is so much suffering and
  polarization\, hatred seems to be growing. </p><br><p dir="ltr">So many of
  us have so much to mourn\, individually and as a people. We will come toge
 ther on <i>Tisha b'Av</i> to mourn\, to allow the sadness and grief to be f
 elt\, expressed and witnessed together. Rav Kook\, the great mystic and fir
 st Chief Ashkenazi Rabbi of British Mandate Palestine\, wrote: “If we were 
 destroyed\, and the world with us\, due to baseless hatred\, then we shall 
 rebuild ourselves\, and the world with us\, with baseless love — <i>ahavat 
 hinam</i>.” (Orot HaKodesh vol. III\, p. 324).</p><br><i>Tisha b'Av</i>\, a
 s Rabbi Lew <i>z’l</i> reminds us\, is the beginning of the High Holy Day s
 eason. Let us mourn together and rebuild better-- from love.
LAST-MODIFIED:20241104T183943Z
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Tuesday Morning Minyan & Tisha B'av
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
