UID:4iugleuep14tlo3coj2ng1kqc4@google.com
CREATED:20250803T125630Z
DESCRIPTION:<p dir="ltr">On <i>Tisha b&#39\;Av</i>\, we commemorate disaste
 rs that have befallen the Jewish people\, including the destruction of the 
 First and Second Temples in Jerusalem. The Babylonian Talmud teaches that t
 he second devastating destruction of the Temple happened because of <i>sina
 t hinam</i> - baseless hatred. Today\, in a world in which there is so much
  suffering and polarization\, hatred seems to be growing. </p><br><p dir="l
 tr">So many of us are mourning\, individually and as a people. We will come
  together on <i>Tisha b&#39\;Av</i> to grieve\, to allow the sadness to be 
 felt\, expressed and witnessed together. Rav Kook\, the great mystic and fi
 rst Chief Ashkenazi Rabbi of British Mandate Palestine\, wrote: “If we were
  destroyed\, and the world with us\, due to baseless hatred\, then we shall
  rebuild ourselves\, and the world with us\, with baseless love — <i>ahavat
  hinam</i>.” (Orot HaKodesh vol. III\, p. 324).</p><br><i>Tisha b&#39\;Av</
 i>\, as Rabbi Lew <i>z’l</i> reminds us\, begins the High Holy Day season. 
 Let us mourn together to rebuild better-- from love.<br><br><p dir="ltr"><b
 >Sunday\, August 3 - Tisha b’Av</b></p><p dir="ltr">8 a.m. – Morning Minyan
  and Reading of <i>Eicha</i> / Lamentations</p><p dir="ltr">In-person and o
 n Zoom</p><p dir="ltr">6 p.m. – Mincha</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250803T125630Z
SEQUENCE:0
